      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The +3 starts here (and on a reset): interrupts off, a delay of $6C03 rounds, then\nRAM_CLEAR.","comment":"No interrupts during start-up"},
        "1": {"comment":"$6C03 rounds"},
        "4": {"synopsis":"The delay.","comment":"One round"},
        "9": {"comment":"Every RAM bank cleared, then tested"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: ROM 3's RST $10 (CALL_ROM3), which prints A through the current channel.","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A: A printed through the current channel"},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: ROM 3's RST $18 (CALL_ROM3): the character at CH_ADD.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: ROM 3's RST $20 (CALL_ROM3): the next character at CH_ADD.","comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP: A = the next character at CH_ADD"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: calls the routine in ROM 3 whose address is the word after the RST, then returns\npast the word:\n1. HL = that address; $5B5A = the place after the word, the return point.\n2. CALL_ROM3_GO keeps the address in $5B58, stacks $5B21 (ROM3_RETURN's copy) as the\n   routine's return, then the address, and jumps to $5B00 (SWAP_ROM's copy), whose RET\n   enters ROM 3 there with HL as it was.\n3. When the routine returns, $5B21 swaps back to this ROM and returns to $5B5A. Keeps every\n   register for the routine; interrupts are on afterwards (SWAP_ROM ends with EI).","comment":"HL = the return address, the word's place"},
        "41": {"comment":"A kept"},
        "42": {"comment":"The routine address's low byte"},
        "43": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "45": {"comment":"$5B5A = the return point after the call"},
        "48": {"comment":"HL = the routine's address"},
        "51": {"comment":"A back"},
        "52": {"comment":"On in CALL_ROM3_GO"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"INT (interrupt mode 1): runs ROM 3's interrupt routine at $0038: the stack gets INT_RETURN,\n$5B00 (SWAP_ROM's copy, to come back) and $0038, then $5B00 swaps the ROMs and returns into\nROM 3's $0038. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "57": {"comment":"INT_RETURN, for the end"},
        "61": {"comment":"SWAP_ROM's copy, to swap back after the routine"},
        "65": {"comment":"ROM 3's interrupt routine, entered by the swap's RET"},
        "69": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs: on in ROM 3 at $0038"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"Where the interrupt comes back to: HL back, the disk motor's time-out counted\n(MOTOR_TIMEOUT, interrupts off), interrupts on, and return.","comment":"HL back"},
        "73": {"comment":"The disk motor's time-out, interrupts off"},
        "77": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI handler: when NMIADD ($5CB0) is not zero it jumps there (JP (HL), with AF and HL\nstill on the stack); when it is zero it returns at once (NMI_RETURN).","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "104": {"comment":"HL = NMIADD"},
        "107": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "111": {"comment":"No: jump there (AF and HL still stacked)"},
        "112": {"synopsis":"AF and HL back; RETN.","comment":"0: registers back"},
        "114": {"comment":"Return from the NMI"},
        "116": {"synopsis":"Counts the disk motor's time-out down: with bank 7 paged in (the paging byte $5B5C with bits\n0-2 set, to port $7FFD), when the count at $E600 is not 0 and FRAMES is even, the count goes\ndown by one; when it reaches 0, bit 3 of port $1FFD is cleared (its copy at $5B67 too),\nwhich turns the motor off. Then port $7FFD gets $5B5C back. The same job as ROM 2's\nMOTOR_TIMEOUT. Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "118": {"comment":"Bank 7 paged in: the count is at $E600"},
        "128": {"comment":"Is the motor's count running?"},
        "134": {"comment":"FRAMES even?"},
        "141": {"comment":"One less"},
        "145": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "148": {"comment":"Not 0 yet?"},
        "150": {"comment":"0: bit 3 of port $1FFD cleared, the motor off"},
        "153": {"comment":"Its copy with bit 3 cleared"},
        "161": {"comment":"Port $1FFD written"},
        "163": {"synopsis":"Port $7FFD gets the paging byte $5B5C back.","comment":"The paging byte back into port $7FFD"},
        "171": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "172": {"comment":"Return"},
        "174": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM3's second half: the routine's address kept in $5B58; the stack gets ROM3_RETURN's\ncopy ($5B21) and the routine's address, HL as it was, then SWAP_ROM's copy at $5B00.","comment":"The routine's address kept"},
        "177": {"comment":"ROM3_RETURN's copy as the routine's return"},
        "180": {"comment":"ROM3_RETURN under it, HL back"},
        "181": {"comment":"The routine's address on top, HL back"},
        "182": {"comment":"The routine's address"},
        "186": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs: the RET enters ROM 3 at the routine"},
        "189": {"synopsis":"Copied to $5B00 at start-up with the routines after it ($00BD-$010E to $5B00-$5B51) and run\nfrom there: flips bit 4 of port $7FFD and bit 2 of port $1FFD (the ROM number's low and high\nbits; their copies at $5B5C and $5B67), with interrupts off, so that ROM 0 and ROM 3 change\nplaces (and ROM 1 and ROM 2); interrupts on, and a RET made with an address on the stack\ncontinues in the other ROM. Keeps every register.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "191": {"comment":"Port $7FFD: bit 4, the ROM's low bit, flipped"},
        "194": {"comment":"The paging byte with bit 4 flipped"},
        "199": {"comment":"Interrupts off while paging"},
        "200": {"comment":"Stored and written"},
        "205": {"synopsis":"At $5B10: SWAP_ROM's second half, entered on its own by SWAP_HIGH_GO with AF and BC already\nstacked: only bit 2 of port $1FFD (the ROM's high bit) flipped, then interrupts on, BC and\nAF back and RET.","comment":"Port $1FFD: bit 2, the ROM's high bit, flipped"},
        "208": {"comment":"The other paging byte with bit 2 flipped"},
        "213": {"comment":"Stored and written"},
        "218": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "219": {"comment":"Registers back; the RET goes on in the other ROM"},
        "222": {"synopsis":"At $5B21: where a ROM 3 routine called by CALL_ROM3 returns to: the ROMs swapped back\n(SWAP_ROM), then on at the address in $5B5A, past the RST's word. Keeps every register.","comment":"Swap back to this ROM"},
        "225": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "226": {"comment":"The return point at $5B5A on the stack, HL back"},
        "230": {"comment":"On past the RST's word"},
        "231": {"synopsis":"At $5B2A: flips only the ROM's high bit (SWAP_ROM_HIGH at $5B10, so ROM 1 and ROM 3, or ROM\n0 and ROM 2, change places), then goes on at the address in $5B5A (GO_5B5A's copy at $5B34)\nin the ROM now paged in. Nothing in this ROM uses it; ROM 1 loads $5B2A (at $00AD, $10FD,\n$185A). Keeps every register.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "232": {"comment":"GO_5B5A's copy ($5B34) as where to go on"},
        "235": {"comment":"GO_5B5A under the registers, HL back"},
        "236": {"comment":"Stacked as SWAP_ROM_HIGH expects them"},
        "238": {"comment":"Only the ROM's high bit flipped ($5B10)"},
        "241": {"synopsis":"At $5B34: jumps to the address in $5B5A, keeping every register.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "242": {"comment":"The address at $5B5A on the stack, HL back"},
        "246": {"comment":"Go there"},
        "247": {"synopsis":"At $5B3A: pages ROM 1 in from scratch, with interrupts off: port $1FFD = $10 (ROM high bit\n0, disk motor off) and port $7FFD = $10 (ROM 1, bank 0, normal screen), both copies set,\nthen on at $253A in ROM 1. ROM 1 pushes $5B3A and points ERR_SP at it (at $1372, $1428,\n$24F8, $25BA), so an error report ends up here.","comment":"Interrupts off while paging"},
        "249": {"comment":"Written"},
        "254": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "257": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = $10: ROM 1, bank 0, normal screen"},
        "259": {"comment":"Written"},
        "264": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "268": {"comment":"On at $253A in ROM 1, now paged in"},
        "271": {"synopsis":"Clears the eight RAM banks, 7 down to 0: each paged in at $C000 (port $7FFD) and $C000-$FFFF\nset to 0. Then RAM_TEST.","comment":"Eight banks, 7 down to 0"},
        "273": {"synopsis":"One bank: bank B - 1.","comment":"A = B - 1, the bank"},
        "274": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "276": {"comment":"Paged in at $C000"},
        "279": {"comment":"Written"},
        "281": {"comment":"$C000-$FFFF cleared to 0"},
        "287": {"comment":"$3FFF more after the first"},
        "290": {"comment":"The first byte 0"},
        "292": {"comment":"The rest"},
        "294": {"comment":"The counter back"},
        "295": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "297": {"synopsis":"Tests the byte at $DCBA in each RAM bank, 0 up to 7: each of its eight bits is written alone\nand read back set, then the other seven written and the bit read back clear. A failure stops\nat RAM_FAULT with E counting the bits left and A' the bank. Bank 7 stays paged in\nafterwards. Then the AY's register 14 is set to $FF and the start-up goes on at COLD_START.","comment":"From bank 0 up"},
        "298": {"comment":"The byte tested in every bank"},
        "301": {"comment":"The paging port"},
        "304": {"synopsis":"One bank: bank A paged in, D = 1 (the bit), E = 8 (the count).","comment":"D = 1, the first bit; E = 8 bits"},
        "307": {"comment":"Bank A paged in at $C000"},
        "309": {"comment":"The bank kept in A'"},
        "310": {"synopsis":"One bit.","comment":"The bit alone written"},
        "311": {"comment":"Written"},
        "312": {"comment":"Read back: is the bit set?"},
        "314": {"comment":"No: a fault"},
        "317": {"comment":"Every other bit written"},
        "318": {"comment":"Written"},
        "319": {"comment":"Read back: is the bit clear?"},
        "321": {"comment":"No: a fault"},
        "324": {"comment":"The next bit"},
        "326": {"comment":"All eight bits?"},
        "327": {"comment":"The next bit"},
        "329": {"comment":"The bank back"},
        "330": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "331": {"comment":"All eight banks?"},
        "333": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "335": {"comment":"C = $FD for ports $FFFD and $BFFD"},
        "337": {"comment":"D, E = their high bytes $FF and $BF"},
        "341": {"comment":"AY register 14 selected (port $FFFD)"},
        "342": {"comment":"Register 14"},
        "346": {"comment":"Register 14 = $FF (port $BFFD)"},
        "347": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "351": {"comment":"On with the start-up"},
        "353": {"comment":"Not reached from anywhere: border from B'"},
        "354": {"comment":"B' as the colour"},
        "357": {"synopsis":"Forever. Nothing jumps to $0161, the border-setting code before it.","comment":"Forever"},
        "359": {"synopsis":"After the RAM test: A' = 0, then START_SETUP.","comment":"A' = 0: a start from reset"},
        "361": {"comment":"The stack above the screen, in bank 5"},
        "364": {"synopsis":"Sets the machine up (from COLD_START with A' = 0, and from $266F with A' = $52, without the\nRAM clear and test):\n1. The stack at $6000; AY register 7 = $FF; the RAM routines from $00BD copied to\n   $5B00-$5B51; $5B5D = $CF.\n2. As a 48K start: P_RAMT = $FFFF, the UDGs copied below it from ROM 3's letters A-U ($3EAF\n   down, through ROM 3's $1661), UDG, RASP/PIP, RAMTOP, CHARS = $3C00, IM 1, IY = $5C3A;\n   FLAGS bit 4 set (128K mode).\n3. The +3's own variables: $5B66 bits 7 and 3 cleared and bit 2 set, $5B7B = 9, $5B5F =\n   $000B, FLAGS2 bit 6 cleared, $5B61, $5B63 and $5B65 = 0, $FF24 = $EC00 (bank 7), $5B64 =\n   $50, $5B75 and $5B77 = 10, $5B79 and $5B7A = $54.\n4. CHANS from CHANS_128_INIT, the program, variable and edit-line pointers, the colours\n   ($38), $EC13 = 0, border 7, REPDEL $23 and REPPER 5, KSTATE free, STRMS from STRMS_INIT,\n   FLAGS bit 1 cleared, ERR_NR = $FF, DF_SZ = 2.\n5. With A' = $52 it ends at $2675. Otherwise the stack under the UDGs, interrupts on, CLS\n   (ROM 3's CLS_CMD), the test screen when BREAK is held (TEST_ON_BREAK), COPYRIGHT_MSG\n   printed; $5B6A = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), $EC11 and $EC0F = $38; ROM\n   1's $2570 (through $3E80); DF_SZ = 2, TV_FLAG bit 5 set, EDITOR_RESET, bank 0\n   (BANK0_STACK), and the start-up menu (MAIN_MENU).","comment":"AY register 7 selected"},
        "365": {"comment":"Register 7"},
        "369": {"comment":"Register 7 = $FF: tones and noise off"},
        "370": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "374": {"comment":"The RAM routines at $00BD copied to $5B00-$5B51"},
        "377": {"comment":"From $00BD, 82 bytes"},
        "385": {"comment":"$5B5D = $CF"},
        "387": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "390": {"comment":"P_RAMT = $FFFF"},
        "396": {"comment":"ROM 3's letters A-U ($3E08-$3EAF), 168 bytes"},
        "402": {"comment":"HL = the source's end, DE = P_RAMT"},
        "403": {"comment":"ROM 3's LDDR; RET (in MAKE_ROOM): the UDGs below P_RAMT"},
        "406": {"comment":"HL = the byte below them"},
        "407": {"comment":"UDG = $FF58, the first UDG"},
        "408": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "411": {"comment":"HL = $FF57"},
        "412": {"comment":"RASP = $40, PIP = 0"},
        "419": {"comment":"RAMTOP = $FF57, below the UDGs"},
        "422": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 7 cleared"},
        "425": {"comment":"Its bit 7 cleared"},
        "427": {"comment":"$5B7B = 9"},
        "432": {"comment":"CHARS = $3C00"},
        "438": {"comment":"Interrupt mode 1"},
        "440": {"comment":"IY at ERR_NR, as BASIC expects"},
        "444": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 set: 128K mode"},
        "448": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 3 cleared, bit 2 set"},
        "451": {"comment":"Bit 3 cleared"},
        "453": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "455": {"comment":"$5B5F = $000B"},
        "461": {"comment":"$5B61, $5B63 and $5B65 = 0"},
        "471": {"comment":"$FF24 = $EC00 (bank 7, left paged in by the test)"},
        "477": {"comment":"$5B64 = $50"},
        "482": {"comment":"$5B75 and $5B77 = 10"},
        "491": {"comment":"$5B79 and $5B7A = $54"},
        "499": {"comment":"CHANS = $5CB6"},
        "502": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "505": {"comment":"The channels from CHANS_128_INIT, 21 bytes"},
        "508": {"comment":"21 bytes"},
        "512": {"comment":"Copied to $5CB6"},
        "515": {"comment":"HL at the channels' $80 end marker"},
        "516": {"comment":"DATADD = it"},
        "519": {"comment":"PROG and VARS just after it"},
        "520": {"comment":"PROG"},
        "523": {"comment":"VARS"},
        "526": {"comment":"The variables' end marker"},
        "528": {"comment":"E_LINE after it"},
        "529": {"comment":"E_LINE"},
        "532": {"comment":"The edit line: ENTER and the $80 end marker"},
        "534": {"comment":"The edit line's end marker after ENTER"},
        "538": {"comment":"WORKSP, STKBOT and STKEND after it"},
        "541": {"comment":"STKBOT"},
        "544": {"comment":"STKEND"},
        "547": {"comment":"ATTR_P, ATTR_T and BORDCR = $38: black on white"},
        "549": {"comment":"ATTR_P"},
        "552": {"comment":"ATTR_T"},
        "555": {"comment":"BORDCR"},
        "558": {"comment":"$EC13 = 0 (bank 7)"},
        "562": {"comment":"White border"},
        "564": {"comment":"Written"},
        "566": {"comment":"REPDEL = $23, REPPER = 5"},
        "572": {"comment":"KSTATE's two key slots free ($FF)"},
        "575": {"comment":"The second slot free"},
        "578": {"comment":"STRMS from STRMS_INIT, 14 bytes"},
        "584": {"comment":"14 bytes"},
        "587": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "589": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 1 cleared: not the printer"},
        "593": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no report"},
        "597": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "601": {"comment":"A = the start's kind, from A'"},
        "602": {"comment":"$52 ('R', from $266F)?"},
        "604": {"comment":"Yes: this start ends at $2675"},
        "607": {"comment":"The stack just under the UDGs (RAMTOP + 1)"},
        "611": {"comment":"SP = RAMTOP + 1"},
        "612": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "613": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_CMD: the whole screen cleared"},
        "616": {"comment":"The test screen when BREAK is held"},
        "619": {"comment":"The copyright message"},
        "622": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "625": {"comment":"The editor's stack at $5BFF, kept in $5B6A"},
        "631": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "634": {"comment":"$EC11 and $EC0F = $38 (bank 7)"},
        "636": {"comment":"$EC11"},
        "639": {"comment":"$EC0F"},
        "642": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "645": {"comment":"ROM 1's $2410, through $3E80 and the word after"},
        "650": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "653": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "657": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 set"},
        "661": {"comment":"The editor's state cleared"},
        "664": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "667": {"comment":"The start-up menu"},
        "670": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at DE through RST $10, up to and including the character with bit 7 set\n(printed without it).\nExit: DE = the place after the text.","comment":"The character without bit 7"},
        "673": {"comment":"DE kept round the print"},
        "676": {"comment":"The character again"},
        "677": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "678": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: was it the last?"},
        "682": {"synopsis":"Start-up's test screen, shown only when BREAK (CAPS SHIFT and SPACE) is held; otherwise it\nreturns at once.\n1. Border 7, stream 2, TV_FLAG = 0, AT 0,0.\n2. TEST_TEXT (\"1987\", the \"87\" bright) printed in every ink and paper: inks 7 down to 0, for\n   each the papers 7 down to 0; then the pixels of lines 8-23 cleared and the attributes of\n   lines 0-7 copied over lines 8-15 and 16-23, which leaves colour bars.\n3. Interrupts off; then forever: a tone of $0370 half-cycles, and the key sets of\n   TEST_KEY_SETS tried in turn until one is held, $2000 misses before the next tone. A set\n   held jumps to its address: this ROM's $21DF for Q A Z P L M, $22D0 for E U A, $0000 for B\n   V.","comment":"Is SPACE down (port $7FFE bit 0)?"},
        "687": {"comment":"No: back"},
        "688": {"comment":"Is CAPS SHIFT down (port $FEFE bit 0)?"},
        "693": {"comment":"No: back"},
        "694": {"comment":"White border"},
        "698": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "700": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "703": {"comment":"TV_FLAG = 0"},
        "707": {"comment":"AT 0,0"},
        "714": {"comment":"E = 8: eight papers, eight inks, eight characters"},
        "716": {"comment":"B = the paper counter, D = the ink counter"},
        "718": {"synopsis":"One group of eight characters: ATTR_T from the paper (B - 1) and the ink (D - 1).","comment":"The paper (B - 1) into bits 3-5"},
        "726": {"comment":"The ink (D - 1)"},
        "728": {"comment":"ATTR_T = the colours"},
        "731": {"comment":"The eight characters of TEST_TEXT"},
        "735": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"One character"},
        "738": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "741": {"comment":"The next paper"},
        "743": {"comment":"The papers again from 8"},
        "744": {"comment":"The next ink"},
        "747": {"comment":"The pixels of lines 8-23 cleared ($4800-$57FF)"},
        "760": {"comment":"HL = $5800, the attributes of lines 0-7"},
        "761": {"comment":"Copied over lines 8-15 and 16-23: colour bars"},
        "769": {"comment":"No interrupts from here"},
        "770": {"synopsis":"The tone: $0370 half-cycles, the speaker bit flipped after each wait of $0099 rounds; then\nthe key sets.","comment":"A tone of $0370 half-cycles"},
        "773": {"comment":"Border 7, speaker bit 0"},
        "775": {"synopsis":"One half-cycle.","comment":"One half-cycle's wait"},
        "778": {"synopsis":"The wait."},
        "783": {"comment":"The speaker bit (bit 4) flipped"},
        "789": {"comment":"All half-cycles done?"},
        "794": {"comment":"$2000 misses before the tone again"},
        "797": {"comment":"The list of key sets"},
        "801": {"synopsis":"The next key set from TEST_KEY_SETS; after the last ($0000) the list starts again.","comment":"HL = the next set's address"},
        "811": {"comment":"The list's end?"},
        "815": {"comment":"Yes: from the start of the list"},
        "821": {"synopsis":"One row of the set: port BC read, its low five bits must be the set's byte. A set ends with\nport $0000 and the address to go to.","comment":"A keyboard row's port"},
        "826": {"comment":"The set's end?"},
        "830": {"comment":"That row's keys"},
        "834": {"comment":"Exactly these keys down?"},
        "835": {"comment":"Yes: the set's next row"},
        "837": {"comment":"No: one miss more"},
        "840": {"comment":"Misses left: the next set"},
        "842": {"comment":"None: the tone again"},
        "844": {"synopsis":"The whole set is held: on at its address.","comment":"The set's address"},
        "847": {"comment":"Jump there"},
        "849": {"synopsis":"A key set for TEST_ON_BREAK (TEST_KEY_SETS points at the byte before it): port and row value\nfor each row, $0000, then the address. $FBFE $1E (Q), $FDFE $1E (A), $FEFE $1D (Z), $DFFE\n$1E (P), $BFFE $1D (L), $7FFE $1B (M); then $21DF."},
        "871": {"synopsis":"A bit failed the RAM test (E = the bits left, A' = the bank): A = the bit's number, 0-7. In\nbank 0 the border shows that number and the machine stops (RAM_FAULT_STOP); in any other\nbank the border flashes between that colour and its complement (the number xor 7), forever.","comment":"A = the failing bit's number (8 - E)"},
        "874": {"comment":"Kept in A'; A = the bank"},
        "875": {"comment":"Bank 0?"},
        "878": {"comment":"Yes: A = the bit's number"},
        "879": {"comment":"A steady border in that colour"},
        "881": {"synopsis":"Forever.","comment":"Forever"},
        "883": {"synopsis":"Not bank 0: C = the bit's number, B = it xor 7.","comment":"A = the bit's number"},
        "884": {"comment":"C = it, B = it xor 7"},
        "889": {"synopsis":"Border C, a wait of 65536 rounds, border B, a wait of $2AAA rounds; forever.","comment":"Border colour C"},
        "892": {"comment":"A long wait"},
        "895": {"synopsis":"The long wait."},
        "900": {"comment":"Border colour B"},
        "903": {"comment":"A shorter wait"},
        "906": {"synopsis":"The short wait."},
        "911": {"comment":"Again"},
        "913": {"synopsis":"TEST_ON_BREAK's second key set, as TEST_KEYS_1: $FBFE $1B (E), $DFFE $17 (U), $FDFE $1E (A);\nthen $22D0."},
        "926": {"synopsis":"TEST_ON_BREAK's third key set: $7FFE $0F (B), $FEFE $0F (V); then $0000, a restart."},
        "936": {"synopsis":"TEST_ON_BREAK's list of key sets, each address the byte before a set: $0350 (TEST_KEYS_1),\n$0395 (TEST_KEYS_2), $039D (TEST_KEYS_3), and $0000 to end it."},
        "944": {"synopsis":"TEST_ON_BREAK's eight characters: BRIGHT 0, \"19\", BRIGHT 1, \"87\"."},
        "952": {"synopsis":"CHANS as start-up copies it to $5CB6 (21 bytes): K (output $09F4, input $10A8), S ($09F4,\n$15C4), X ($0F81, $15C4), P ($3A05, $3A00), then the $80 end marker. The addresses are ROM\n3's: K, S and X's as in the 48K ROM; P's are ROM 3's ROM_SWAP_3D06 and ROM_SWAP_3D03, which go\non in ROM 1."},
        "973": {"synopsis":"STRMS as start-up copies it to $5C10: the offsets of streams -3 to 3 into CHANS: 1 (K), 6\n(S), 11 (R), 1, 1, 6, 16 (P)."},
        "987": {"synopsis":"The start-up message, printed by START_SETUP through PRINT_BIT7_TEXT: $7F (the copyright\nsign in the character set), \"1982, 1986, 1987 Amstrad Plc.\" and ENTER, which has bit 7 set."},
        "1018": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the editing rows from the program and draws them; the cursor goes to E_PPC's line\nwhen it is among them. An editing row is 35 bytes ($EC16 + 35 x row): 32 characters (0 an\nempty cell), a flags byte (bit 0: the first row of a line), then the line's number, high\nbyte first. The rows above the screen are kept at $F9DB (a count, then the rows); $FC9A is\nthe number of the line they belong to.\n1. $EEF5 bit 0 cleared, bit 1 set (E_PPC's line looked for); when E_PPC is 0, $EC06 = 0.\n2. The rows above are made again: $F9D7 = the line before $FC9A ($1418), both buffers\n   emptied ($12F0, $11A4), then as many rows as were above taken from the program ($11AD)\n   and put back above ($1338).\n3. Rows 0 to $EC15 filled with the next rows ($11AD). In E_PPC's first row (flags bit 0, the\n   number matching) the search succeeds ($EEF5 bit 0); from there the cursor moves $EC06\n   places on through the line's characters, row by row ($0F0F), and is stored (CURSOR_STORE,\n   $0ADC) at the row and column reached, no further than a row's last character ($0F31);\n   $EEF5 = 0 then.\n4. E_PPC not found: $FC9A = E_PPC and the rows above emptied, so that its line comes at the\n   top (when E_PPC is 0: $FC9A = 0 and E_PPC = the program's first line, $1420); then the\n   whole again from ROWS_REBUILD_GO.\n5. The rows drawn (ROWS_DRAW).\nExit: Z.","comment":"$EEF5 bit 0 cleared, bit 1 set: E_PPC looked for"},
        "1021": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared: not found yet"},
        "1023": {"comment":"Bit 1 set: looking"},
        "1025": {"synopsis":"Again from here (RB_AGAIN), with E_PPC changed.","comment":"Is E_PPC 0?"},
        "1030": {"comment":"No: keep $EC06"},
        "1032": {"comment":"Yes: $EC06 = 0"},
        "1035": {"synopsis":"The count of rows above the screen kept; $F9D7 = the line before $FC9A; both buffers\nemptied.","comment":"The count of rows above the screen kept"},
        "1039": {"comment":"$F9D7 = the line before $FC9A"},
        "1042": {"comment":"HL = the line before $FC9A"},
        "1048": {"comment":"Both buffers emptied"},
        "1051": {"comment":"The rows below emptied too"},
        "1054": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "1055": {"synopsis":"One row from the program put back above the screen, until the count is used up.","comment":"Rows left to put back above?"},
        "1056": {"comment":"None: fill the editing rows"},
        "1058": {"comment":"One row from the program"},
        "1059": {"comment":"HL = the next row's text"},
        "1062": {"comment":"Put above the screen"},
        "1063": {"comment":"Put above"},
        "1066": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "1070": {"synopsis":"Rows 0 to $EC15: B = the row, C = $EC15, DE = the row's place; the first two kept on the\nstack.","comment":"Row 0's place"},
        "1072": {"comment":"DE = row 0's place"},
        "1075": {"comment":"B = row 0, C = the last editing row"},
        "1076": {"comment":"C = $EC15, the last row"},
        "1080": {"comment":"Kept for the end"},
        "1082": {"synopsis":"One row: the next from the program ($11AD); while E_PPC is looked for, is this E_PPC's first\nrow?","comment":"The next row from the program"},
        "1085": {"comment":"Still looking for E_PPC's line?"},
        "1090": {"comment":"No: just copy"},
        "1094": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "1097": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "1098": {"comment":"The first row of a line?"},
        "1100": {"comment":"No: not E_PPC's"},
        "1102": {"comment":"DE = its number, high byte first"},
        "1106": {"comment":"Is it E_PPC?"},
        "1107": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "1112": {"comment":"Not the same: not E_PPC's"},
        "1114": {"comment":"Yes: found"},
        "1117": {"comment":"$EEF5 bit 0 set: found"},
        "1119": {"synopsis":"Not E_PPC's first row."},
        "1121": {"synopsis":"The row copied into the editing rows (35 bytes); DE = the next row's place.","comment":"The row copied into the editing rows"},
        "1123": {"comment":"35 bytes"},
        "1130": {"comment":"The next row's place kept"},
        "1132": {"comment":"DE = the copied row"},
        "1133": {"comment":"E_PPC's line found in this row?"},
        "1138": {"comment":"No: the next row"},
        "1140": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "1142": {"synopsis":"The cursor $EC06 places on: while there are places left and the row has a character at or\nafter column B ($0F0F), one more column.","comment":"Places left to move?"},
        "1147": {"comment":"None: the search ends"},
        "1149": {"comment":"A character at or after column B?"},
        "1150": {"comment":"Is there text at or after column B?"},
        "1154": {"comment":"No: past the row's end"},
        "1156": {"comment":"One place used, one column on"},
        "1158": {"comment":"$EC06 = places left"},
        "1161": {"comment":"Again"},
        "1163": {"synopsis":"No places left: past the row's last character, B goes back to just after it ($0F31); the\nsearch ends ($EEF5 = 0).","comment":"Past the last character: back to just after it"},
        "1166": {"comment":"None: B back to just after the last"},
        "1169": {"comment":"The search ends"},
        "1172": {"comment":"$EEF5 = 0"},
        "1174": {"synopsis":"The cursor stored at this row, column B, remembered column B (CURSOR_STORE, $0ADC).","comment":"B = the column, C = the row"},
        "1175": {"comment":"The row number again"},
        "1179": {"comment":"The cursor stored there"},
        "1182": {"synopsis":"The next row, up to $EC15.","comment":"The row back"},
        "1184": {"comment":"Past the last editing row?"},
        "1185": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "1187": {"comment":"Up to the last"},
        "1189": {"comment":"Was E_PPC looked for?"},
        "1194": {"comment":"No: draw the rows"},
        "1196": {"comment":"Was it found?"},
        "1198": {"comment":"Found: draw the rows"},
        "1200": {"comment":"Not found: is E_PPC 0?"},
        "1205": {"comment":"Yes: the first line"},
        "1207": {"comment":"No: its line at the top"},
        "1210": {"comment":"The rows above emptied"},
        "1213": {"comment":"Again"},
        "1215": {"synopsis":"E_PPC 0: $FC9A = 0, and E_PPC = the program's first line ($1420).","comment":"E_PPC 0: $FC9A = 0"},
        "1218": {"comment":"E_PPC = the program's first line"},
        "1221": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "1224": {"synopsis":"Again (ROWS_REBUILD_GO).","comment":"The whole again"},
        "1226": {"comment":"From ROWS_REBUILD_GO"},
        "1229": {"synopsis":"Rows 0 to $EC15 drawn (ROWS_DRAW, with Z)."},
        "1231": {"comment":"Z: the cursor not moved after drawing"},
        "1232": {"synopsis":"Draws editing rows B to C on the screen, each through $16FE. With NZ on entry the cursor\nwould then be moved $EC06 places on ($0C43 each) and stored ($0ADC); both callers (RB_DRAW\nand $10D6) enter with Z, so that part ($04E6-$04FE) is never run.\nEntry: B = the first row, C = the last, F's Z flag as above.\nExit: Z; HL = the place after the last row drawn.","comment":"The flags kept"},
        "1233": {"comment":"A = the last row, C = the first"},
        "1235": {"comment":"The first row's place"},
        "1238": {"comment":"HL = the row"},
        "1239": {"synopsis":"One row drawn ($16FE); the next, up to A.","comment":"Kept"},
        "1240": {"comment":"Drawn"},
        "1244": {"comment":"The next row's place"},
        "1247": {"comment":"The next row's place"},
        "1248": {"comment":"Up to the last"},
        "1250": {"comment":"Up to the last"},
        "1252": {"comment":"Z on entry: done"},
        "1254": {"comment":"The cursor's place"},
        "1257": {"synopsis":"One place on ($0C43), $EC06 times, then the cursor stored.","comment":"One place on"},
        "1260": {"comment":"$EC06 places in all"},
        "1266": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "1269": {"comment":"More to move?"},
        "1271": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1274": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "1275": {"synopsis":"Clears editing rows 0 to $EC15 on the screen ($1D6B with B = 0, D = $EC15).\nExit: through $1D6B.","comment":"From line 0"},
        "1277": {"comment":"To the last editing row"},
        "1280": {"comment":"D = the last row"},
        "1281": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "1284": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the editing rows up by one: row 0 goes to the rows above the screen ($1338; when\nthere is no room there, nothing is done), the next row from the program ($11AD) comes in at\nrow $EC15 (ROWS_UP_FROM with B = 0).\nExit: carry when scrolled; HL kept when not.","comment":"Row 0"},
        "1287": {"comment":"C = row 0"},
        "1288": {"comment":"DE = its place"},
        "1291": {"comment":"Put above the screen: was there room?"},
        "1294": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1295": {"comment":"No: nothing done"},
        "1296": {"comment":"HL = the next row from the program"},
        "1299": {"synopsis":"Rows B+1 to $EC15 moved up by one into rows B to $EC15 - 1, the screen scrolled the same way\n($1712), and the row at HL copied into row $EC15.\nEntry: B = the row that goes, DE = its place, HL = the row that comes in at the bottom.\nExit: carry. Keeps BC."},
        "1300": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1301": {"comment":"HL = the row below row B"},
        "1304": {"comment":"HL = the next row's place"},
        "1305": {"comment":"Is B the last row?"},
        "1310": {"comment":"Yes: no rows to move"},
        "1313": {"synopsis":"One row up.","comment":"One row up, 35 bytes"},
        "1314": {"comment":"35 bytes"},
        "1320": {"comment":"Up to the last row"},
        "1321": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "1323": {"comment":"Up to the last"},
        "1326": {"synopsis":"The screen scrolled up ($1712); the new row into the last row.","comment":"HL = the new row"},
        "1327": {"comment":"The screen scrolled up the same way"},
        "1330": {"comment":"The new row into the last row"},
        "1333": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "1335": {"comment":"Carry: scrolled"},
        "1338": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the editing rows down by one: the last row above the screen comes back ($12F9; when\nthere is none, nothing is done) and goes in at row 0 (ROWS_DOWN_FROM with B = 0).\nExit: carry when scrolled.","comment":"Row 0"},
        "1340": {"comment":"The last row above the screen back: was there one?"},
        "1343": {"comment":"No: nothing done"},
        "1344": {"synopsis":"Row $EC15 goes to the rows below the screen ($11EC; when there is no room there, nothing is\ndone), rows B to $EC15 - 1 move down by one, the screen is scrolled the same way ($1726),\nand the row at HL is copied into row B.\nEntry: B = the row, HL = the row that comes in.\nExit: carry when done. Keeps BC."},
        "1345": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1346": {"comment":"C = the last row"},
        "1349": {"comment":"C = $EC15"},
        "1350": {"comment":"Its place"},
        "1353": {"comment":"It goes below the screen: was there room?"},
        "1356": {"comment":"No: nothing done"},
        "1358": {"comment":"DE = the end of the row before"},
        "1359": {"comment":"HL = the last row's end"},
        "1362": {"comment":"HL = the last row's end"},
        "1365": {"comment":"Is B the last row?"},
        "1367": {"comment":"Yes: no rows to move"},
        "1369": {"synopsis":"One row down (copied from its end).","comment":"One row down, from its end"},
        "1370": {"comment":"35 bytes, backwards"},
        "1376": {"comment":"Down to row B"},
        "1377": {"comment":"The row before"},
        "1379": {"comment":"Down to row B"},
        "1381": {"synopsis":"DE = row B's place; the screen scrolled down ($1726); the new row into row B.","comment":"DE = row B's place"},
        "1382": {"comment":"Row B's start"},
        "1385": {"comment":"The screen scrolled down the same way"},
        "1388": {"comment":"The new row into row B"},
        "1391": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "1393": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "1396": {"synopsis":"No room below: no carry.","comment":"Not done"},
        "1397": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "1399": {"synopsis":"Puts character A in column B of the row at DE, moving columns B to 30 one to the right.\nExit: A = E = the character pushed out of column 31; Z when that was 0 (an empty cell); HL =\nthe row's flags byte. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "1400": {"comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "1404": {"comment":"D = the character carried, A = the column"},
        "1406": {"synopsis":"One column: its character swapped with the one carried, up to column 31.","comment":"Swapped with the column's"},
        "1407": {"comment":"The carried one in"},
        "1409": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "1410": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "1411": {"comment":"Up to column 31"},
        "1413": {"comment":"Up to column 31"},
        "1415": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out; is it 0?"},
        "1416": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "1420": {"synopsis":"Takes the character in column B out of the row at DE, moving columns B+1 to 31 one to the\nleft; character A comes in at column 31.\nExit: A = E = the character taken out; Z when it was 0 (an empty cell); HL = the row's flags\nbyte. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "1421": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "1425": {"comment":"Kept for the exit"},
        "1426": {"comment":"D = the character carried in"},
        "1427": {"comment":"From column 31"},
        "1429": {"comment":"Into the loop at column 31"},
        "1431": {"synopsis":"One column: its character swapped with the one carried; column B ends it.","comment":"Swapped with the column's"},
        "1432": {"comment":"The carried one in"},
        "1434": {"comment":"Column B reached?"},
        "1435": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "1437": {"comment":"One column left"},
        "1438": {"synopsis":"One column to the left.","comment":"The column to the left"},
        "1441": {"synopsis":"Column B's character in A; Z when it was 0.","comment":"A = column B's character; is it 0?"},
        "1442": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "1447": {"synopsis":"Back to RAM bank 0 (paging byte 0: ROM 0, bank 0, normal screen, through PAGE_WRITE) and to\nthe stack kept in $5B6A, which in turn keeps this one: the pair of BANK7_STACK. The return\naddress goes with the caller; AF and HL kept (HL through $5B58).\nChanges: AF'.","comment":"A kept in A'"},
        "1448": {"comment":"Paging byte 0: bank 0, ROM 0, normal screen"},
        "1450": {"comment":"Interrupts off while the stack changes"},
        "1451": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "1454": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "1455": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "1458": {"comment":"The other stack swapped in"},
        "1461": {"comment":"$5B6A = this stack"},
        "1465": {"comment":"SP = the other"},
        "1466": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1467": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1470": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "1471": {"comment":"A back"},
        "1473": {"synopsis":"Writes A to port $7FFD and to the paging byte at $5B5C. Keeps BC.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "1474": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "1477": {"comment":"Written"},
        "1479": {"comment":"Its copy at $5B5C"},
        "1484": {"synopsis":"Swaps the stack with the one kept in $5B6A, then pages RAM bank 7 in at $C000 (paging byte\n7, PAGE_WRITE): where the editor's own data lives ($EC00 up). The return address goes with\nthe caller; AF and HL kept (HL through $5B58).\nChanges: AF'.","comment":"A kept in A'"},
        "1485": {"comment":"No interrupts while the stack changes"},
        "1486": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "1487": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "1490": {"comment":"The other stack swapped in"},
        "1493": {"comment":"$5B6A = this stack"},
        "1497": {"comment":"SP = the other"},
        "1498": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1501": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "1502": {"comment":"Paging byte 7: bank 7 at $C000"},
        "1504": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "1507": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1508": {"comment":"A back"},
        "1510": {"synopsis":"The editor's key table for TABLE_DISPATCH ($2166; KEY_DISPATCH with no menu up): a count\n($15), then for each key its code and the address of its routine: $0B $0B5F, $0A $0B80, $08\n$0BA2, $09 $0BAE, $AD $0B1A, $AC $0AF0, $AF $0A9F, $AE $0AAC, $A6 $0A4E, $A5 $0A76, $A8\n$0B52, $A7 $0B45, $AA KEY_DELETE_RIGHT, $0C KEY_DELETE_LEFT, $B3 $10E5, $B4 $108A, $B0\n$1140, $B1 $110C, $0D $0A0F (ENTER), $A9 SCREEN_TOGGLE, $07 MENU_OPEN."},
        "1574": {"synopsis":"The key table with a menu up (KEY_DISPATCH): a count (4), then code and routine for each\nkey: $0B MENU_UP, $0A MENU_DOWN, $07 and $0D MENU_SELECT."},
        "1587": {"synopsis":"Clears the editor's state: UPPER_SETUP, $FC9A = 0, $EC0D = $82, E_PPC = 0, $16B6, $1758.","comment":"Editing in the upper screen"},
        "1590": {"comment":"$FC9A = 0: no rows above"},
        "1593": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1596": {"comment":"$EC0D = $82"},
        "1598": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1601": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "1604": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1607": {"comment":"The editing rows set up ($16B6)"},
        "1610": {"comment":"The keys' defaults ($1758)"},
        "1614": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu: $5B6A = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), stream 2 (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT); then MAIN_MENU_SET.\nObserved: the start-up menu \"128 +3\" lists Loader, +3 BASIC, Calculator and 48 BASIC, above\n\"1982, 1986, 1987 Amstrad Plc.\" and \"Drives A: and M: available.\".","comment":"The editor's stack at $5BFF"},
        "1617": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1620": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1623": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "1625": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "1628": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's actions (MENU_ACTIONS) and text ($07FF) into $F6EA and $F6EC; $EC0D bit\n1 set (a menu up), bit 4 cleared, $EC0C = 0; the menu drawn ($189A), then the key loop\n(MAIN_KEY_LOOP). EDITOR_TO_MENU comes here with bank 7 and its stack already in place.","comment":"$F6EA = the menu's actions"},
        "1631": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1634": {"comment":"$F6EC = its text"},
        "1637": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1641": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 1 set (a menu up), bit 4 cleared"},
        "1648": {"comment":"$EC0C = 0: the bar on item 0"},
        "1652": {"comment":"The menu drawn"},
        "1656": {"comment":"The key loop"},
        "1659": {"synopsis":"The +3 BASIC editor and the Calculator: IX = $FD98, $5B6A = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack,\nstream 2, the key mode ($185A); it waits for a key (FLAGS bit 5), then: $EC0D bit 3 cleared;\nunless editing is in the lower screen ($EC0D bit 6), the bar for the mode $EC0E (0: +3\nBASIC, $1A5A; 4: the Calculator, $1A5F; any other: the start-up menu, EDITOR_TO_MENU); then\nEDITOR_ROWS.","comment":"IX = $FD98"},
        "1663": {"comment":"The editor's stack at $5BFF"},
        "1666": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1669": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1672": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "1674": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "1677": {"comment":"The key mode set"},
        "1680": {"comment":"Has a key arrived (FLAGS bit 5)?"},
        "1683": {"synopsis":"Until a key arrives (FLAGS bit 5)."},
        "1685": {"comment":"Not yet: wait"},
        "1687": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared"},
        "1692": {"comment":"Editing in the lower screen?"},
        "1694": {"comment":"Yes: no bar"},
        "1696": {"comment":"The mode: 4, the Calculator?"},
        "1701": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1703": {"comment":"0, +3 BASIC?"},
        "1705": {"comment":"Neither: the start-up menu"},
        "1708": {"comment":"The +3 BASIC bar"},
        "1711": {"comment":"To the rows"},
        "1713": {"synopsis":"Calculator: its bar ($1A5F).","comment":"The Calculator's bar"},
        "1716": {"synopsis":"The rows above and below the screen emptied ($11A4, $12F0); the Calculator goes straight to\nthe key loop. MENU_SET_GO jumps here.","comment":"The rows below the screen emptied"},
        "1719": {"comment":"The rows above emptied"},
        "1722": {"comment":"The Calculator?"},
        "1727": {"comment":"Yes: straight to the key loop"},
        "1729": {"comment":"Is E_PPC set?"},
        "1734": {"comment":"Yes: from it"},
        "1736": {"comment":"Is there a program (PROG = VARS)?"},
        "1739": {"comment":"BC = VARS"},
        "1744": {"comment":"Equal: no program"},
        "1748": {"comment":"No: $EC08 = 0"},
        "1751": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1754": {"synopsis":"HL = $EC08 in place of E_PPC (set to 0 first when there is no program).","comment":"HL = $EC08"},
        "1757": {"synopsis":"E_PPC = the number of the first line at or after HL (bank 0; ROM 3's FIND_LINE and LINE_NO);\nthen, unless $EC0D bit 5 is set, $EC06 = 0, the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD), the cursor\nshown ($0ABD) and the ENTER key's routine run ($0A0F); on to MAIN_KEY_LOOP.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1760": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: the first line at or after HL"},
        "1763": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "1766": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1769": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "1773": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 5 set?"},
        "1778": {"comment":"Yes: straight to the key loop"},
        "1780": {"comment":"$EC06 = 0"},
        "1783": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1786": {"comment":"The rows rebuilt"},
        "1789": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "1792": {"comment":"As ENTER"},
        "1795": {"synopsis":"The stack reset to $5BFF; then forever: a key (WAIT_KEY, $1871), a click (CLICK_A with PIP),\nand the key handled (KEY_DISPATCH).","comment":"The stack reset to $5BFF"},
        "1798": {"synopsis":"The next key.","comment":"A key"},
        "1801": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1802": {"comment":"A click of PIP"},
        "1805": {"comment":"The click"},
        "1808": {"comment":"The key back"},
        "1809": {"comment":"Handled"},
        "1812": {"comment":"Again"},
        "1814": {"synopsis":"Handles key A: looked up in KEY_TABLE_B when $EC0D bit 1 is set (a menu is up), else in\nKEY_TABLE_A (TABLE_DISPATCH, $2166); a key found runs its routine (and a click when that\nreturns no carry). A key not found: with $EC0D bit 1 set, MODE = 0; otherwise, with $EC0D\nbit 0 set, a click; below $A3, KEY_INSERT; $A3 and up go back to KEY_LOOP_WAIT, leaving\nKEY_DISPATCH's return address on the stack.","comment":"A menu up ($EC0D bit 1)?"},
        "1819": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1820": {"comment":"The menu's keys"},
        "1823": {"comment":"Yes: the menu's keys"},
        "1825": {"comment":"No menu: the editor's keys"},
        "1828": {"synopsis":"The key looked up (TABLE_DISPATCH).","comment":"Looked up and run: found?"},
        "1831": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "1833": {"comment":"Found: a click when it returns no carry"},
        "1838": {"synopsis":"Not in the table.","comment":"Not found: a menu up?"},
        "1839": {"comment":"No menu"},
        "1841": {"comment":"Menu up: MODE = 0"},
        "1842": {"comment":"MODE = 0: K mode back"},
        "1846": {"synopsis":"No menu up.","comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set?"},
        "1851": {"comment":"No: no click"},
        "1853": {"comment":"Yes: a click"},
        "1857": {"synopsis":"Below $A3: KEY_INSERT; otherwise ignored.","comment":"Below $A3?"},
        "1859": {"comment":"No: ignored (the return address left stacked)"},
        "1861": {"comment":"A character: put in"},
        "1864": {"synopsis":"Key $A9 and the editor's menu item 2 (MENU_SCREEN): moves editing between the upper screen\nand the two-row lower screen. Not in the Calculator ($EC0E = 4: returns with no carry). The\nrows cleared on the screen (ROWS_CLEAR), $EC0D bit 3 cleared and bit 6 flipped; bit 6 now\nset: SCREEN_TO_LOWER, clear: SCREEN_TO_UPPER.\nExit: carry.","comment":"The Calculator?"},
        "1869": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "1870": {"comment":"The rows cleared from the screen"},
        "1873": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared"},
        "1876": {"comment":"Bit 3 cleared"},
        "1878": {"comment":"Bit 6 flipped: the other screen"},
        "1879": {"comment":"Bit 6 flipped"},
        "1882": {"comment":"Is it the lower screen now?"},
        "1884": {"comment":"No: the upper screen"},
        "1886": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1891": {"synopsis":"Now the upper screen.","comment":"No: the upper"},
        "1894": {"synopsis":"Carry.","comment":"Carry"},
        "1896": {"synopsis":"Editing in the lower screen: lines 21-23 cleared ($1A8E), $EC0D bit 6 set, two editing rows\n($0EFB), the window for lines 22-23 ($1C95), the cursor's start (CURSOR_SET_LOWER); then\nSCREEN_REFILL.","comment":"Lines 21-23 cleared"},
        "1899": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 6 set: the lower screen"},
        "1902": {"comment":"Bit 6 set"},
        "1904": {"comment":"Two editing rows"},
        "1907": {"comment":"The window for lines 22-23"},
        "1910": {"comment":"The cursor's start"},
        "1915": {"synopsis":"Editing in the upper screen: $EC0D bit 6 cleared, UPPER_SETUP, the \"+3 BASIC\" bar ($1A5A);\nthen SCREEN_REFILL.","comment":"$EC0D bit 6 cleared: the upper screen"},
        "1918": {"comment":"Bit 6 cleared"},
        "1920": {"comment":"Editing in the upper screen"},
        "1923": {"comment":"The +3 BASIC bar"},
        "1926": {"synopsis":"When $FC9A is not 0, the line before it is looked up ($1418; HL is not kept, so $FC9A\nstays); the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD), and the cursor shown ($0ABD).","comment":"Rows above the screen?"},
        "1931": {"comment":"Yes: the line before $FC9A looked up"},
        "1934": {"comment":"The rows rebuilt"},
        "1937": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "1940": {"synopsis":"A click of RASP / 2 (CLICK_A).","comment":"A = RASP / 2"},
        "1943": {"comment":"Halved"},
        "1945": {"synopsis":"A short tone: DE = A, HL = $0C80, through ROM 3's TONE_OUT. Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept round TONE_OUT"},
        "1947": {"comment":"DE = A, the cycles"},
        "1949": {"comment":"E = A"},
        "1950": {"comment":"HL = $0C80, the pitch"},
        "1953": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's TONE_OUT; IX back.","comment":"ROM 3's TONE_OUT"},
        "1956": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "1959": {"synopsis":"A tone with DE = $30 and HL = $0300 (a higher pitch than CLICK_A's $0C80), through ROM 3's\nTONE_OUT. Called from $0DB5. Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept round TONE_OUT"},
        "1961": {"comment":"DE = $30 cycles"},
        "1964": {"comment":"HL = $0300, a higher pitch"},
        "1967": {"comment":"Through TONE_OUT"},
        "1969": {"synopsis":"Key $07 (EDIT) in the editor: the cursor off ($0AB7), $EC0D bit 1 set (a menu up), the bar\non the first item ($EC0C = 0), and the current menu (its text at ($F6EC)) drawn ($189A).\nExit: carry.\nObserved: EDIT in +3 BASIC opens Options: +3 BASIC, Renumber, Screen, Print, Exit.","comment":"The cursor off"},
        "1972": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 1 set: a menu up"},
        "1975": {"comment":"Bit 1 set"},
        "1977": {"comment":"$EC0C = 0: the bar on item 0"},
        "1978": {"comment":"$EC0C = 0"},
        "1980": {"comment":"The current menu's text"},
        "1983": {"comment":"Drawn"},
        "1984": {"comment":"Drawn"},
        "1987": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "1989": {"synopsis":"Keys $0D (ENTER) and $07 (EDIT) with a menu up: $EC0D bit 1 cleared, the screen under the\nmenu put back ($1950), the item $EC0C's routine from the actions at ($F6EA) run\n(TABLE_DISPATCH, $2166), then the cursor shown ($0ABD).","comment":"$EC0D bit 1 cleared: no menu up"},
        "1992": {"comment":"Bit 1 cleared"},
        "1995": {"comment":"A = the bar's item ($EC0C)"},
        "1996": {"comment":"The menu's actions"},
        "2001": {"comment":"The screen under the menu put back"},
        "2004": {"comment":"The item back"},
        "2006": {"comment":"The item's routine run"},
        "2009": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "2012": {"synopsis":"Key $0B (up) with a menu up: the bar one item up (MENU_MOVE with carry).","comment":"Carry: up"},
        "2013": {"comment":"Into MENU_MOVE"},
        "2015": {"synopsis":"Key $0A (down) with a menu up: the bar one item down (MENU_MOVE without carry).","comment":"No carry: down"},
        "2016": {"synopsis":"The bar moved from item $EC0C, up ($19B9) with carry, down ($19C8) without, in the menu\nwhose text is at ($F6EC); $EC0C = the new item.\nExit: carry.","comment":"A = the bar's item"},
        "2020": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "2021": {"comment":"The menu's text"},
        "2024": {"comment":"Up: the bar one item up"},
        "2027": {"comment":"Down: one item down"},
        "2030": {"comment":"HL = $EC0C"},
        "2031": {"comment":"The new item"},
        "2032": {"synopsis":"Item 0 of the editor's and the Calculator's menus (EDIT_MENU_ACTS, CALC_MENU_ACTS): nothing;\nthe menu is just gone.\nExit: carry.","comment":"Carry"},
        "2034": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's actions (MAIN_MENU_SET): a count (4), then for each item its number and\nroutine: 0 MENU_LOADER, 1 MENU_P3_BASIC, 2 MENU_CALCULATOR, 3 GO_48_BASIC. The text follows\nat $07FF: a count (5), the title \"128 +3  \" ended by $FF."},
        "2057": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's items, last letter with bit 7 set: Loader, +3 BASIC, Calculator, 48\nBASIC, then $A0. The bars $1A64, $1A5A and $1A5F print the first three ($0809, $080F, $0817)\nas their titles."},
        "2090": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu (EDITOR_MENU_SET): a count (5), then item 0 MENU_STAY, 1 MENU_RENUMBER, 2\nMENU_SCREEN, 3 MENU_PRINT, 4 MENU_EXIT; then ($083A) a count (6) and the title \"Options \"\nended by $FF."},
        "2116": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu items, last letter with bit 7 set: +3 BASIC, Renumber, Screen, Print,\nExit, then $A0."},
        "2148": {"synopsis":"The Calculator's menu (MENU_CALCULATOR): a count (2), item 0 MENU_STAY, item 1 MENU_EXIT;\nthen ($086B) a count (3) and the title \"Options \" ended by $FF."},
        "2165": {"synopsis":"The Calculator's menu items, last letter with bit 7 set: Calculator, Exit, then $A0."},
        "2180": {"synopsis":"MENU_LOADER's text for the lower screen (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT): AT 0,0, INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT 0,\nthen \"Insert tape and press PLAY\", ENTER, \"To cancel - press BREAK twice\", its last letter\nwith bit 7 set."},
        "2245": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 2: editing moved to the other screen (SCREEN_TOGGLE), then\nEDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"Editing on the other screen"},
        "2248": {"comment":"The editor's menu again"},
        "2250": {"synopsis":"Back to the start-up menu (the editor's menu item 4, the Calculator's item 1): $EC0D bit 6\ncleared, UPPER_SETUP, screen lines 0-23 cleared ($1D6B), bank 0 and the machine stack\n(BANK0_STACK), then MAIN_MENU.","comment":"$EC0D bit 6 cleared"},
        "2253": {"comment":"Bit 6 cleared"},
        "2255": {"comment":"Editing in the upper screen"},
        "2258": {"comment":"Lines 0-23 cleared"},
        "2262": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "2265": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2268": {"comment":"The start-up menu"},
        "2271": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's 48 BASIC (MENU_ACTIONS item 3): bank 0 and the machine stack\n(BANK0_STACK), then ROM 1's $1488 through $3E80, which does the rest.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2274": {"comment":"ROM 1's $1488, through $3E80 and the word after"},
        "2280": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 0, Loader: the \"Loader\" bar ($1A64), LOADER_MSG in the lower screen\n(TV_FLAG bit 0 set meanwhile) unless $5B66 bit 4 is set, TV_FLAG bit 6 set, $EC0E = 7, AT\n0,0 ($191D), bank 0 (BANK0_STACK), then ROM 1's $12E8 through $3E80.","comment":"The Loader bar"},
        "2283": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 set: the lower screen"},
        "2286": {"comment":"Bit 0 set"},
        "2288": {"comment":"The loader's message"},
        "2291": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "2292": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 4 set?"},
        "2298": {"comment":"Yes: no message"},
        "2300": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "2303": {"synopsis":"With or without the message: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared and bit 6 set, $EC0E = 7, AT 0,0, then\nROM 1's $12E8.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared, bit 6 set"},
        "2305": {"comment":"Bit 6 set"},
        "2307": {"comment":"$EC0E = 7"},
        "2309": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2312": {"comment":"AT 0,0"},
        "2315": {"comment":"PRINT_AT_BC"},
        "2318": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2321": {"comment":"ROM 1's $12E8, through $3E80 and the word after"},
        "2327": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 1: the program renumbered ($1A95; a click when that returns no\ncarry), E_PPC = 0, $EC08 = 0, then MENU_BAR_BACK.","comment":"The program renumbered"},
        "2330": {"comment":"A click when that returns no carry"},
        "2333": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "2336": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2339": {"comment":"$EC08 = 0"},
        "2342": {"comment":"The bar, then the editor's menu"},
        "2344": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 3: bank 0 (BANK0_STACK) and ROM 1's $1451 through $3E80 (LLIST run as\na command), then MENU_BAR_BACK.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2347": {"comment":"ROM 1's $1451 (LLIST run), through $3E80"},
        "2352": {"synopsis":"Unless editing is in the lower screen ($EC0D bit 6), the \"+3 BASIC\" bar again (as\nMENU_P3_BASIC); then EDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"Editing in the lower screen?"},
        "2357": {"comment":"Yes: no bar"},
        "2359": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 1, +3 BASIC: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared, the \"+3 BASIC\" bar ($1A5A),\nthen EDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared"},
        "2362": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared"},
        "2364": {"comment":"The +3 BASIC bar"},
        "2367": {"synopsis":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 cleared; mode 0 (+3 BASIC), the editor's menu (EDIT_MENU_ACTS, its text\nat $083A); then MENU_SET_GO.","comment":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 cleared"},
        "2370": {"comment":"Bit 5 cleared"},
        "2372": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "2374": {"comment":"Mode 0: +3 BASIC"},
        "2376": {"comment":"The editor's menu actions"},
        "2379": {"comment":"Its text"},
        "2382": {"comment":"Set and on"},
        "2384": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 2: $EC0D bits 5 and 4 set, bit 6 cleared; UPPER_SETUP; the\n\"Calculator\" bar ($1A5F); $EC0E = 4; E_PPC = 0; the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD); the cursor\nat row 0, column 0 ($0AC3); mode 4 and the Calculator's menu (CALC_MENU_ACTS, its text at\n$086B), then MENU_SET_GO.","comment":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 set, bit 6 cleared"},
        "2387": {"comment":"Bit 5 set"},
        "2389": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "2391": {"comment":"Bit 6 cleared"},
        "2393": {"comment":"Editing in the upper screen"},
        "2396": {"comment":"The Calculator's bar"},
        "2399": {"comment":"$EC0E = 4"},
        "2401": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2404": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "2407": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2410": {"comment":"The rows rebuilt"},
        "2413": {"comment":"Row 0, column 0"},
        "2416": {"comment":"A = 0: the remembered column"},
        "2417": {"comment":"The cursor put there"},
        "2420": {"comment":"Mode 4: the Calculator"},
        "2422": {"comment":"The Calculator's menu actions"},
        "2425": {"comment":"Its text"},
        "2428": {"synopsis":"$EC0E = A (the mode), $F6EA = HL (the menu's actions), $F6EC = DE (its text), then on in\nEDITOR_MAIN at EDITOR_ROWS.","comment":"$EC0E = the mode"},
        "2431": {"comment":"$F6EA = the actions"},
        "2434": {"comment":"$F6EC = the text"},
        "2438": {"comment":"On in EDITOR_MAIN"},
        "2441": {"synopsis":"Editing in the upper screen: 21 editing rows ($0EED), the window for lines 0-20 ($1C8C), and\nthe cursor's start (CURSOR_SET_UPPER).","comment":"21 editing rows in the upper screen"},
        "2444": {"comment":"The window for lines 0-20"},
        "2447": {"comment":"The cursor's start"},
        "2450": {"synopsis":"EDITOR_MAIN with a mode other than 0 or 4: screen lines 0-23 cleared ($1D6B), then\nMAIN_MENU_SET (the start-up menu set up and drawn).","comment":"Lines 0-23 cleared"},
        "2454": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "2457": {"comment":"The start-up menu set and drawn"},
        "2460": {"synopsis":"CURSOR_SET_UPPER's block for $2152: a count (6), then $F6EE-$F6F3 = 0, 0, 0, 4, $10, $14\n(row, column and remembered column 0, then three bytes for the upper screen)."},
        "2467": {"synopsis":"CURSOR_SET_LOWER's block: a count (6), then $F6EE-$F6F3 = 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1."},
        "2474": {"synopsis":"$F6EE-$F6F3 from CURS_LOWER_INIT ($2152 copies a counted block).","comment":"The lower screen's block"},
        "2477": {"comment":"To $F6EE-$F6F3"},
        "2480": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "2483": {"synopsis":"$F6EE-$F6F3 from CURS_UPPER_INIT.","comment":"The upper screen's block"},
        "2486": {"comment":"To $F6EE-$F6F3"},
        "2489": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "2492": {"synopsis":"A character key (KEY_CHAR, codes below $A3): with $EC0D bit 0 set it is ignored (the cursor\nshown again, $0ABD). Otherwise $EC0D bit 7 cleared and bit 3 set (the line changed), the\ncursor off ($0AB7), the character put in at the cursor ($0F4F), the cursor one place on\n($0C43), $EC0D bit 7 set again; the cursor stored with its column as the remembered one and\nshown ($0AC3), or, when it could not move, shown where it was ($0ABD).","comment":"HL = $EC0D"},
        "2495": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "2497": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set?"},
        "2499": {"comment":"Yes: the key ignored, the cursor shown"},
        "2502": {"comment":"Bit 7 cleared, bit 3 set: the line changed"},
        "2504": {"comment":"Bit 3 set"},
        "2506": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "2507": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "2508": {"comment":"The cursor off"},
        "2512": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "2513": {"comment":"The character put in at the cursor"},
        "2517": {"comment":"The cursor one place on"},
        "2521": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set again"},
        "2522": {"comment":"Bit 7 set"},
        "2524": {"comment":"Could not move: shown where it was"},
        "2527": {"comment":"Moved: stored, its column remembered"},
        "2531": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "2534": {"synopsis":"Key $AA: $EC0D bit 3 set, the cursor off ($0AB7), the character under it taken out ($0FE0),\nthen the cursor shown ($0AC3, the column remembered).","comment":"$EC0D bit 3 set: the line changed"},
        "2537": {"comment":"Bit 3 set"},
        "2539": {"comment":"The cursor off"},
        "2542": {"comment":"The character under it taken out"},
        "2545": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "2546": {"comment":"A = the column, remembered"},
        "2547": {"comment":"Shown there"},
        "2550": {"synopsis":"Key $0C (DELETE): $EC0D bit 0 cleared and bit 3 set, the cursor off ($0AB7), one place back\n($0C26; at the start nothing more, the cursor shown, $0ABD); the character there taken out\n($0FE0), then the cursor shown ($0AC3, the column remembered).","comment":"HL = $EC0D"},
        "2553": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared, bit 3 set"},
        "2557": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2560": {"comment":"One place back: not possible?"},
        "2564": {"comment":"Then only CURSOR_ON"},
        "2567": {"comment":"LINE_DELETE_CHAR: the character there out"},
        "2570": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "2571": {"comment":"The column remembered"},
        "2572": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2575": {"synopsis":"Key $0D (ENTER), also called from $0700: the cursor off. A row that is empty and is a\nwhole line by itself (flags bits 0 and 3) does nothing. Otherwise, when the line was changed\n($EC0D bit 3), it is entered ($0D59; nothing more when that returns no carry); then the\ncursor goes to the line's end ($0D17), one place on ($0C43), a blank row is made there\n($0F9C), and the cursor is stored at its column 0 (CURSOR_PUT).\nExit: carry.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2578": {"comment":"The remembered column kept"},
        "2579": {"comment":"DE = the cursor row's place"},
        "2583": {"comment":"Anything on the row?"},
        "2589": {"comment":"Text: the line entered if changed"},
        "2591": {"comment":"Empty: a line of one row (flags bits 0 and 3)?"},
        "2601": {"synopsis":"Changed ($EC0D bit 3)? Then the line entered ($0D59)."},
        "2606": {"comment":"Unchanged: on to the next line"},
        "2608": {"comment":"EDIT_LINE_ENTER"},
        "2611": {"comment":"A report: the cursor shown only"},
        "2613": {"synopsis":"The cursor to the line's end ($0D17), one place on, a blank row there ($0F9C), column 0.","comment":"TO_LINE_END"},
        "2616": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT: one place on"},
        "2619": {"comment":"NEW_BLANK_ROW: a blank row there"},
        "2622": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "2624": {"comment":"A = the remembered column back"},
        "2626": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2629": {"synopsis":"An empty one-row line: only the cursor shown.","comment":"A back"},
        "2631": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2634": {"synopsis":"Not entered: the cursor shown.","comment":"A back"},
        "2635": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2638": {"synopsis":"Key $A6: E_PPC = the program's first line (bank 0; ROM 3's FIND_LINE from 0 and LINE_NO);\nthe cursor's colour $0F ($1CA3), the rows rebuilt ($03FA), the cursor shown\n(CURSOR_ON). Not in the Calculator (no carry: a click).\nExit: carry.","comment":"The Calculator: no carry, a click"},
        "2644": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2647": {"comment":"From line 0"},
        "2650": {"comment":"Bank 0 and its stack ($05A7): the program"},
        "2653": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: HL = the first line"},
        "2656": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "2659": {"comment":"Back to bank 7 and its stack ($05CC)"},
        "2662": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "2666": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $0F"},
        "2668": {"comment":"$1CA3 sets the cursor's colour"},
        "2671": {"comment":"$03FA: the rows rebuilt"},
        "2674": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "2675": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2678": {"synopsis":"Key $A5: E_PPC = the line before the first one numbered 9999 or more (FIND_LINE's DE, then\nLINE_NO), normally the program's last; the cursor's colour $0F, the rows rebuilt, the cursor\nshown. Not in the Calculator (no carry: a click).\nExit: carry.","comment":"The Calculator: no carry, a click"},
        "2684": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2687": {"comment":"Line 9999"},
        "2690": {"comment":"Bank 0 and its stack ($05A7): the program"},
        "2693": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: DE = the line before"},
        "2696": {"comment":"HL = the line before it"},
        "2697": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "2700": {"comment":"Back to bank 7 and its stack ($05CC)"},
        "2703": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "2707": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $0F"},
        "2709": {"comment":"$1CA3 sets the cursor's colour"},
        "2712": {"comment":"$03FA: the rows rebuilt"},
        "2715": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "2716": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2719": {"synopsis":"Key $AF: the cursor off, back to the start of the previous word ($0CB5); stored with the\ncolumn remembered (CURSOR_PUT), or, when it did not move, shown again (CURSOR_ON).","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2722": {"comment":"WORD_LEFT"},
        "2725": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2728": {"comment":"The column remembered: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2732": {"synopsis":"Key $AE: the cursor off, on to the start of the next word ($0CD4); stored (CURSOR_PUT), or,\nwhen it did not move, shown again.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2735": {"comment":"WORD_RIGHT"},
        "2738": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2740": {"comment":"The column remembered: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2743": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off the screen: its place (CURSOR_GET), the cell's attribute put back\n($1749).\nExit: C = the row, B = the column, A = the remembered column, HL = $F6F1.","comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "2746": {"comment":"$1749: the cell's attribute back"},
        "2749": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor at its place (CURSOR_GET, then $173A: the cell's attribute kept, the\ncursor's colour put in).\nExit: as CURSOR_GET.","comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "2752": {"comment":"$173A: the cursor's colour put in the cell"},
        "2755": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to row C, column B, remembered column A (CURSOR_STORE), sets its colour to\n$0F ($1CA3: ink 7 on paper 1), and shows it ($173A). Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"CURSOR_STORE"},
        "2758": {"comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "2760": {"comment":"Ink 7 on paper 1"},
        "2762": {"comment":"$1CA3 sets the cursor's colour"},
        "2765": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "2767": {"comment":"$173A: the cursor's colour put in the cell"},
        "2770": {"synopsis":"C = the cursor's row ($F6EE), B = its column ($F6EF), A = the remembered column ($F6F0), the\none up and down movement aim for.\nExit: HL = $F6F1.","comment":"HL = the cursor's row, $F6EE"},
        "2773": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "2775": {"comment":"B = the column"},
        "2777": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2778": {"comment":"HL = $F6F1"},
        "2780": {"synopsis":"The other way: $F6EE = C, $F6EF = B, $F6F0 = A.\nExit: HL = $F6F0.","comment":"HL = the cursor's row, $F6EE"},
        "2783": {"comment":"The row"},
        "2785": {"comment":"The column"},
        "2787": {"comment":"The remembered column"},
        "2789": {"synopsis":"A = the character at column B of window row C (ROW_ADDRESS); 0 is no character.\nExit: DE = the row. Keeps BC, HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "2790": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "2793": {"comment":"HL = B"},
        "2796": {"comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "2797": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "2800": {"synopsis":"Key $AC (the key table at $05E6): the cursor down ten rows. Each step is ROW_DOWN, the\ncursor kept as\nnear the remembered column ($F6F0) as the row's text allows (COL_PLACE_R) and stored at once\n(the cursor at $F6EE, $0ADC). A row with no text sends it back up one row (ROW_UP); the last\nrow stops it.\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($0AC3); no carry (a click) when it could not go the whole\nway, or did not move at all ($0ABD).","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2803": {"comment":"E = the remembered column, D = 10 rows"},
        "2806": {"synopsis":"One row down."},
        "2807": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "2811": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2813": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2814": {"comment":"Each row's place stored"},
        "2817": {"comment":"Column E placed in the row's text"},
        "2821": {"comment":"No text on the row?"},
        "2823": {"comment":"Ten rows yet?"},
        "2826": {"comment":"Ten rows: done"},
        "2827": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2829": {"synopsis":"A row without text: back up one row, the column placed (COL_PLACE_R); no carry."},
        "2830": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up one"},
        "2834": {"comment":"Column E"},
        "2835": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_R"},
        "2838": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2839": {"comment":"No carry: a click"},
        "2840": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2842": {"synopsis":"Key $AD (the key table at $05E6): the cursor up ten rows, as ED_KEY_TEN_DOWN in the other\ndirection\n(ROW_UP, COL_PLACE_L). A row with no text sends it back down one row, to the start of that\nrow's text.\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($0AC3); no carry (a click) when it could not go the whole\nway.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2845": {"comment":"E = the remembered column, D = 10 rows"},
        "2848": {"synopsis":"One row up."},
        "2849": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "2853": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2855": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2856": {"comment":"Each row's place stored"},
        "2859": {"comment":"Column E placed in the row's text"},
        "2860": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_L"},
        "2863": {"comment":"No text on the row?"},
        "2865": {"comment":"Ten rows yet?"},
        "2868": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2869": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2872": {"synopsis":"A row without text: back down one row, to the start of its text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT from\ncolumn 0).","comment":"The flags (no carry) kept"},
        "2873": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN: back down one"},
        "2876": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "2878": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "2882": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2885": {"synopsis":"Key $A7 (the key table at $05E6): the cursor to the end of its line's text (TO_LINE_END);\nthat column\nbecomes the remembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2888": {"comment":"TO_LINE_END"},
        "2891": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2894": {"comment":"The new column remembered"},
        "2895": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2898": {"synopsis":"Key $A8 (the key table at $05E6): the cursor to the start of its line's text\n(TO_LINE_START); that\ncolumn becomes the remembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2901": {"comment":"TO_LINE_START"},
        "2904": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2907": {"comment":"The new column remembered"},
        "2908": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2911": {"synopsis":"Key $0B (the key table at $05E6): the cursor up one row (ROW_UP), as near the remembered\ncolumn ($F6F0)\nas the row's text allows (COL_PLACE_L); the remembered column is kept. A row with no text\nsends the cursor back down, to the column placed there (COL_PLACE_R).\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($0AC3); no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2914": {"comment":"E = the remembered column"},
        "2916": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "2920": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2923": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_L)"},
        "2927": {"comment":"A = the remembered column, kept"},
        "2928": {"comment":"Text: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2931": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "2932": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN: back down"},
        "2935": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "2937": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_R"},
        "2941": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2944": {"synopsis":"Key $0A (the key table at $05E6): the cursor down one row (ROW_DOWN), as near the remembered\ncolumn as\nthe row's text allows (COL_PLACE_L); a row with no text sends it back up (ROW_UP,\nCOL_PLACE_R).\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($0AC3); no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2947": {"comment":"E = the remembered column"},
        "2949": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "2953": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2956": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_L)"},
        "2960": {"comment":"A = the remembered column, kept"},
        "2961": {"comment":"Text: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2965": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up"},
        "2969": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_R)"},
        "2973": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2974": {"comment":"No carry: a click"},
        "2975": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2978": {"synopsis":"Key $08 (the key table at $05E6): the cursor one place left (CURSOR_LEFT); the new column\nbecomes the\nremembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2981": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "2984": {"comment":"Moved: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2987": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2990": {"synopsis":"Key $09 (the key table at $05E6): the cursor one place right (CURSOR_RIGHT); the new column\nbecomes the\nremembered one. When that fails after going down a row, the cursor goes back up to the end\nof that row's text (TEXT_END_LEFT from column 31).\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2993": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "2996": {"comment":"Moved: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2999": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "3000": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up"},
        "3003": {"comment":"From column 31: the end of the row's text"},
        "3005": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "3008": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "3009": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "3012": {"synopsis":"Places column B of row C in the row's text: TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT, and TEXT_END_LEFT when that\nfails.\nExit: carry when the row has text (B moved onto or next to it); no carry for a row with\nnone. Keeps DE."},
        "3013": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "3016": {"comment":"Failed: TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "3021": {"synopsis":"As COL_PLACE_R, the other way round: TEXT_END_LEFT first, then TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT.\nExit: carry when the row has text. Keeps DE."},
        "3022": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "3025": {"comment":"Failed: TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "3030": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor's row C up one:\n1. Leaving the first row of an edited line enters it first (LEAVE_FIRST_ROW); a report there\nstops the move.\n2. Row C, when it holds no text, is removed (REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW).\n3. With C greater than ($F6F1), C goes up one; otherwise the window scrolls down a row\n($053A) and C stays; when it cannot scroll, C goes up unless it is row 0.\nExit: carry when the cursor moved (or the window scrolled); no carry otherwise. Keeps B.","comment":"LEAVE_FIRST_ROW: an edited line entered first"},
        "3033": {"comment":"A report while entering the line: no move"},
        "3036": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3039": {"comment":"Row C empty? Removed"},
        "3048": {"comment":"Above row ($F6F1)?"},
        "3055": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "3056": {"comment":"The window scrolled down a row"},
        "3060": {"comment":"Scrolled: C stays"},
        "3061": {"comment":"Row 0: no move"},
        "3064": {"synopsis":"C one row up; carry."},
        "3066": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "3067": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor's row C down one: a row C with no text is removed instead\n(REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW), the rows below moving up into it. Otherwise ROW_DOWN_TEXT.\nExit: carry when the cursor moved (or the window scrolled). Keeps B."},
        "3068": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3071": {"comment":"Row C empty? Removed instead"},
        "3077": {"comment":"Text: on down"},
        "3079": {"comment":"REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW"},
        "3082": {"synopsis":"Leaving the last row of an edited line enters it first (LEAVE_LAST_ROW; a report stops the\nmove). With C less than ($F6F2), C goes down one; otherwise the window scrolls up a row\n($0504) and C stays; when it cannot scroll, C goes down unless it is already row ($F6F3).","comment":"LEAVE_LAST_ROW: an edited line entered first"},
        "3085": {"comment":"A report: no move"},
        "3087": {"comment":"Below row ($F6F2)?"},
        "3095": {"comment":"The row and HL kept"},
        "3097": {"comment":"The window scrolled up a row"},
        "3102": {"comment":"Scrolled: C stays"},
        "3103": {"comment":"Row ($F6F3): no move"},
        "3107": {"synopsis":"C one row down; carry."},
        "3109": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "3110": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor (row C, column B) one place left within the text: to the column before, or\npast the gaps before it (TEXT_END_LEFT); from column 0 (or with nothing to the left) up a\nrow (ROW_UP), to the end of that row's text.\nExit: carry and A = the new column when it moved; no carry, B = 0 and A as on entry\notherwise.\nChanges: DE.","comment":"D = the remembered column"},
        "3111": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "3115": {"comment":"E = the column"},
        "3116": {"comment":"Back to the text"},
        "3119": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3120": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "3121": {"synopsis":"Nothing to the left on this row: up a row, to the end of its text."},
        "3122": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "3126": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3127": {"comment":"No row above: no carry"},
        "3128": {"comment":"The end of the row above's text"},
        "3133": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3134": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "3135": {"comment":"Not moved: A back, B = 0"},
        "3139": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor (row C, column B) one place right within the text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT). Past\nthe row's end:\n1. With $EC0D bit 7 clear and row C not continued (flags bit 1), the row is marked as\ncontinued (bit 1 set, bit 3 cleared), the cursor goes down a row (ROW_DOWN) and a blank\nrow flagged as the line's last row is inserted there (INSERT_ROW), the first ($FD6B)\ncolumns of a row then cleared ($16EE); carry and A = column.\n2. Otherwise down a row (ROW_DOWN) to the start of its text.\nExit: carry and A = the new column when it moved.\nChanges: DE.","comment":"D = the remembered column"},
        "3140": {"comment":"One column right"},
        "3141": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3146": {"comment":"E = the new column"},
        "3147": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT: text there?"},
        "3150": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3152": {"synopsis":"Past the row's end.","comment":"B back to column 31"},
        "3153": {"comment":"The row and HL kept"},
        "3155": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set?"},
        "3162": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3165": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3170": {"comment":"Row C continued already?"},
        "3174": {"comment":"Now continued, no longer the line's last row"},
        "3178": {"comment":"DE = the row after it"},
        "3183": {"comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "3185": {"comment":"Row C's old flags kept"},
        "3186": {"comment":"Down a row"},
        "3189": {"comment":"A = them"},
        "3190": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3193": {"comment":"DE = the row after it"},
        "3198": {"comment":"Flags: not the first row, the last"},
        "3202": {"comment":"A blank row inserted at row C"},
        "3205": {"comment":"The first ($FD6B) columns of the row at DE cleared"},
        "3208": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3209": {"comment":"Carry: moved"},
        "3211": {"synopsis":"Down a row, to the start of its text; no carry (A = E, B = 0) when it has none.","comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "3214": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "3218": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3219": {"comment":"No row below: no carry"},
        "3220": {"comment":"The start of the new row's text"},
        "3222": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "3225": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3226": {"comment":"Text: carry"},
        "3227": {"comment":"None: A = E, B = 0, no carry"},
        "3231": {"synopsis":"TEXT_FROM_COL on window row C: carry when column B is in or just after the row's text, or\ntext follows it (B moved to it). Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3233": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3236": {"comment":"TEXT_FROM_COL"},
        "3239": {"comment":"MOVE_END: DE and HL back"},
        "3242": {"synopsis":"TEXT_BACK_FROM on window row C: carry when column B holds a character, or B moved back to\njust after the last character before it. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3244": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3247": {"comment":"TEXT_BACK_FROM"},
        "3250": {"comment":"MOVE_END: DE and HL back"},
        "3253": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to the start of the word before it: left (CURSOR_LEFT) past any spaces,\nthen on left to the space before the word, then right one place (CURSOR_RIGHT).\nExit: carry when it got there; no carry when it ran out of text. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3255": {"synopsis":"Left past spaces.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "3258": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "3260": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "3263": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3267": {"synopsis":"Left to the space before the word.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "3270": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "3272": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "3275": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3279": {"comment":"Right onto the word's first character"},
        "3282": {"synopsis":"No more text: no carry.","comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "3284": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to the start of the next word: right (CURSOR_RIGHT) to the next space, then\npast the spaces to a character.\nExit: carry when it got there; no carry (one place back left) when no word follows on the\nrow. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3286": {"synopsis":"Right to a space.","comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "3289": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "3291": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "3294": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3298": {"synopsis":"Right past spaces.","comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "3301": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "3303": {"comment":"More text on the row?"},
        "3308": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "3311": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3315": {"comment":"Carry: at the word"},
        "3316": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "3318": {"synopsis":"No word follows: back one place, no carry.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT: back one place"},
        "3321": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "3322": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "3324": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor up (ROW_UP) to its line's first row (flags bit 0) and there to the start of\nthe text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT from column 0).\nExit: carry when it got there. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3326": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3329": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3333": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "3337": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "3340": {"comment":"Moved: again"},
        "3342": {"comment":"Could not: MOVE_END"},
        "3344": {"synopsis":"First row: the start of its text.","comment":"From column 0"},
        "3346": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "3349": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "3351": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor down (ROW_DOWN) to its line's last row (flags bit 3) and there to just\nafter the text (TEXT_END_LEFT from column 31).\nExit: carry when it got there. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3353": {"synopsis":"The line's last row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3356": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3360": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "3364": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "3367": {"comment":"Moved: again"},
        "3369": {"comment":"Could not: MOVE_END"},
        "3371": {"synopsis":"Last row: the end of its text.","comment":"From column 31"},
        "3373": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "3376": {"synopsis":"HL and DE restored.","comment":"HL and DE back"},
        "3379": {"synopsis":"Before the cursor leaves row C downwards: when the line was edited ($EC0D bit 3) and row C\nis its last row (flags bit 3), the line is entered (EDIT_LINE_ENTER).\nExit: carry when the move may go on.","comment":"A = the editor's flags"},
        "3382": {"comment":"The line edited?"},
        "3386": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3389": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3393": {"comment":"Row C its line's last?"},
        "3397": {"comment":"EDIT_LINE_ENTER"},
        "3399": {"synopsis":"As LEAVE_LAST_ROW, upwards: when the line was edited ($EC0D bit 3) and row C is its first\nrow (flags bit 0), the line is entered (EDIT_LINE_ENTER).\nExit: carry when the move may go on.","comment":"A = the editor's flags"},
        "3402": {"comment":"The line edited?"},
        "3406": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3409": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3413": {"comment":"Row C its line's first?"},
        "3417": {"synopsis":"Enters the edited line the cursor is on:\n1. Up from row C to the line's first row (flags bit 0): the reader LINE_ROWS_CHAR is set to\nstart there in state 2 (the window's rows); when the line starts above the window, in\nstate 1 at row 0 (the rows kept above). $EC00-$EC02 (state with bit 7 set, column 0, row)\nand a copy in $EC03-$EC05; $EC06 = 0.\n2. $142D and $1DFA, then, in bank 0 on its stack ($05A7), the routine at $2650 in\nROM 1 through $3E80 (which pages ROM 1 in and calls the address in the word after\nthe CALL); back in bank 7 ($05CC) with interrupts on.\n3. No report (ERR_NR = $FF): $EC0D bit 3 cleared, $1758, $03FA unless in Calculator\nmode ($EC0E = 4), a tone ($07A7), the cursor reloaded; carry.\n4. A report: ENTER_FAILED.\nExit: carry when the cursor may move on.","comment":"State 2: the window's rows"},
        "3419": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3422": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3426": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "3430": {"comment":"Up a row"},
        "3431": {"comment":"Still in the window?"},
        "3434": {"comment":"Above the window: state 1, row 0"},
        "3438": {"synopsis":"The reader's state, column 0 and row, twice.","comment":"HL = the reader, $EC00"},
        "3441": {"comment":"DE = its copy, $EC03"},
        "3444": {"comment":"Bit 7: counting to the cursor"},
        "3446": {"comment":"The state"},
        "3450": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "3456": {"comment":"Row C"},
        "3459": {"comment":"No characters counted yet"},
        "3465": {"comment":"$142D: the expansion reset"},
        "3468": {"comment":"$1DFA: the rows into the edit line"},
        "3471": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "3473": {"comment":"Bank 0 and its stack ($05A7)"},
        "3476": {"comment":"ROM 1's $24F0, the word after the CALL"},
        "3481": {"comment":"Back to bank 7 and its stack ($05CC)"},
        "3484": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "3485": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "3487": {"comment":"A report (ERR_NR not $FF)?"},
        "3493": {"comment":"No report: the line no longer edited"},
        "3498": {"comment":"$1758: the key mode reset"},
        "3501": {"comment":"Calculator mode?"},
        "3506": {"comment":"Not the Calculator: the rows rebuilt ($03FA)"},
        "3509": {"comment":"A tone"},
        "3512": {"comment":"CURSOR_GET: the cursor reloaded"},
        "3515": {"comment":"Carry: entered"},
        "3517": {"synopsis":"A report while the line was entered: the reader set back to the line's start ($EC03-$EC05\ncopied to $EC00-$EC02, bit 7 cleared), BC from $1DF6 (or $EC06 when it gives no carry), and\nthe cursor moved by the difference: left (CURSOR_LEFT) $EC06 - BC places, or right\n(CURSOR_RIGHT, $EC0D bit 7 cleared) BC - $EC06 places, each stopping when the cursor cannot\nmove. Then $EC0D bit 7 set, the cursor stored, the cursor's colour $17 (instead of $0F)\ngiven to $1CA3; no carry, so the move does not happen.","comment":"The reader back at the line's start, not counting"},
        "3523": {"comment":"The state, bit 7 cleared"},
        "3529": {"comment":"The column"},
        "3533": {"comment":"The row"},
        "3535": {"comment":"BC = the count from $1DF6"},
        "3538": {"comment":"No carry: BC = $EC06, no move"},
        "3544": {"synopsis":"HL = $EC06 - BC; the cursor reloaded.","comment":"HL = $EC06 - BC"},
        "3550": {"comment":"The subtraction's flags kept"},
        "3552": {"comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "3557": {"comment":"BC the larger: right"},
        "3559": {"comment":"Equal: no move"},
        "3561": {"synopsis":"One place left."},
        "3562": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3563": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "3567": {"comment":"Could not: done"},
        "3569": {"comment":"One place fewer"},
        "3570": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "3574": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3576": {"synopsis":"BC above $EC06: HL = BC - $EC06 places right."},
        "3577": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 cleared while moving right"},
        "3583": {"comment":"DE = $EC06 - BC"},
        "3584": {"comment":"HL = BC - $EC06"},
        "3590": {"synopsis":"One place right."},
        "3591": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3592": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "3596": {"comment":"Could not: done"},
        "3598": {"comment":"One place fewer"},
        "3599": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "3603": {"synopsis":"The cursor stored, its colour $17; no carry.","comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set"},
        "3608": {"comment":"CURSOR_STORE"},
        "3611": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $17"},
        "3613": {"comment":"$1CA3 sets the cursor's colour"},
        "3616": {"comment":"No carry: the move not made"},
        "3618": {"synopsis":"Gives the next character of the line being entered, read from the editor's rows (from\n$1F30). The reader's state is $EC00 (low four bits; bit 7 set while characters before the\ncursor are counted), column $EC01 and row $EC02. While bit 7 is set, $EC06 counts each call.\nThe state picks the routine through ROWS_CHAR_TABLE ($2166): 1 the rows kept above\nthe window (ROWS_ABOVE_CHAR), 2 the window's rows (ROWS_SCREEN_CHAR), 4 the rows kept below\nit (ROWS_BELOW_CHAR); each passes over 0s (no character) and returns the next character with\nL = the new state; 8, the line's end, is not in the table and gives $0D.\nExit: A = the character; the column, row and state stored back.","comment":"HL = the reader's state"},
        "3621": {"comment":"Counting to the cursor?"},
        "3625": {"comment":"One more character before the cursor"},
        "3632": {"synopsis":"State, column and row; the state's routine.","comment":"HL = the reader"},
        "3635": {"comment":"A = the state"},
        "3637": {"comment":"B = the column"},
        "3639": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "3640": {"comment":"The row's address kept"},
        "3641": {"comment":"The state's routine"},
        "3643": {"comment":"HL = ROWS_CHAR_TABLE"},
        "3646": {"comment":"$2166: the state's routine"},
        "3649": {"comment":"E = the new state"},
        "3651": {"comment":"No routine (state 8): $0D"},
        "3655": {"synopsis":"Row, column and the new state stored.","comment":"The row"},
        "3657": {"comment":"The column"},
        "3659": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "3660": {"comment":"The state's low four bits replaced"},
        "3665": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "3667": {"synopsis":"LINE_ROWS_CHAR's table for $2166: a count (3), then for each state its number and\nroutine: 2 ROWS_SCREEN_CHAR, 4 ROWS_BELOW_CHAR, 1 ROWS_ABOVE_CHAR."},
        "3677": {"synopsis":"State 1: the next character from row C of the rows kept above the window ($F9DE,\nROW_ADDRESS_HL through $1385); after their last row on to state 2 at row 0, column 0.\nExit: A = the character, L = 1.","comment":"ABOVE_ROW_ADDR: DE = row C above the window"},
        "3680": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "3683": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3685": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "3689": {"comment":"State 1"},
        "3692": {"synopsis":"The next row; past the last, state 2.","comment":"The next row"},
        "3693": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "3695": {"comment":"Past the rows above? (HL = the word at $F9DB)"},
        "3699": {"comment":"C against the byte at ($F9DB), not the count itself"},
        "3702": {"comment":"State 2 at row 0, column 0"},
        "3706": {"synopsis":"State 2: the next character from window row C (ROW_ADDRESS). Reaching the cursor's place\n($F6EE row, $F6EF column) clears $EC00 bit 7, which stops the count in $EC06. A row that is\nits line's last (flags bit 3) ends the line ($0D, state 8); past row ($F6F3) on to state 4\nat row 1.\nExit: A = the character, L = 2.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "3707": {"comment":"The cursor's row?"},
        "3714": {"comment":"The cursor's column?"},
        "3719": {"comment":"Reached: stop counting"},
        "3724": {"synopsis":"HL back."},
        "3725": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3728": {"comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "3731": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3733": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "3737": {"comment":"State 2"},
        "3740": {"synopsis":"The row's end: the line's last row?","comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3744": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "3748": {"comment":"State 8: the line's end"},
        "3753": {"synopsis":"The next row; past row ($F6F3), state 4.","comment":"HL = the window's last row, $F6F3"},
        "3756": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "3757": {"comment":"Past row ($F6F3)?"},
        "3759": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "3763": {"comment":"State 4 at row 1, column 0"},
        "3767": {"synopsis":"State 4: the next character from row C of the rows kept below the window ($F6F8,\nROW_ADDRESS_HL through $1291, rows 1 up to the count in $F6F5). The line's last row (flags\nbit 3), or the last row kept, ends the line ($0D, state 8).\nExit: A = the character, L = 4.","comment":"BELOW_ROW_ADDR: DE = row C below the window"},
        "3770": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "3773": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3775": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "3779": {"comment":"State 4"},
        "3782": {"synopsis":"The row's end: the line's last row?","comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3786": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "3790": {"comment":"The next row, from column 0"},
        "3793": {"comment":"Past the last row kept?"},
        "3799": {"synopsis":"The line's end: A = $0D, L = 8."},
        "3804": {"synopsis":"A = the character at column B of the row at DE, B moved on; carry. No carry when B is past\ncolumn 31.","comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3807": {"comment":"No carry when past"},
        "3809": {"comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "3813": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "3814": {"comment":"B moved on"},
        "3815": {"comment":"Carry: one read"},
        "3817": {"synopsis":"Copy lists for $2152 (a count, then the bytes): 1, $14 (EDIT_IN_MAIN), and at $0EEB 1, $01\n(EDIT_IN_LOWER), each put in $EC15."},
        "3819": {"synopsis":"1, $01: EDIT_IN_LOWER's $EC15."},
        "3821": {"synopsis":"Editing in the main screen: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared and $EC15, the window's last row, = 20\n(ROW_COUNT_MAIN through $2152).","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared"},
        "3826": {"comment":"$EC15 = 20"},
        "3835": {"synopsis":"Editing in the lower screen: TV_FLAG bit 0 set, the print position at row 0, column 0\n($191D), and $EC15, the window's last row, = 1 (ROW_COUNT_LOWER through $2152).","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 set"},
        "3843": {"comment":"Row 0, column 0"},
        "3846": {"comment":"$EC15 = 1"},
        "3855": {"synopsis":"Is column B of the row at DE in or next to text? Carry when the character at B is not 0, or\n(B not 0) the one before it is not 0, or one further right up to column 30 is not 0 (B moved\nto it; A = it).\nExit: no carry, B = 31, when the row is empty from there on.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "3860": {"comment":"A character at B?"},
        "3864": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "3868": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "3869": {"comment":"The column before"},
        "3871": {"comment":"A character before B?"},
        "3876": {"synopsis":"A character here?"},
        "3881": {"synopsis":"The next column, up to 30.","comment":"The next column"},
        "3884": {"comment":"Up to column 30"},
        "3889": {"synopsis":"Carry when column B of the row at DE holds a character; otherwise B moves left over 0s to\njust after the last character before it (carry), or to 0 when there is none (no carry).\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "3894": {"comment":"A character at B?"},
        "3898": {"synopsis":"A 0 here: one column left."},
        "3903": {"comment":"Column 0: none, no carry"},
        "3906": {"comment":"One column left"},
        "3910": {"synopsis":"Just after the character; carry."},
        "3913": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of column B in the row at DE, A = the character there.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "3917": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "3919": {"synopsis":"Inserts character A at the cursor (row C, column B), the rest of the line moving right\nacross its rows; nothing when $EC0D bit 0 is set (no carry).\n1. The character goes in at column B ($0577) and the row is redrawn ($16FE).\n2. The character pushed out of column 31, when not 0, goes on to the next row: when row C\nwas its line's last (flags bit 3 or 5 set) a blank row is inserted after it (INSERT_ROW,\nflags as row C's without bit 0, the first ($FD6B) columns cleared by $16EE) and taken at\ncolumn 0; otherwise at the start of the next row's text (TEXT_FROM_COL). Row C's flags\nlose bits 3 and 5 and get bit 1 (continued).\n3. Past the window's last row ($EC15) the character goes to $123C. Keeps BC.","comment":"HL = the editor's flags"},
        "3922": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "3923": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set: nothing"},
        "3926": {"comment":"The cursor kept"},
        "3927": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "3928": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3932": {"synopsis":"The character in at column B; the row redrawn.","comment":"In at column B; A = the character pushed out of column 31"},
        "3935": {"comment":"The character pushed out kept"},
        "3936": {"comment":"HL = the row, for $16FE"},
        "3937": {"comment":"The row redrawn"},
        "3941": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "3943": {"comment":"Nothing pushed out: done"},
        "3945": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3946": {"comment":"The next row, from column 0"},
        "3949": {"comment":"Past the window's last row?"},
        "3955": {"comment":"Row C's flags: bits 3 and 5 cleared; Z when they were clear"},
        "3961": {"comment":"A = the flags as they were"},
        "3962": {"comment":"Row C continued"},
        "3964": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "3965": {"comment":"DE = the next row"},
        "3969": {"comment":"Not the line's last row before: already continued"},
        "3971": {"comment":"New row's flags: not the first"},
        "3973": {"comment":"INSERT_ROW: a new row there"},
        "3976": {"comment":"Not inserted: done"},
        "3978": {"comment":"Its first columns cleared"},
        "3981": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "3982": {"comment":"Into the new row"},
        "3984": {"synopsis":"The row already continued: into the next row at its text's start.","comment":"TEXT_FROM_COL: B = where its text starts"},
        "3987": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "3988": {"comment":"Into that row"},
        "3990": {"synopsis":"Past the window's last row: $123C.","comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "3991": {"comment":"Into the rows below"},
        "3994": {"synopsis":"BC back."},
        "3996": {"synopsis":"Inserts a blank row at row C flagged as both the first and the last row of a line ($09,\nINSERT_ROW); DE = row C's address first.","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3999": {"comment":"Flags: first and last row"},
        "4001": {"synopsis":"Inserts BLANK_ROW at window row C ($0540, the rows from C down moving down) and gives it\nflags A.\nExit: carry when inserted. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "4003": {"comment":"B = the row"},
        "4004": {"comment":"HL = BLANK_ROW"},
        "4007": {"comment":"C = the flags"},
        "4009": {"comment":"The template inserted at row B"},
        "4013": {"comment":"A = the flags"},
        "4014": {"comment":"Not inserted?"},
        "4016": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "4017": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4020": {"comment":"The new row's flags"},
        "4025": {"comment":"Carry: inserted"},
        "4026": {"synopsis":"DE and BC back."},
        "4029": {"synopsis":"A blank editor row for INSERT_ROW: 32 columns of 0 (no character), flags $09 (the line's\nfirst and last row) and two 0 bytes."},
        "4064": {"synopsis":"Deletes the character at the cursor (row C, column B), the rest of the line moving left\nacross its rows:\n1. Down the continued rows (flags bit 1) to the line's last row; when the line runs on past\nthe window's last row ($EC15), $1297 gives the character to bring in from below,\notherwise 0 is brought in.\n2. From that row back up to row C each row moves one column left ($058C) from the start of\nits text (from column B on row C), taking the character in at column 31; the character\nmoved out at the left is carried to the row above.\n3. A row other than row C left without text is removed (REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW); the others are\nredrawn ($16FE).\nExit: carry. Keeps BC.","comment":"The cursor kept"},
        "4065": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4068": {"comment":"Its row and column kept"},
        "4069": {"synopsis":"Row C continued (flags bit 1)?"},
        "4073": {"comment":"Row C continued?"},
        "4075": {"comment":"A = 0: nothing to bring in"},
        "4079": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "4080": {"comment":"DE = it, 35 bytes on"},
        "4085": {"comment":"Past the window's last row?"},
        "4091": {"comment":"C = the window's last row"},
        "4092": {"comment":"A = the character from below"},
        "4095": {"synopsis":"H = column B, L = row C of the cursor."},
        "4096": {"synopsis":"One row: its start column (B on the cursor's row, the text's start on the others)."},
        "4097": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4101": {"comment":"B = the character to bring in"},
        "4102": {"comment":"The cursor's row?"},
        "4105": {"comment":"Z and A kept"},
        "4108": {"comment":"From column B"},
        "4111": {"synopsis":"A later row: from the start of its text.","comment":"Z and A kept"},
        "4113": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "4115": {"comment":"B = the start of the row's text"},
        "4120": {"synopsis":"$F6F4 bit 0 set on the cursor's row (Z on entry), cleared for a later row.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4121": {"comment":"$F6F4 bit 0 set (the cursor's row)"},
        "4126": {"comment":"A later row: bit 0 cleared"},
        "4130": {"synopsis":"The row moved left, A in at column 31.","comment":"Moved left from B, A in at 31; A = the one moved out"},
        "4133": {"comment":"The character taken out kept"},
        "4139": {"comment":"The cursor's row?"},
        "4143": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "4145": {"comment":"Text left on the row?"},
        "4150": {"comment":"None: the row removed"},
        "4153": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "4157": {"synopsis":"The row redrawn.","comment":"HL = the row, for $16FE"},
        "4159": {"comment":"The row redrawn"},
        "4162": {"synopsis":"The row above, with the character moved out.","comment":"A = the character taken out"},
        "4163": {"comment":"Up a row"},
        "4164": {"comment":"It goes into the row above at column 31"},
        "4165": {"comment":"H, L = the cursor's column and row"},
        "4166": {"comment":"Z: this was the cursor's row"},
        "4167": {"comment":"A = the character to bring in"},
        "4168": {"comment":"Until the cursor's row is done"},
        "4171": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "4172": {"comment":"The cursor back"},
        "4174": {"synopsis":"Removes window row C (at DE), which holds no text:\n1. When it is not its line's first row (flags bit 0), the row above (for row 0 the last of\nthe rows kept above the window: $FC9A moved by $1418, row ($F9DB) - 1 through $1385)\nloses flags bit 1 and takes row C's flags.\n2. A row taken from below the window (ROW_FROM_BELOW) and row C removed ($0513: the rows\nbelow it move up, the taken row at the bottom).\nExit: carry.","comment":"HL = row C's flags"},
        "4178": {"comment":"A = them"},
        "4179": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "4183": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "4184": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "4185": {"comment":"Row 0?"},
        "4189": {"comment":"The row kept again"},
        "4190": {"comment":"The rows kept above: their last row"},
        "4193": {"comment":"$1418: the line before it"},
        "4196": {"comment":"$FC9A = it"},
        "4199": {"comment":"C = the rows kept above, less 1: their last"},
        "4204": {"comment":"ABOVE_ROW_ADDR: DE = that row"},
        "4207": {"comment":"The row back"},
        "4210": {"synopsis":"Row C - 1.","comment":"Row C - 1"},
        "4211": {"comment":"DE = row C - 1"},
        "4214": {"synopsis":"The row above: bit 1 cleared, row C's flags added.","comment":"The row back"},
        "4215": {"comment":"A = row C's flags"},
        "4216": {"comment":"HL = the row above's flags"},
        "4220": {"comment":"Not continued; row C's flags taken"},
        "4224": {"synopsis":"Row C removed, a row from below at the bottom.","comment":"B = the row"},
        "4225": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4228": {"comment":"A row from below at HL"},
        "4231": {"comment":"Row C removed, the rows below up"},
        "4234": {"synopsis":"Key $B4 (the key table at $05E6): deletes left of the cursor: the spaces before it, then the\nword\nbefore them, stopping at the space before the word or at the line's start (AT_LINE_START).\nEach step is CURSOR_LEFT and LINE_DELETE_CHAR; the cursor then goes right past that space.\nThen DEL_KEY_END.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off"},
        "4237": {"synopsis":"At the line's start? Otherwise left one, deleted; a space: again.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4238": {"comment":"At the line's start?"},
        "4243": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "4246": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4247": {"comment":"Could not: DEL_KEY_END"},
        "4249": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "4252": {"comment":"It kept"},
        "4254": {"comment":"Deleted"},
        "4257": {"comment":"HL and A back"},
        "4259": {"comment":"A space? Again"},
        "4263": {"synopsis":"The word: left one; a space ends it, any other character is deleted.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4264": {"comment":"AT_LINE_START"},
        "4267": {"comment":"The line's start: done"},
        "4269": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "4272": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4273": {"comment":"Could not: DEL_KEY_END"},
        "4275": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "4278": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "4282": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "4283": {"comment":"LINE_DELETE_CHAR"},
        "4286": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4287": {"comment":"Again"},
        "4289": {"synopsis":"The space before the word: back right past it.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4290": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT: past the space"},
        "4293": {"synopsis":"HL back."},
        "4294": {"synopsis":"The end of a deleting key: $EEF5 bit 2 cleared and the window's rows 0 to ($EC15) redrawn\n($04D0), $EC0D bit 3 set (the line edited), the cursor stored and shown ($0AC3).\nExit: A = the cursor's column, flags as on entry.","comment":"A = the cursor's column"},
        "4295": {"comment":"Kept, with the flags"},
        "4297": {"comment":"Rows redrawn one at a time again"},
        "4302": {"comment":"A = ($EC15), the window's last row"},
        "4305": {"comment":"The cursor's row and column kept"},
        "4306": {"comment":"B = row 0, C = the last row"},
        "4309": {"comment":"Z: $04D0 only draws, the cursor is not moved"},
        "4310": {"comment":"Rows 0 to ($EC15) redrawn"},
        "4314": {"comment":"The line edited"},
        "4320": {"comment":"The cursor stored and shown"},
        "4323": {"comment":"A = the cursor's column, the flags as on entry"},
        "4325": {"synopsis":"Key $B3 (the key table at $05E6): deletes at the cursor (LINE_DELETE_CHAR) up to and\nincluding the next\nspace, then the spaces after it; stops at the line's end (a 0 at the cursor). Then\nDEL_KEY_END with carry.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off, row redraws held back"},
        "4328": {"synopsis":"A character at the cursor? Deleted; on to the first space.","comment":"A = the character at the cursor (CHAR_AT_ROW_COL)"},
        "4333": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "4335": {"comment":"Carry for DEL_KEY_END"},
        "4338": {"comment":"It is deleted (LINE_DELETE_CHAR); A kept for the test"},
        "4345": {"comment":"Not a space: on"},
        "4349": {"synopsis":"Spaces after it deleted.","comment":"A = the character now at the cursor"},
        "4352": {"comment":"Not a space: done"},
        "4357": {"comment":"The space deleted (LINE_DELETE_CHAR)"},
        "4362": {"comment":"On to the next character"},
        "4364": {"synopsis":"Key $B1 (the key table at $05E6): deletes everything before the cursor back to the start of\nits line:\non the line's later rows a place left (CURSOR_LEFT) and deleted at a time\n(LINE_DELETE_CHAR); on its first row the character before the cursor while column B is not 0\nand the character before it is not 0. Then DEL_KEY_END with carry.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off, row redraws held back"},
        "4367": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = the cursor's row (ROW_ADDRESS)"},
        "4371": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "4375": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "4379": {"comment":"One place left (CURSOR_LEFT)"},
        "4382": {"comment":"Could not move: done"},
        "4384": {"comment":"The character there deleted (LINE_DELETE_CHAR)"},
        "4388": {"comment":"Again, from the row test"},
        "4390": {"comment":"Not reached: the jump at $1124 goes to $110F"},
        "4391": {"synopsis":"First row: the characters before the cursor, back to the text's start."},
        "4392": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "4396": {"comment":"A = the character before the cursor (CHAR_AT_ROW_COL)"},
        "4401": {"comment":"A character before the cursor?"},
        "4405": {"comment":"One column back, and that character deleted"},
        "4409": {"comment":"Again"},
        "4411": {"synopsis":"HL back; carry; DEL_KEY_END."},
        "4412": {"synopsis":"Carry; DEL_KEY_END."},
        "4413": {"comment":"DEL_KEY_END: the window redrawn, the cursor shown"},
        "4416": {"synopsis":"Key $B0 (the key table at $05E6): deletes at the cursor (LINE_DELETE_CHAR) until a 0 is at\nthe cursor:\nthe rest of the line. Then DEL_KEY_END with carry.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off, row redraws held back"},
        "4419": {"synopsis":"A character at the cursor?","comment":"A = the character at the cursor (CHAR_AT_ROW_COL)"},
        "4422": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "4424": {"comment":"Carry for DEL_KEY_END"},
        "4427": {"comment":"It is deleted (LINE_DELETE_CHAR)"},
        "4432": {"comment":"Again"},
        "4434": {"synopsis":"The start of a deleting key: $EC0D bit 0 cleared, the cursor loaded and taken off the screen\n($0AB7), $EEF5 bit 2 set (rows are not redrawn one at a time while it is: $16FE), HL =\n$F6F1."},
        "4437": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared"},
        "4439": {"comment":"The cursor loaded, taken off"},
        "4445": {"comment":"No redraws one row at a time"},
        "4451": {"synopsis":"Is the cursor (row C, column B) at the start of its line's text? Z when row C is the line's\nfirst row (flags bit 0) and B is 0 or the character before column B is 0; otherwise NZ, A =\n1.","comment":"DE = row C (ROW_ADDRESS)"},
        "4454": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "4458": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "4465": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "4467": {"comment":"A = the character before column B (CHAR_AT_ROW_COL)"},
        "4474": {"comment":"A character before the cursor?"},
        "4476": {"synopsis":"NZ.","comment":"A = 1 and NZ: not at the start"},
        "4480": {"synopsis":"Z.","comment":"A = 0 and Z: at the start"},
        "4482": {"synopsis":"DE = the address of row C of the editor's window, the rows from $EC16, 35 bytes each: 32\ncolumns of characters (0 is no character), at +$20 the row's flags (bit 0 the line's first\nrow, bit 1 continued on the next row, bit 3 the line's last row), and two bytes at +$21 and\n+$22.\nExit: HL = $0023. Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"HL = the window's first row"},
        "4485": {"synopsis":"DE = HL + 35 * C: row C of the rows from HL ($1291 for $F6F8, $1385 for $F9DE).\nExit: HL = $0023. Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"AF kept"},
        "4486": {"comment":"A = the rows to step over"},
        "4487": {"comment":"DE = 35, the size of a row"},
        "4490": {"synopsis":"35 for each row.","comment":"Row 0 reached?"},
        "4493": {"comment":"One row on"},
        "4495": {"comment":"One fewer to go"},
        "4497": {"synopsis":"DE = the row.","comment":"DE = the row, HL = 35"},
        "4500": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of column B of window row C (ROW_ADDRESS). Keeps DE."},
        "4501": {"comment":"DE = row C (ROW_ADDRESS)"},
        "4504": {"comment":"HL = DE + B: the cell at column B"},
        "4510": {"synopsis":"A copy list for $2152 (a count, then the bytes): 5, then $00, $00, $00, $F8, $F6 for\n$F6F5-$F6F9 (BELOW_RESET)."},
        "4516": {"synopsis":"$F6F5-$F6F7 = 0 (no rows kept below the window) and $F6F8-$F6F9 = $F6F8 (BELOW_INIT_DATA\nthrough $2152).","comment":"HL = BELOW_INIT_DATA, the list"},
        "4519": {"comment":"DE = $F6F5, where it goes"},
        "4522": {"comment":"$2152 copies it"},
        "4525": {"synopsis":"Takes the next row from those kept below the window: with $F6F5 (their count) not 0, $EC0D\nbit 0 cleared and the 20 rows from $F6F8 + 35 moved down one row, so the first lands at\n$F6F8; with none kept, $142D, $1420 (on $F9D7, updated when it gives carry) and $13A4\nmake them first. $F6F5 = the count less one.\nExit: HL = $F6F8. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4527": {"comment":"HL = $F6F5, the count, kept for the end"},
        "4531": {"comment":"Rows kept below?"},
        "4536": {"comment":"None: made"},
        "4539": {"comment":"HL = $F9D7, the line number to start from"},
        "4545": {"comment":"No line after it: $F9D7 kept"},
        "4547": {"comment":"$F9D7 = the line found"},
        "4550": {"synopsis":"BC = the place; $13A4 on $F6F5.","comment":"BC = the line's number, for LINE_TO_ROWS"},
        "4552": {"comment":"HL = $F6F5"},
        "4553": {"comment":"LINE_TO_ROWS: the line's rows from $F6F8; A = the rows"},
        "4556": {"comment":"All but the one taken are kept"},
        "4557": {"comment":"To store the count"},
        "4559": {"synopsis":"Rows kept: shifted down one."},
        "4562": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared"},
        "4564": {"comment":"DE = $F6F8, HL = $F6F8 + 35"},
        "4573": {"comment":"20 rows down one"},
        "4578": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "4579": {"comment":"Carry: a row given"},
        "4580": {"synopsis":"The count stored; HL = $F6F8.","comment":"DE = $F6F5"},
        "4581": {"comment":"The count stored"},
        "4582": {"comment":"HL = the row taken: the first, at $F6F8"},
        "4588": {"synopsis":"Puts the editor row at DE (35 bytes: 32 cells, flags at +$20, line number at +$21, high byte\nfirst) in front of the rows kept below the screen ($F6F5 the count, the rows from $F6F8, 35\nbytes each, row 1 the nearest):\n1. When the row's flags have bits 0 and 4 set, $F9D7 = the number of the line before the\nrow's line ($1418; kept when there is none).\n2. When bit 0 is set, the buffer is emptied (count 0) and the row is not kept.\n3. Otherwise, with fewer than 20 rows ($14), the row is copied to $F6F8 and rows 0-19 moved\nto rows 1-20, so it becomes row 1; the count goes up by one.\nExit: HL = $F6F8; carry when the row was kept or the buffer emptied, no carry when the\nbuffer was full.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4590": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags"},
        "4594": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 4 both set?"},
        "4600": {"comment":"HL, DE kept"},
        "4602": {"comment":"DE = the row's line number"},
        "4607": {"comment":"Expansion reset"},
        "4611": {"comment":"The line before it"},
        "4616": {"comment":"Kept as $F9D7"},
        "4619": {"synopsis":"No line before: $F9D7 kept."},
        "4621": {"synopsis":"A line's first row (bit 0) empties the buffer.","comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "4623": {"comment":"HL = $F6F5, the count, kept for the end"},
        "4627": {"comment":"Not a first row: the row put in front"},
        "4629": {"comment":"Count 0"},
        "4632": {"comment":"To store the count"},
        "4634": {"synopsis":"The row put in front, when there is room.","comment":"A = the count"},
        "4635": {"comment":"20 rows already?"},
        "4639": {"comment":"The row copied to $F6F8"},
        "4648": {"comment":"Rows 0-19 moved one row on, from the end"},
        "4651": {"comment":"DE = the end of the rows, HL = 35 bytes before it"},
        "4659": {"comment":"20 rows, from the last byte back"},
        "4664": {"comment":"One more"},
        "4666": {"comment":"To store the count"},
        "4668": {"synopsis":"Carries character A, pushed off the end of the screen's last row (HL = that row's flags\nbyte), into the rows below the screen ($F6F5):\n1. B = column 0, C = row 1 (BELOW_ROW_ADDR). When the screen row's bit 3 was set, it is\ncleared and the row after it is found as in step 3.\n2. The character is put in at the row's first used column ($0F0F moves B over empty cells;\n$0577 inserts it, pushing the row's cells on). When nothing is pushed off the row's end,\nthe count becomes C and the row's bit 3 is set: done.\n3. The cell pushed off goes on to the next row (C + 1; at row 21, with a character in the\nprevious row's last cell, $EC0D bit 0 is set). The previous row gets bit 1 set and bit 3\ncleared; when its bit 1 was already set the next row is used as it is (step 2), otherwise\nrow C is made a new last row: cleared, flags 8, indented by $FD6B cells ($16EE).\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE and the character kept"},
        "4671": {"comment":"Column 0, row 1"},
        "4675": {"comment":"DE = row 1 below the screen (BELOW_ROW_ADDR)"},
        "4680": {"comment":"The screen row was a line's last?"},
        "4686": {"synopsis":"B moved over the row's empty cells ($0F0F).","comment":"B = the row's first column of text (TEXT_FROM_COL)"},
        "4689": {"comment":"A = the character carried"},
        "4690": {"synopsis":"A inserted at column B of row DE ($0577).","comment":"It goes in at column B ($0577); A = the one pushed out"},
        "4693": {"comment":"Nothing pushed off?"},
        "4695": {"comment":"The character pushed out kept"},
        "4696": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "4699": {"comment":"Past row 20?"},
        "4702": {"comment":"Within 20: on to the next row"},
        "4704": {"comment":"The last cell of the row before used?"},
        "4709": {"comment":"That cell empty: on to the next row"},
        "4712": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set"},
        "4718": {"synopsis":"The row before marked as continued (bit 1 set, bit 3 cleared); DE = row C.","comment":"Was the row before already continued?"},
        "4724": {"comment":"DE = row C below the screen (BELOW_ROW_ADDR)"},
        "4727": {"comment":"Yes: its next row exists"},
        "4729": {"comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4731": {"comment":"A new row: cleared, flags 8 (bit 3)"},
        "4738": {"comment":"Indented"},
        "4741": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "4742": {"comment":"It goes into the new row"},
        "4744": {"synopsis":"Nothing more pushed off: the count = C, bit 3 on row C's flags.","comment":"A = the rows used"},
        "4745": {"comment":"The count of rows kept below"},
        "4748": {"comment":"Row C is now the line's last"},
        "4753": {"synopsis":"DE = row C of the rows below the screen: $F6F8 + 35 x C ($1185).\nExit: HL = $0023. Keeps AF.","comment":"HL = the first row below the screen"},
        "4756": {"comment":"ROW_ADDRESS_HL does the rest"},
        "4759": {"synopsis":"Pulls the rows below the screen one character back, from the last row ($F6F5) up to row 1:\nin each row the character at its first used column is taken out and the one from the row\nbelow put in at column 31 ($058C). A row left with no text is dropped: the row before (the\nscreen's last row, line $EC15, for row 1) loses bit 1 and takes the dropped row's flags, and\nthe count goes down by one. $EC0D bit 0 is cleared first.\nExit: carry, A = the character taken from row 1 (0 when none); with no rows kept, A = 0 and\nno carry.\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4761": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared"},
        "4766": {"comment":"C = the count"},
        "4770": {"comment":"No rows kept below?"},
        "4771": {"comment":"A = 0, the character for the last row"},
        "4775": {"synopsis":"Row C: DE = its address; its first used column found ($0F0F).","comment":"DE = row C below the screen (BELOW_ROW_ADDR)"},
        "4778": {"comment":"The incoming character kept"},
        "4779": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "4781": {"comment":"No text in the row?"},
        "4786": {"comment":"A = the character for column 31"},
        "4787": {"comment":"A in at column 31, the cell at B taken out"},
        "4790": {"comment":"The character taken out kept, for the row above"},
        "4792": {"comment":"Any text left in the row?"},
        "4798": {"comment":"Text left: on to the row above"},
        "4800": {"synopsis":"An empty row: A = its flags, for the row before.","comment":"HL = the row's flags byte, past column 31"},
        "4802": {"comment":"The flags and BC kept"},
        "4804": {"comment":"Row 1?"},
        "4809": {"comment":"The row before: the screen's last row"},
        "4813": {"comment":"DE = the screen's last row (ROW_ADDRESS)"},
        "4818": {"synopsis":"The row before: row C - 1 of the buffer.","comment":"Row C - 1 of the rows below"},
        "4819": {"comment":"DE = that row (BELOW_ROW_ADDR)"},
        "4822": {"synopsis":"The row before: bit 1 cleared, the dropped row's flags added; the count one less.","comment":"BC and the dropped row's flags back"},
        "4824": {"comment":"HL = the row before's flags byte"},
        "4828": {"comment":"Not continued on the next row now"},
        "4830": {"comment":"The dropped row's flags added to it"},
        "4832": {"comment":"One row fewer kept below"},
        "4836": {"synopsis":"The row above, until row 1 is done.","comment":"A = the character taken out, for the row above"},
        "4837": {"comment":"The row above"},
        "4840": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "4841": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "4844": {"synopsis":"ABOVE_INIT's bytes for $2152: a count (3), then $00 for $F9DB and $F9DE for $F9DC."},
        "4848": {"synopsis":"Empties the stack of rows above the screen: $F9DB (the count) = 0 and $F9DC (the pointer\npast the top row) = $F9DE, copied from ABOVE_INIT_DATA through $2152.","comment":"HL = ABOVE_INIT_DATA, the list"},
        "4851": {"comment":"DE = $F9DB, where it goes"},
        "4854": {"comment":"$2152 copies it"},
        "4857": {"synopsis":"Takes the row nearest the screen off the stack of rows above it ($F9DB the count, $F9DC the\npointer past the top row, rows 35 bytes each from $F9DE):\n1. With rows on the stack, the pointer moves back 35 bytes and the count goes down by one:\nHL = that row.\n2. With none, the line before $FC9A ($1418, after $142D) is expanded into rows\nfrom $F9E1 (LINE_TO_ROWS) and $FC9A becomes its number. All its rows but the last stay on\nthe stack (count = rows - 1, pointer = the last row's address); HL = the last row.\nExit: carry and HL = the row; no carry when the stack was empty and there is no line before\n$FC9A.\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4859": {"comment":"HL = $F9DB, the count, kept for the end"},
        "4863": {"comment":"Rows on the stack?"},
        "4867": {"comment":"HL kept again"},
        "4868": {"comment":"$142D: the expansion reset"},
        "4871": {"comment":"The line before $FC9A"},
        "4879": {"comment":"Found: it is $FC9A now"},
        "4882": {"synopsis":"BC = the line found (or 0).","comment":"BC = the line's number, for LINE_TO_ROWS"},
        "4884": {"comment":"HL = $F9DB"},
        "4885": {"comment":"HL = $F9DE"},
        "4888": {"comment":"No line before: the pointer = $F9DE, the count kept"},
        "4890": {"comment":"Its rows from $F9E1"},
        "4893": {"comment":"All but the last kept"},
        "4894": {"comment":"HL = the line's last row: the one taken"},
        "4897": {"synopsis":"A row off the stack: the pointer back by 35 bytes.","comment":"HL = the pointer past the top row"},
        "4900": {"comment":"Back 35 bytes: HL = the row taken"},
        "4905": {"comment":"Carry: the count is stored"},
        "4906": {"comment":"One row fewer"},
        "4907": {"synopsis":"With carry: the count = A and the pointer = DE.\nExit: HL = DE.","comment":"DE = the new pointer"},
        "4908": {"comment":"HL = $F9DB"},
        "4909": {"comment":"No carry: the count left as it is"},
        "4911": {"comment":"The count"},
        "4912": {"synopsis":"The pointer = DE.","comment":"The pointer, at $F9DC"},
        "4916": {"comment":"HL = the row"},
        "4920": {"synopsis":"Puts the editor row at DE on the stack of rows above the screen ($F9DB):\n1. When the row's flags have bits 0 and 4 set, $FC9A = the row's line number.\n2. When bit 3 is set (the line's last row), the stack is emptied (count 0, pointer $F9DE)\nand $FC9A moves to the line after it ($1420, after $142D; 0 when none): the\nrow is not kept.\n3. Otherwise, with fewer than 20 rows ($14), the row is copied to the pointer, which moves\non 35 bytes, and the count goes up by one.\nExit: carry when the row was kept or the stack emptied; no carry when it was full.\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4922": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags"},
        "4926": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 4 both set?"},
        "4932": {"comment":"DE, HL kept"},
        "4938": {"comment":"$FC9A = the row's line number"},
        "4944": {"synopsis":"A line's last row (bit 3) empties the stack.","comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "4946": {"comment":"HL = $F9DB, kept for the end"},
        "4950": {"comment":"Not a last row: the row pushed"},
        "4952": {"comment":"HL kept again"},
        "4953": {"comment":"$142D: the expansion reset"},
        "4956": {"comment":"The line after $FC9A, or 0"},
        "4962": {"comment":"$FC9A = it"},
        "4965": {"comment":"HL = $F9DE"},
        "4969": {"comment":"Count 0, pointer $F9DE"},
        "4972": {"comment":"To store them"},
        "4974": {"synopsis":"The row copied on top, when there is room.","comment":"A = the count"},
        "4975": {"comment":"20 rows already?"},
        "4977": {"comment":"Full: the row not kept"},
        "4979": {"comment":"One more"},
        "4980": {"comment":"HL = the pointer: where the row goes"},
        "4986": {"comment":"The row copied on top"},
        "4989": {"comment":"DE = the new pointer"},
        "4990": {"comment":"Carry: the count and the pointer stored"},
        "4993": {"synopsis":"Full: the row is not kept."},
        "4997": {"synopsis":"DE = row C of the stack above the screen: $F9DE + 35 x C ($1185).\nExit: HL = $0023. Keeps AF.","comment":"HL = the stack's first row"},
        "5000": {"comment":"ROW_ADDRESS_HL does the rest"},
        "5003": {"synopsis":"LINE_TO_ROWS's table for $2166: a count (8), then a code and a routine for each:\n$0D $16C6, $01 $16D4, and $12, $13, $14, $15, $10, $11 $1428."},
        "5028": {"synopsis":"Writes the text of a program line into editor rows from HL + 3, the expansion being set up\nfor it ($152A or $15B0):\n1. The first row: its flags (+$20) = 1, its line number (+$21, high byte first) = BC; B =\ncolumn 0, C = 1 row.\n2. Each character from $1611 (none in Calculator mode, $EC0E = 4) is looked up in\nEXPAND_CODES: the colour codes $10-$15 lose their argument; $0D ends the line\n($16C6).\n3. Any other character goes in at column B ($16BF). In a full row (column 32) $13FF\nends it with flags XOR $12 and starts the next, indented by $FD6B cells ($16EE);\nwith 20 rows written the line is ended there instead, with $0D.\n4. When the text runs out, the line is ended with $0D, or with $01 ($16D4) when\nnothing at all was written.\nExit: HL = the first row, A = C = the number of rows, carry, DE = the last row.","comment":"DE = the first row"},
        "5033": {"comment":"The first row kept, for the exit"},
        "5034": {"comment":"Flags 1; the line number"},
        "5044": {"comment":"Row 1, column 0"},
        "5048": {"synopsis":"The next character, unless in Calculator mode.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "5050": {"comment":"Calculator mode?"},
        "5055": {"comment":"No: A = the line's next character ($1611)"},
        "5060": {"comment":"Got one?"},
        "5062": {"comment":"None: $0D, or $01 for an empty first row"},
        "5069": {"comment":"Still column 0?"},
        "5075": {"comment":"No: $0D"},
        "5077": {"synopsis":"The character looked up in EXPAND_CODES.","comment":"HL = EXPAND_CODES"},
        "5080": {"comment":"Its routine run, if A is a code ($2166)"},
        "5083": {"comment":"Line ended?"},
        "5085": {"comment":"Argument skipped?"},
        "5087": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "5088": {"comment":"Room in the row?"},
        "5091": {"comment":"Yes: it goes in"},
        "5093": {"comment":"A new row, flags XOR $12"},
        "5095": {"comment":"$13FF: this row ended, the next started"},
        "5098": {"comment":"Got a row: indented"},
        "5100": {"comment":"No room: the line ends"},
        "5105": {"synopsis":"The new row indented.","comment":"$16EE: the line's later rows start indented"},
        "5108": {"synopsis":"The character in at column B.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "5109": {"comment":"$16BF: in at column B, B + 1"},
        "5112": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5114": {"synopsis":"HL = the first row, A = the rows.","comment":"HL = the first row"},
        "5115": {"comment":"A = the rows written"},
        "5117": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "5119": {"synopsis":"Ends row DE (ROW_CLEAR_REST) with its flags XOR A and starts the next: C + 1, DE + 35, its\nflags 0.\nExit: carry; no carry (and nothing changed after the flags) when C was 20 or more.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "5120": {"comment":"ROW_CLEAR_REST: the row's rest cleared, HL = its flags"},
        "5123": {"comment":"The flags XOR A"},
        "5126": {"comment":"20 rows already?"},
        "5129": {"comment":"Yes: no carry, no new row"},
        "5130": {"comment":"One row more"},
        "5131": {"comment":"DE = the next row, 35 bytes on"},
        "5136": {"comment":"Its flags byte 0"},
        "5142": {"comment":"Carry: a new row"},
        "5144": {"synopsis":"PREV_LINE_START for the line before line HL.\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry and HL = 0 when there is\nnone.","comment":"PREV_LINE_START"},
        "5147": {"comment":"Found: carry, HL = its number"},
        "5148": {"comment":"None: HL = 0"},
        "5152": {"synopsis":"NEXT_LINE_START for the line after line HL (the first line for HL = 0).\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry and HL = 0 when there is\nnone.","comment":"NEXT_LINE_START"},
        "5155": {"comment":"Found: carry, HL = its number"},
        "5156": {"comment":"None: HL = 0"},
        "5160": {"synopsis":"EXPAND_CODES' routine for the colour codes $10-$15 (the word table at $138B): the argument\nafter the code read (EXPAND_NEXT) and dropped.\nExit: no carry, so LINE_TO_ROWS goes on; with nothing left, EXPAND_INIT and carry.","comment":"The argument (EXPAND_NEXT)"},
        "5163": {"comment":"Got one: no carry, LINE_TO_ROWS goes on"},
        "5165": {"synopsis":"Resets the expansion of a line ($FC9F, the place in the program, and $FCA1, the place in a\ntext, both 0) and copies the 232 bytes $1442-$1529 (KEYWORD_TEXT to WORD_FIND_END) to $FCAE\nin\nbank 7, where EXPAND_NEXT and the tokenizer call them: KEYWORD_TEXT runs at $FCAE,\nWORD_TO_BUFFER at $FD09, KEYWORD_FIND at $FD43, WORD_FIND at $FD5C.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No place in the program"},
        "5171": {"comment":"No text pending"},
        "5174": {"comment":"KEYWORD_TEXT and the rest, 232 bytes, to $FCAE"},
        "5186": {"synopsis":"Run at $FCAE: puts the text of keyword $A5 + A in the buffer at $FCA3 (WORD_TO_BUFFER).\nInterrupts off, ROM 3 and bank 7 paged in (port $7FFD = $17, port $1FFD = $5B67 with bit 2\nset); the search starts from the entry of ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE for $A5, $B5, $C5, $D5, $E5\nor\n$F5 ($0096, $00CF, $0100, $013E, $018B, $01D4) below A, then passes over the rest of A's\nstrings (each ends with bit 7 set).\nEntry: A = the keyword's code - $A5.","comment":"Interrupts off; A kept"},
        "5188": {"comment":"Bank 7, the ROM's low bit set"},
        "5195": {"comment":"The ROM's high bit set too: ROM 3"},
        "5205": {"comment":"A = the keyword's place after $A5"},
        "5206": {"comment":"Keyword $F5 or above?"},
        "5210": {"comment":"$E5-$F4?"},
        "5214": {"comment":"$D5-$E4?"},
        "5218": {"comment":"$C5-$D4?"},
        "5222": {"comment":"$B5-$C4?"},
        "5226": {"comment":"$A5-$B4: from RND's entry in ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE"},
        "5231": {"synopsis":"Keywords $B5-$C4.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $B5"},
        "5233": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $B5"},
        "5238": {"synopsis":"Keywords $C5-$D4.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $C5"},
        "5240": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $C5"},
        "5245": {"synopsis":"Keywords $D5-$E4.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $D5"},
        "5247": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $D5"},
        "5252": {"synopsis":"Keywords $E5-$F4.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $E5"},
        "5254": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $E5"},
        "5259": {"synopsis":"Keywords $F5-$FF.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $F5"},
        "5261": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $F5"},
        "5264": {"synopsis":"B = the strings to pass over.","comment":"B = the strings to pass over"},
        "5265": {"comment":"None to pass over?"},
        "5266": {"synopsis":"Any more to pass over?"},
        "5268": {"synopsis":"Up to the end of this string (bit 7).","comment":"A = the next byte of the string"},
        "5270": {"comment":"Bit 7: the string's last?"},
        "5274": {"comment":"One string fewer"},
        "5275": {"comment":"Any more?"},
        "5277": {"synopsis":"Run at $FD09 (and the end of KEYWORD_TEXT at $FCAE): copies the string at HL (ended by bit\n7)\nto $FCA3 for EXPAND_NEXT, $FCA1 = $FCA3. A space goes first unless $FC9E is not 0 ($FC9E is\ncleared); the last character loses bit 7 and $A0 (a space with bit 7) follows it. Then the\npaging from $5B5C and $5B67 is put back and interrupts are allowed again.\nExit: HL past the string.","comment":"DE = the buffer at $FCA3, and $FCA1 = it"},
        "5284": {"comment":"No space wanted ($FC9E not 0)?"},
        "5288": {"comment":"$FC9E = 0, the flags kept for the test"},
        "5293": {"comment":"Not 0: no space"},
        "5295": {"comment":"The leading space"},
        "5299": {"synopsis":"One character, up to the one with bit 7.","comment":"A = B = the next character"},
        "5302": {"comment":"To the buffer"},
        "5304": {"comment":"Bit 7: the last?"},
        "5308": {"comment":"The last without bit 7"},
        "5311": {"comment":"Over the last again"},
        "5314": {"comment":"Then $A0, a space with bit 7, ends the text"},
        "5317": {"comment":"The paging as it was: port $7FFD from $5B5C"},
        "5325": {"comment":"Port $1FFD from $5B67"},
        "5333": {"comment":"Interrupts allowed again"},
        "5335": {"synopsis":"Run at $FD43: looks the word at $FDA0 up in ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE from RND's entry ($0096;\nB = $A5, the code of its first keyword), with ROM 3 and bank 7 paged in and interrupts off;\nWORD_FIND does the rest.","comment":"Interrupts off; A kept"},
        "5337": {"comment":"Bank 7, the ROM's low bit set"},
        "5344": {"comment":"The ROM's high bit set too: ROM 3"},
        "5355": {"comment":"HL = RND's entry in ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE"},
        "5358": {"comment":"B = $A5, the code of the first keyword"},
        "5360": {"synopsis":"Run at $FD5C (and the end of KEYWORD_FIND): compares the word at $FDA0 (its last character\nwith bit 7 set) with each string at HL, B counting up from the code of the first, until B\npasses $FF. Lower-case letters in the word match capitals. Then the paging from $5B5C and\n$5B67 is put back and interrupts are allowed again.\nEntry: HL = the first string, B = its code.\nExit: carry and A = the code of the string that matched; no carry when none did.","comment":"DE = the word at $FDA0, for each string"},
        "5363": {"synopsis":"The word's next character, a letter as a capital.","comment":"A = the word's next character"},
        "5366": {"comment":"A lower-case letter?"},
        "5368": {"comment":"A again, bit 7 included"},
        "5369": {"comment":"Not lower case: as it is"},
        "5371": {"comment":"Made a capital"},
        "5373": {"synopsis":"The same as the string's?","comment":"The same as the string's?"},
        "5374": {"comment":"No: the next string"},
        "5376": {"comment":"Both on one character"},
        "5378": {"comment":"The last character?"},
        "5382": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "5383": {"comment":"Then A = the code, paging back"},
        "5385": {"synopsis":"No match: the next string's code; past $FF, none found.","comment":"The next string's code"},
        "5386": {"comment":"Past $FF: none found"},
        "5388": {"synopsis":"Past the end of this string.","comment":"Bit 7: the string's last?"},
        "5394": {"comment":"The word compared with the next string"},
        "5396": {"synopsis":"None found: no carry.","comment":"No carry"},
        "5397": {"synopsis":"A = B; the paging as it was.","comment":"D = the code found"},
        "5399": {"comment":"The paging as it was: port $7FFD from $5B5C"},
        "5407": {"comment":"Port $1FFD from $5B67"},
        "5415": {"comment":"A = the code"},
        "5416": {"comment":"Interrupts allowed again"},
        "5418": {"synopsis":"Sets up the expansion of the first program line numbered above HL (HL = 0: the first line;\n$FC9E = A) for EXPAND_NEXT: LINE_FIND in bank 0, then LINE_START_SET.\nExit: carry, HL = the line's number, DE = the address of its text; no carry when there is\nnone. Bank 7 paged in again.","comment":"EXPAND_CLEAR: nothing pending"},
        "5421": {"comment":"$FC9E = A"},
        "5425": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0, to read the program"},
        "5428": {"comment":"LINE_FIND: the first line HL or above"},
        "5431": {"comment":"Past the end?"},
        "5433": {"comment":"A line numbered above HL?"},
        "5435": {"comment":"HL = 0: this line"},
        "5439": {"comment":"Equal: the next line"},
        "5442": {"comment":"A line there (LINE_IN_PROG)?"},
        "5445": {"comment":"Past the end: none"},
        "5447": {"synopsis":"For the line at HL: its number as four characters at $FCA3 (LINE_NUM_DIGIT; leading zeros\nas 0 bytes, the last with bit 7 set), $FCA1 = $FCA3 and $FC9F = the address of its text.\nExit: carry, HL = the number, DE = the text.","comment":"DE = its number"},
        "5450": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 again"},
        "5453": {"comment":"DE, HL, IX kept"},
        "5457": {"comment":"IX = $FCA3, also $FCA1"},
        "5465": {"comment":"HL = the line's number"},
        "5466": {"comment":"No digit yet"},
        "5468": {"comment":"Thousands (DE = -1000)"},
        "5474": {"comment":"Hundreds (DE = -100)"},
        "5480": {"comment":"Tens (DE = -10)"},
        "5486": {"comment":"Units (DE = -1)"},
        "5492": {"comment":"Bit 7 on the last digit"},
        "5502": {"comment":"IX, HL, DE back"},
        "5506": {"comment":"$FC9F = the line's text"},
        "5512": {"comment":"HL = the number, DE = the text"},
        "5513": {"comment":"Carry: set up"},
        "5515": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 again; the flags as they are.","comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 again"},
        "5519": {"synopsis":"One decimal digit of HL into (IX), DE being minus its place's value (-1000, -100, -10, -1):\na 0 before any other digit (B = 0) is stored as the byte 0; B = 1 once a digit is not 0.\nExit: HL = the remainder, IX + 1.","comment":"A counts the place's value"},
        "5520": {"synopsis":"DE added while it fits; A counts.","comment":"The place's value taken off"},
        "5521": {"comment":"One more"},
        "5522": {"comment":"Not below 0 yet?"},
        "5524": {"comment":"The last one put back"},
        "5526": {"comment":"A = the digit's value"},
        "5527": {"comment":"The digit"},
        "5532": {"comment":"A 0?"},
        "5536": {"comment":"Any digit before it?"},
        "5540": {"comment":"A leading 0: the byte 0"},
        "5547": {"synopsis":"B = 1: zeros from now on are digits.","comment":"Zeros are digits from now on"},
        "5549": {"synopsis":"The next place.","comment":"The next place"},
        "5552": {"synopsis":"As NEXT_LINE_START, for the last program line numbered below HL. No carry when there is\nnone,\nand also when no line is numbered HL or above.","comment":"EXPAND_CLEAR: nothing pending"},
        "5555": {"comment":"$FC9E = A"},
        "5559": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0, to read the program"},
        "5562": {"comment":"LINE_FIND: DE = the line before the one found"},
        "5565": {"comment":"No line HL or above?"},
        "5567": {"comment":"HL = the line before it"},
        "5568": {"comment":"A line before it?"},
        "5571": {"comment":"Yes: its number and text set up"},
        "5574": {"comment":"None: no carry"},
        "5577": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of the line after the line at HL (its length added to its start + 4), DE =\nthe line at HL.","comment":"This line kept"},
        "5578": {"comment":"DE = the line's length"},
        "5583": {"comment":"Past the length bytes"},
        "5584": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "5585": {"comment":"DE = this line"},
        "5587": {"synopsis":"Is HL on a line? Carry when the byte there has bits 6 and 7 clear (a line number's high\nbyte, not the end of the program).","comment":"Bits 6 and 7 clear?"},
        "5590": {"comment":"Yes: carry, a line"},
        "5592": {"comment":"No: the program's end"},
        "5594": {"synopsis":"Compares the line number at HL (high byte first) with BC.\nExit: carry and Z when equal, carry and NZ when the line's is higher, no carry when it is\nlower. Keeps HL.","comment":"High bytes the same?"},
        "5596": {"comment":"No: carry when the line's is higher"},
        "5597": {"comment":"Low bytes the same?"},
        "5601": {"comment":"No: carry when the line's is higher"},
        "5602": {"comment":"Equal: carry and Z"},
        "5604": {"synopsis":"$FCA1 and $FC9F = 0: nothing to expand. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "5605": {"comment":"Nothing pending, nothing of a line left"},
        "5616": {"synopsis":"Finds the first program line (from PROG) numbered HL or above; the program must be paged in.\nExit: carry, HL = that line, DE = the line before it (0 for none), Z when its number is HL;\nno\ncarry when there is none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = the number sought"},
        "5618": {"comment":"DE = 0: no line before"},
        "5621": {"comment":"HL = PROG, the first line"},
        "5624": {"comment":"No lines at all?"},
        "5628": {"comment":"The first already HL or above?"},
        "5632": {"comment":"Seeking line 0?"},
        "5636": {"synopsis":"The next line, until the end or one numbered HL or above.","comment":"The next line (LINE_NEXT_ADDR), DE = this one"},
        "5639": {"comment":"The program's end?"},
        "5643": {"comment":"Numbered HL or above?"},
        "5646": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5649": {"synopsis":"The next character of the program line being expanded (set up by NEXT_LINE_START or\nPREV_LINE_START):\n1. While a text is pending at $FCA1 (the line number, a keyword's text), its next character,\nwithout bit 7; the one with bit 7 ends the text. $FC9E = $FF after the space ($A0) that\nends a keyword, else 0.\n2. Otherwise the next byte of the line at $FC9F (bank 0): the five-byte form of a number\nafter $0E is passed over. A keyword ($A5 up) puts its text at $FCA3 (KEYWORD_TEXT at\n$FCAE); $A3 and $A4 put \"SPECTRUM\" and \"PLAY\" there (WORD_TO_BUFFER at $FD09); and the\ntext's first character is taken. Any other byte is returned as it is, with $FC9E = 0;\n$0D, the line's end, also ends the expansion (both pointers 0).\nExit: carry and A = the character; no carry when nothing is left.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A text pending?"},
        "5656": {"comment":"A = the text's next character"},
        "5658": {"comment":"The space that ends a keyword?"},
        "5660": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "5665": {"comment":"$FF after the space that ends a keyword"},
        "5667": {"synopsis":"$FC9E = 0, or $FF after a keyword's last space.","comment":"$FC9E = 0 or $FF"},
        "5670": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "5671": {"comment":"The text's last character?"},
        "5675": {"comment":"The last: nothing pending after it"},
        "5678": {"synopsis":"$FCA1 = the next character, or 0 after the last.","comment":"$FCA1 = the next character or 0"},
        "5681": {"comment":"Without bit 7"},
        "5683": {"comment":"Carry: a character"},
        "5686": {"synopsis":"Nothing pending: the next byte of the line, if any.","comment":"Anything left in the line?"},
        "5691": {"comment":"Nothing: no carry"},
        "5694": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0"},
        "5697": {"synopsis":"A = the byte; a number's hidden form passed over.","comment":"A = the line's next byte"},
        "5698": {"comment":"A number's marker?"},
        "5702": {"comment":"Past the marker and the number's 5 bytes"},
        "5708": {"comment":"Then the next byte"},
        "5710": {"synopsis":"Bank 7; $FC9F on.","comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 again"},
        "5713": {"comment":"$FC9F = the next byte"},
        "5717": {"comment":"A 48K keyword?"},
        "5719": {"comment":"No"},
        "5721": {"comment":"A = the keyword's place after $A5"},
        "5723": {"comment":"KEYWORD_TEXT at $FCAE: its text to $FCA3"},
        "5726": {"comment":"Then its first character"},
        "5729": {"synopsis":"$A3 (SPECTRUM) and $A4 (PLAY): their text from OWN_WORDS.","comment":"$A3 or $A4?"},
        "5731": {"comment":"Below $A3: a character"},
        "5733": {"comment":"$A4: PLAY"},
        "5735": {"comment":"HL = \"SPECTRUM\" in OWN_WORDS"},
        "5740": {"synopsis":"$A4: \"PLAY\".","comment":"HL = \"PLAY\" in OWN_WORDS"},
        "5743": {"synopsis":"The text to $FCA3, then its first character.","comment":"WORD_TO_BUFFER at $FD09: the text to $FCA3"},
        "5746": {"comment":"Then its first character"},
        "5749": {"synopsis":"Any other character: $FC9E = 0; $0D ends the expansion.","comment":"$FC9E = 0, A kept"},
        "5756": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "5758": {"comment":"No: the character"},
        "5760": {"comment":"Yes: nothing pending, the line done"},
        "5769": {"synopsis":"Carry: A is a character.","comment":"Carry: A is a character"},
        "5771": {"synopsis":"No carry: nothing left.","comment":"No carry: nothing left"},
        "5774": {"synopsis":"Seven words, each with bit 7 set on its last character, for WORD_FIND (from $211F, B = $F9\nfor the first): \"SPECTRUM\", \"PLAY\", \"GOTO\", \"GOSUB\", \"DEFFN\", \"OPEN#\", \"CLOSE#\". EXPAND_NEXT\nalso prints the first two as the texts of $A3 and $A4."},
        "5811": {"synopsis":"ROW_SETUP's bytes for COPY_COUNTED: a count (2), then 1 for $FD96 and 5 for $FD97."},
        "5814": {"synopsis":"$FD96 = 1 and $FD97 = 5 (the cells a line's later rows are indented by, ROW_INDENT), copied\nfrom ROW_SETUP_DATA by COPY_COUNTED ($2152).","comment":"HL = ROW_SETUP_DATA"},
        "5817": {"comment":"DE = $FD96"},
        "5820": {"comment":"Copied (COPY_COUNTED)"},
        "5823": {"synopsis":"Puts A in column B of row DE; B + 1.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = the cell at column B"},
        "5827": {"comment":"A in it"},
        "5828": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "5830": {"synopsis":"EXPAND_CODES' routine for $0D (the word table at $138B): the rest of row DE cleared\n(ROW_CLEAR_REST), its flags' bits 3 and 4 set, $FD96 bit 0 set.\nExit: carry, which ends LINE_TO_ROWS.","comment":"ROW_CLEAR_REST: the row's rest cleared, HL = its flags"},
        "5833": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4 set"},
        "5837": {"comment":"$FD96 bit 0 set"},
        "5842": {"comment":"Carry: the line has ended"},
        "5844": {"synopsis":"EXPAND_CODES' routine for $01 (a line with no text; the word table at $138B): as\nROW_END_LINE, setting only bit 3 of the flags.","comment":"ROW_CLEAR_REST: the row's rest cleared, HL = its flags"},
        "5847": {"comment":"Bit 3: the line's last row"},
        "5849": {"comment":"$FD96 bit 0 set"},
        "5854": {"comment":"Carry: the line has ended"},
        "5856": {"synopsis":"Clears row DE's cells from column B to 31 (to 0).\nExit: B = 32, HL = the row's flags byte.","comment":"HL = the cell at column B"},
        "5860": {"comment":"A = 32, the column past the last"},
        "5862": {"synopsis":"Up to column 32.","comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "5864": {"comment":"The cell cleared"},
        "5866": {"comment":"The next"},
        "5870": {"synopsis":"Clears row DE's first ($FD97) cells.\nExit: B = ($FD97), the column after them.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A = the indent, from $FD97"},
        "5873": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "5875": {"synopsis":"One cell.","comment":"HL = the cell"},
        "5879": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "5881": {"comment":"The next"},
        "5882": {"comment":"More?"},
        "5886": {"synopsis":"Prints the row at HL on window line C (PRINT_ROW with B = C), unless $EEF5 bit 2 is set.\nKeeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "5890": {"comment":"Output held back ($EEF5 bit 2)?"},
        "5898": {"comment":"B = the line"},
        "5899": {"comment":"PRINT_ROW: the row printed"},
        "5902": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back.","comment":"BC, DE, HL back"},
        "5906": {"synopsis":"Unless $EEF5 bit 2 is set: SCROLL_UP with E = C, which moves window lines B + 1 to C one\nline\nup and prints the row at HL on line C. Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "5910": {"comment":"Output held back ($EEF5 bit 2)?"},
        "5918": {"comment":"E = the last line"},
        "5919": {"comment":"SCROLL_UP: the lines moved up, the row printed"},
        "5922": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back.","comment":"BC, DE, HL back"},
        "5926": {"synopsis":"Unless $EEF5 bit 2 is set: SCROLL_DOWN with E = C, which moves window lines B to C - 1 one\nline down and prints the row at HL on line B. Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "5930": {"comment":"Output held back ($EEF5 bit 2)?"},
        "5938": {"comment":"E = the last line"},
        "5939": {"comment":"SCROLL_DOWN: the lines moved down, the row printed"},
        "5942": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back.","comment":"BC, DE, HL back"},
        "5946": {"synopsis":"Marks the cell at column B, line C: WIN_CURSOR_ON (B and C swapped for it) keeps the cell's\nattribute in (IX+7) and gives it (IX+6)'s colours with its FLASH and BRIGHT bits inverted.\nKeeps all registers.","comment":"All registers kept"},
        "5950": {"comment":"B = the line, C = the column"},
        "5953": {"comment":"WIN_CURSOR_ON"},
        "5956": {"comment":"All registers back"},
        "5961": {"synopsis":"Puts back the attribute CELL_CURSOR_ON kept for the cell at column B, line C\n(WIN_CURSOR_OFF). Keeps all registers.","comment":"All registers kept"},
        "5965": {"comment":"B = the line, C = the column"},
        "5968": {"comment":"WIN_CURSOR_OFF"},
        "5971": {"comment":"All registers back"},
        "5976": {"synopsis":"MODE ($5C41) = 0, REPPER = 2, then KEY_MODE.","comment":"MODE = 0"},
        "5981": {"comment":"REPPER = 2"},
        "5986": {"comment":"KEY_MODE"},
        "5990": {"synopsis":"244 bytes no code in this ROM reads (KEY_DEFAULTS returns just before them; KEY_MODE\nfollows). The low 7 bits of each byte XOR $30 are ASCII; bit 7 is set on many bytes in no\npattern that matters to the text. Decoded, lines ended by $0D credit the ROM's authors,\nthank\nothers, and say it was written on Amstrad PCWs with M80 and L80 under CP/M+."},
        "6234": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bits 2 and 3 set; $5B66 bit 0 set when $EC0D bit 4 is set, else cleared.","comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6237": {"comment":"Bits 2 and 3 set"},
        "6241": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 4 set?"},
        "6246": {"comment":"HL = $5B66"},
        "6249": {"comment":"Yes: bit 0 set"},
        "6251": {"comment":"No: bit 0 cleared"},
        "6254": {"synopsis":"$5B66 bit 0 set.","comment":"Bit 0 set"},
        "6257": {"synopsis":"Waits for a new key (FLAGS bit 5), takes it from LAST_K (MODE bit 0 cleared): codes $20 and\nup, and $06-$0F after ROM 3's KI_CAPS_LOCK accepts them (KEY_CONTROL); $00-$05 and $10-$1F\nare ignored.\nExit: A = the key. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "6258": {"synopsis":"HL = FLAGS, for the next key.","comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6261": {"synopsis":"Until FLAGS bit 5 says a key came.","comment":"A new key?"},
        "6265": {"comment":"It is taken"},
        "6267": {"comment":"A = LAST_K"},
        "6270": {"comment":"MODE bit 0 cleared"},
        "6275": {"comment":"$20 and up: a key"},
        "6279": {"comment":"$10-$1F: ignored"},
        "6283": {"comment":"Below $06: ignored"},
        "6287": {"comment":"KEY_CONTROL: ROM 3's KI_CAPS_LOCK on it"},
        "6290": {"comment":"Not taken: wait again"},
        "6292": {"synopsis":"HL back; A = the key.","comment":"HL back; A = the key"},
        "6294": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's KI_CAPS_LOCK on the key in A.","comment":"ROM 3's KI_CAPS_LOCK: CAPS LOCK or a mode key handled"},
        "6298": {"synopsis":"Draws the menu whose text is at HL (a count, a title ended by $FF, items ended by bit 7):\n1. The area under it saved (MENU_AREA_SAVE); printing to the main screen.\n2. MENU_HEADER_TEXT and the title (PRINT_FF_TEXT), the stripes (DRAW_STRIPES) and\nMENU_AFTER_TITLE.\n3. The items from AT 8,7, one a line (MENU_ITEM).\n4. A border plotted down the left, along the bottom and up the right (PLOT_LINE).\n5. The bar on item 0 (MENU_BAR).","comment":"The menu's text kept"},
        "6299": {"comment":"MENU_AREA_SAVE: what the menu covers saved"},
        "6302": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared: printing to the main screen"},
        "6307": {"comment":"HL = the menu's text"},
        "6308": {"comment":"E = the count"},
        "6310": {"comment":"The header's place and colours (MENU_HEADER_TEXT)"},
        "6317": {"comment":"The title (PRINT_FF_TEXT)"},
        "6321": {"comment":"HL kept; DRAW_STRIPES: the title's stripes"},
        "6325": {"comment":"PAPER 0, a space, PAPER 7, INK 0 after the stripes"},
        "6331": {"comment":"HL = the items"},
        "6332": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "6333": {"comment":"AT line 8, column 7"},
        "6339": {"synopsis":"One item at the print position: a space, then up to 12 characters.","comment":"The line kept"},
        "6340": {"comment":"B = 12 characters at most"},
        "6342": {"comment":"A space first"},
        "6345": {"synopsis":"The next character; the one with bit 7 is the last.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6347": {"comment":"Bit 7: the item's last?"},
        "6351": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "6354": {"synopsis":"The last character without bit 7.","comment":"Without bit 7, printed"},
        "6357": {"synopsis":"Spaces to the width.","comment":"A space, B times: the line is 14 cells wide"},
        "6362": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "6364": {"comment":"AT the next line"},
        "6367": {"comment":"Items left?"},
        "6370": {"comment":"H = 111, L = 56: the border's corner"},
        "6373": {"comment":"E = the count"},
        "6374": {"comment":"Times 8: the height in pixels"},
        "6380": {"comment":"D = the height - 1"},
        "6382": {"comment":"E = 111, the width"},
        "6384": {"comment":"The left side: y - 1 each, D pixels down"},
        "6391": {"comment":"The bottom: x + 1 each, E pixels across"},
        "6398": {"comment":"The right side: y + 1 each, D + 1 pixels up"},
        "6406": {"comment":"The bar on item 0"},
        "6411": {"synopsis":"Plots A pixels from H (y), L (x), stepping by BC (B to H, C to L) each time: ROM 3's\nPLOT_SUB entered at $22E9, past its COORDS store. Keeps all registers but HL, AF.","comment":"AF, HL, DE, BC kept"},
        "6415": {"comment":"B = y (H), C = x (L)"},
        "6417": {"comment":"ROM 3's PLOT_SUB past its COORDS store: pixel C, B"},
        "6420": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6424": {"comment":"H, L one step on"},
        "6425": {"comment":"More?"},
        "6429": {"synopsis":"AT B, C through RST $10.","comment":"AT"},
        "6432": {"comment":"Line B"},
        "6434": {"comment":"Column C"},
        "6437": {"synopsis":"Prints the characters at HL through RST $10, up to the $FF that ends them. A '+' followed by\n'3' is printed as \"+2A\", the '3' and the character after it dropped, unless $5B66 bit 4 is\nset.\nExit: HL past the $FF.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6439": {"comment":"$FF: the end?"},
        "6442": {"comment":"A '+'?"},
        "6446": {"synopsis":"A printed; the next.","comment":"Printed"},
        "6447": {"comment":"The next"},
        "6449": {"synopsis":"A '+': is a '3' next?","comment":"A '3' after the '+'?"},
        "6452": {"comment":"A = '+' (the flags kept)"},
        "6454": {"comment":"No: the '+' printed as it is"},
        "6456": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 4 set?"},
        "6463": {"comment":"Yes: the '+' printed, then the '3'"},
        "6465": {"comment":"No: past the '3' and the character after it"},
        "6467": {"comment":"'+'"},
        "6470": {"comment":"'2'"},
        "6473": {"comment":"Then 'A', printed at PRINT_FF_CHAR"},
        "6477": {"synopsis":"Saves TV_FLAG, COORDS onwards (20 bytes) and the screen and attributes where the menu goes\nto\n$EEF6 on; MENU_AREA_BACK puts them back.","comment":"Carry: saving"},
        "6478": {"comment":"To MENU_AREA_COPY"},
        "6480": {"synopsis":"MENU_AREA_SAVE the other way: back from $EEF6 (from $07D1).","comment":"No carry: putting back"},
        "6481": {"synopsis":"The copy, from the menu's area to $EEF6 with carry, the other way without: DE is kept as the\nplace in $EEF6.","comment":"DE = the store at $EEF6, HL = TV_FLAG"},
        "6487": {"comment":"Saving: from TV_FLAG to the store"},
        "6489": {"comment":"Putting back: the other way"},
        "6490": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG.","comment":"TV_FLAG copied"},
        "6492": {"comment":"DE = the store's place again"},
        "6495": {"synopsis":"HL = COORDS ($5C7D).","comment":"HL = COORDS"},
        "6498": {"comment":"Putting back: swapped"},
        "6501": {"synopsis":"20 bytes from COORDS.","comment":"20 bytes copied"},
        "6506": {"comment":"DE = the store's place again"},
        "6509": {"synopsis":"The screen: 12 lines from line 7, columns 7-20; the direction kept in F'.","comment":"The direction kept in F'"},
        "6510": {"comment":"Line 7, column 7"},
        "6513": {"comment":"POSN_TO_ROM3: line and column in ROM 3's form"},
        "6516": {"comment":"Plus the window's top line"},
        "6521": {"comment":"12 lines"},
        "6523": {"synopsis":"One line: its display address (ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR) + 7.","comment":"Line, count and place kept"},
        "6526": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: HL = the line's display address"},
        "6529": {"comment":"Plus 7: column 7"},
        "6533": {"comment":"DE = the store's place"},
        "6534": {"comment":"MENU_LINE_COPY: the line's 8 pixel rows and attributes"},
        "6537": {"comment":"Count and line back"},
        "6539": {"comment":"The next line down"},
        "6540": {"comment":"More?"},
        "6544": {"synopsis":"Eight pixel rows of 14 bytes, then the line's 14 attributes (ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR),\nbetween\nHL and DE as F' carry says.","comment":"B = 8 pixel rows, C = 14 bytes in each"},
        "6547": {"synopsis":"One pixel row.","comment":"The row count kept, BC = 14"},
        "6550": {"comment":"The row's start kept"},
        "6551": {"comment":"The direction from F'"},
        "6552": {"comment":"Saving: from the screen"},
        "6554": {"comment":"Putting back: to the screen"},
        "6555": {"synopsis":"14 bytes.","comment":"14 bytes"},
        "6557": {"comment":"The pair as it was"},
        "6560": {"synopsis":"The next pixel row down.","comment":"The direction back in F'"},
        "6561": {"comment":"HL = the next pixel row (H + 1)"},
        "6563": {"comment":"Rows left?"},
        "6566": {"comment":"BC = 14 and the store's place kept"},
        "6568": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR: the line's attributes"},
        "6571": {"comment":"HL = the attributes' address"},
        "6572": {"comment":"DE = the store's place, BC = 14"},
        "6574": {"comment":"The direction from F'"},
        "6575": {"comment":"Saving: from the attributes"},
        "6577": {"comment":"Putting back: to them"},
        "6578": {"synopsis":"14 attributes.","comment":"14 attributes"},
        "6580": {"comment":"The pair as it was"},
        "6583": {"synopsis":"The direction back in F'.","comment":"The direction back in F'"},
        "6585": {"synopsis":"Moves the menu's bar from item A to the one above it, from item 0 to the last ((HL) - 2, HL\nbeing the menu's text, whose first byte is DRAW_MENU's count).\nExit: A = the new item, carry.","comment":"The bar off item A"},
        "6588": {"comment":"The item above"},
        "6589": {"comment":"Not above item 0?"},
        "6592": {"comment":"Above it: the last item, (HL) - 2"},
        "6595": {"synopsis":"The bar on item A.","comment":"The bar on item A"},
        "6598": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "6600": {"synopsis":"Moves the menu's bar from item A to the one below it, from the last ((HL) - 2) to item 0.\nExit: A = the new item. Keeps DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "6601": {"comment":"The bar off item A"},
        "6604": {"comment":"The item below"},
        "6605": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "6606": {"comment":"A = the last item, (HL) - 2"},
        "6609": {"comment":"Past it?"},
        "6610": {"comment":"A = the item below"},
        "6611": {"comment":"Not past the last: kept"},
        "6614": {"comment":"Past it: item 0"},
        "6615": {"synopsis":"The bar on item A.","comment":"The bar on item A"},
        "6618": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "6620": {"synopsis":"Flips the menu's bar on or off at item A: the 14 attribute cells of row $5907 + 32 x A\nbecome $68 when they are $78, otherwise $78. Keeps all registers.","comment":"AF, HL, DE kept"},
        "6623": {"comment":"HL = item 0's bar: line 8, column 7"},
        "6626": {"comment":"DE = 32, an attribute line"},
        "6629": {"comment":"Item 0?"},
        "6632": {"synopsis":"One attribute line per item.","comment":"Down a line"},
        "6633": {"comment":"For each item"},
        "6636": {"synopsis":"$68 (cyan paper) where it is $78 (white paper), else $78.","comment":"White paper ($78)?"},
        "6641": {"comment":"Yes: cyan paper ($68)"},
        "6643": {"synopsis":"14 cells.","comment":"14 cells"},
        "6645": {"synopsis":"One cell.","comment":"The cell"},
        "6647": {"comment":"More?"},
        "6650": {"comment":"DE, HL, AF back"},
        "6654": {"synopsis":"DRAW_MENU's and TITLE_BAR's header, ended by $FF (PRINT_FF_TEXT): AT 7,7; OVER 0; INVERSE 0;\nINK 7; PAPER 0; BRIGHT 1."},
        "6668": {"synopsis":"Printed after a menu's stripes, ended by $FF: PAPER 0, a space, PAPER 7, INK 0."},
        "6676": {"synopsis":"DRAW_STRIPES' two character pictures, 8 bytes each, copied to $5B7C: a triangle filling the\nlower right of the cell (01 03 07 ... FF) and its complement (FE FC ... 00)."},
        "6692": {"synopsis":"The stripes, ended by $FF, printed with codes $20 and $21 as STRIPE_GLYPHS' pictures:\nINK 2, ' ', PAPER 6, '!', INK 4, ' ', PAPER 5, '!', INK 0, ' '."},
        "6708": {"synopsis":"Draws the coloured stripes after a title: STRIPE_GLYPHS copied to $5B7C and STRIPE_TEXT\nprinted with CHARS = $5A7C, so that codes $20 and $21 are those pictures; CHARS back.\nKeeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE and HL kept"},
        "6711": {"comment":"The two diagonal pictures (STRIPE_GLYPHS) to $5B7C"},
        "6722": {"comment":"CHARS kept"},
        "6726": {"comment":"CHARS = $5A7C: codes $20 and $21 are the pictures at $5B7C"},
        "6732": {"comment":"The stripes (STRIPE_TEXT, PRINT_FF_TEXT)"},
        "6738": {"comment":"CHARS back"},
        "6742": {"comment":"HL, DE and BC back"},
        "6746": {"synopsis":"The bottom title bar with \"+3 BASIC\" ($080F): on at TITLE_BAR.","comment":"HL = \"+3 BASIC\" at $080F"},
        "6751": {"synopsis":"The bottom title bar with \"Calculator\" ($0817).","comment":"HL = \"Calculator\" at $0817"},
        "6756": {"synopsis":"The bottom title bar with \"Loader\" ($0809).","comment":"HL = \"Loader\" at $0809"},
        "6759": {"synopsis":"Draws the title bar on line 21 with the text at HL (ended by bit 7): lines 21 to 23 cleared\n(CLEAR_LOW_3), line 21's attributes $40, MENU_HEADER_TEXT's colours, the text at AT 21,0\n(PRINT_BIT7_TEXT, $029E), then the stripes at AT 21,26 (DRAW_STRIPES).","comment":"The text kept"},
        "6760": {"comment":"CLEAR_LOW_3: lines 21 to 23 cleared"},
        "6763": {"comment":"Line 21's attributes"},
        "6766": {"comment":"32 cells of $40: BRIGHT 1, PAPER 0, INK 0"},
        "6770": {"synopsis":"One attribute.","comment":"One cell"},
        "6772": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "6774": {"comment":"MENU_HEADER_TEXT's colours"},
        "6780": {"comment":"AT 21,0"},
        "6786": {"comment":"DE = the title"},
        "6787": {"comment":"Printed up to its bit-7 end (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT)"},
        "6790": {"comment":"AT 21,26 and the stripes"},
        "6795": {"comment":"DRAW_STRIPES, which returns to the caller"},
        "6798": {"synopsis":"Clears lines 21 to 23 (CLEAR_LINES with B = 21, D = 23).","comment":"B = 21, the first line"},
        "6800": {"comment":"D = 23, the last"},
        "6802": {"comment":"Cleared (CLEAR_LINES)"},
        "6805": {"synopsis":"Renumbers the program, from the number in $5B75 in steps of the one in $5B77 (start-up sets\nboth to 10 at $01E5), with bank 0 and the machine stack:\n1. The lines counted (COUNT_LINES); none, or start + step x count (one step past the last\nline's new number; the product's overflow is not tested) 10000 or more: RENUM_FAIL.\n2. Every line's text is searched for LINE, LIST, LLIST, GO TO, GO SUB, RESTORE and RUN\nfollowed by a plain number (RENUM_REF); each such number is replaced by the new number of\nthe line it names.\n3. Every line gets its new number, start + step x its place.\n4. Bank 7 and its stack; $5B73 = 0.\nExit: carry when done; no carry (RENUM_FAIL) when there are no lines, the numbers would go\npast 9999, or there is no room for a longer number.\nObserved: lines 1 and 2 became 10 and 20; $5B75 and $5B77 held 10 and 10.","comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "6808": {"comment":"COUNT_LINES: DE = the number of lines"},
        "6811": {"comment":"No lines at all?"},
        "6816": {"comment":"HL = the step, from $5B77"},
        "6819": {"comment":"HL = step x count; its overflow not tested"},
        "6822": {"comment":"DE = step x count"},
        "6823": {"comment":"Plus the start, from $5B75"},
        "6827": {"comment":"10000 or more?"},
        "6836": {"comment":"From the first line"},
        "6839": {"synopsis":"One line: $5B73 = the address of its length, $5B95 = the next line's (ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM).","comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: DE = the next line"},
        "6842": {"comment":"HL = the address of the line's length"},
        "6844": {"comment":"Kept in $5B73"},
        "6847": {"comment":"HL = the line's first character"},
        "6849": {"comment":"$5B95 = the next line"},
        "6853": {"synopsis":"The line's next character, past a hidden number (ROM 3's SKIP_NUMBER); up to its ENTER each\nis checked by RENUM_REF.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "6854": {"comment":"Past a hidden number (ROM 3's SKIP_NUMBER)"},
        "6857": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "6861": {"comment":"RENUM_REF: a keyword with a line number to change?"},
        "6864": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6866": {"synopsis":"The line done: on to the next, up to VARS.","comment":"DE = the next line"},
        "6870": {"comment":"Reached VARS?"},
        "6876": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "6879": {"comment":"COUNT_LINES again: DE = the count"},
        "6882": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "6884": {"comment":"DE = 0, the line's place"},
        "6887": {"comment":"HL = PROG, the first line"},
        "6890": {"synopsis":"One line's new number: step x DE + start, written high byte first over the old; then past\nthe line by its length.","comment":"Count, place and line kept"},
        "6893": {"comment":"HL = the step"},
        "6896": {"comment":"ROM 3's HL_HL_X_DE: HL = step x place"},
        "6899": {"comment":"Plus the start: the new number"},
        "6904": {"comment":"DE = the new number"},
        "6905": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "6906": {"comment":"Written over the old, high byte first"},
        "6910": {"comment":"BC = the line's length"},
        "6913": {"comment":"HL past the length, then past the line"},
        "6915": {"comment":"DE = the next place"},
        "6917": {"comment":"BC = the lines left"},
        "6918": {"comment":"The last line?"},
        "6923": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 and its stack"},
        "6926": {"comment":"$5B73 = 0"},
        "6930": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "6932": {"synopsis":"RENUM_REF's keywords, searched with CPIR: LINE, LIST, LLIST, GO TO, GO SUB, RESTORE, RUN\n($CA $F0 $E1 $EC $ED $E5 $F7)."},
        "6939": {"synopsis":"Checks the character A at HL for a line number to change: when it is one of RENUM_TOKENS and\na number follows (spaces, digits, '.', 'E' after a digit) whose hidden form is followed by\n':' or ENTER, the number's text and hidden value are replaced by the new number of the line\nit names (the first line from that number on): RENUM_REF_NUMBER. $5B93 = the place after the\nkeyword, $5B8B = the old text's length.\nExit: HL = the place to go on from; $5B95 and the line's length moved by the change.","comment":"HL = the place after the character"},
        "6940": {"comment":"$5B93 = it"},
        "6943": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6944": {"comment":"RENUM_TOKENS' 7 codes searched for A"},
        "6950": {"comment":"One of RENUM_TOKENS?"},
        "6952": {"comment":"HL = the place after the character"},
        "6953": {"comment":"Not one: back"},
        "6954": {"comment":"BC counts the number's characters"},
        "6956": {"synopsis":"The next character of the number.","comment":"A = the next character"},
        "6957": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "6961": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_TEST: a digit?"},
        "6964": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6966": {"comment":"A '.'?"},
        "6970": {"comment":"The hidden number's marker?"},
        "6974": {"comment":"'e' or 'E'?"},
        "6980": {"comment":"After a digit (BC not 0)?"},
        "6984": {"synopsis":"Not a plain number: left as it is; on from $5B93.","comment":"HL = the place after the keyword"},
        "6988": {"synopsis":"Counted; the next.","comment":"Counted"},
        "6989": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6992": {"synopsis":"The hidden number reached: $5B8B = the text's length; only a number followed (past spaces)\nby ':' or ENTER is changed.","comment":"$5B8B = the text's length"},
        "6996": {"comment":"The marker's place kept"},
        "6997": {"comment":"ROM 3's SKIP_NUMBER: HL past the hidden number"},
        "7000": {"comment":"SKIP_SPACES"},
        "7003": {"comment":"A = the character after it"},
        "7004": {"comment":"HL = the marker"},
        "7005": {"comment":"A ':' after it?"},
        "7009": {"comment":"ENTER after it? Neither: left as it is"},
        "7012": {"synopsis":"The number's value (ROM 3's PUSH_NUMBER, FP_TO_BC) looked up as a line (ROM 3's FIND_LINE).\nNo such line and nothing after the program (the byte there $80):\n9999. Otherwise HL is the\nline found.","comment":"HL = the hidden number"},
        "7013": {"comment":"ROM 3's PUSH_NUMBER: its value stacked"},
        "7016": {"comment":"ROM 3's FP_TO_BC: BC = the value"},
        "7019": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "7021": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: HL = the first line from it on"},
        "7024": {"comment":"That line itself?"},
        "7026": {"comment":"No: the byte there, a line's or the variables'"},
        "7027": {"comment":"$80: past the last line?"},
        "7031": {"comment":"No line from it on: 9999"},
        "7036": {"synopsis":"The line found: its new number, step x its place (COUNT_LINES_TO) + start.","comment":"$5B91 = the line found"},
        "7039": {"comment":"COUNT_LINES_TO: DE = the lines before it"},
        "7042": {"comment":"HL = the step"},
        "7045": {"comment":"ROM 3's HL_HL_X_DE: HL = step x place"},
        "7048": {"comment":"Plus the start: its new number"},
        "7053": {"synopsis":"The new number HL as text at $5B8D (NUMBER_TEXT, leading zeros dropped); $5B8B = its length\nless the old text's. Longer: room made after the keyword when STKEND + the difference + $82\nstays below SP (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), else RENUM_NO_ROOM.","comment":"DE = the text's place, $5B8D"},
        "7056": {"comment":"The new number kept, for the hidden form"},
        "7057": {"comment":"NUMBER_TEXT: HL = the first digit kept, B = digits after it"},
        "7060": {"comment":"DE = the new text's length"},
        "7064": {"comment":"The length and the first digit kept"},
        "7066": {"comment":"HL = the new length"},
        "7069": {"comment":"BC = the old length"},
        "7073": {"comment":"HL = the new length less the old"},
        "7076": {"comment":"$5B8B = the difference"},
        "7079": {"comment":"The same length?"},
        "7081": {"comment":"Shorter?"},
        "7083": {"comment":"Longer: BC = the bytes to make room for"},
        "7085": {"comment":"HL = the place after the keyword"},
        "7088": {"comment":"The place and the length kept"},
        "7090": {"comment":"STKEND + the difference past 65535?"},
        "7096": {"comment":"DE = STKEND + the difference"},
        "7097": {"comment":"Plus $82 bytes to spare"},
        "7103": {"comment":"Still below SP?"},
        "7108": {"comment":"DE = the length, HL = the place"},
        "7110": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM: room after the keyword"},
        "7113": {"comment":"On to the copy"},
        "7115": {"synopsis":"No room: the two words dropped; on to RENUM_FAIL.","comment":"The length and the place dropped"},
        "7117": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), no carry, and a return: the swap back to bank 7's stack\nreturns to RENUMBER's caller from any depth.","comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 and its stack"},
        "7120": {"comment":"No carry: not done"},
        "7122": {"synopsis":"Shorter: BC = the old length less the new; that many bytes after the keyword removed (ROM\n3's\nRECLAIM).","comment":"BC less the new length, one by one"},
        "7126": {"comment":"HL = the place after the keyword"},
        "7129": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM: BC bytes removed there"},
        "7132": {"synopsis":"The new digits copied after the keyword, then the number marker $0E and the new value's five\nbytes (ROM 3's STACK_BC); the line's length at ($5B73) and the next line's address ($5B95)\nmoved by the change.\nExit: HL = the place after the number.","comment":"DE = the place after the keyword"},
        "7136": {"comment":"HL = the new text, BC = its length"},
        "7138": {"comment":"The digits copied in"},
        "7140": {"comment":"HL = the byte after them"},
        "7141": {"comment":"The number's marker"},
        "7143": {"comment":"BC = the new number"},
        "7144": {"comment":"The five bytes' place kept"},
        "7146": {"comment":"ROM 3's STACK_BC: the new value, HL = its 5 bytes"},
        "7149": {"comment":"DE = their place"},
        "7150": {"comment":"The five bytes copied over the old ones"},
        "7155": {"comment":"The place after them kept"},
        "7157": {"comment":"HL = the address of the line's length"},
        "7161": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "7164": {"comment":"Plus the difference"},
        "7168": {"comment":"DE = the new length"},
        "7169": {"comment":"HL = its address"},
        "7170": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7173": {"comment":"The next line's address"},
        "7176": {"comment":"Moved by the difference"},
        "7184": {"comment":"HL = the place after the number"},
        "7186": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of program lines: COUNT_LINES_TO with $5B91 = VARS.","comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "7189": {"comment":"$5B91 = it, the place to count to"},
        "7192": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of program lines before the address in $5B91, stepping from PROG with ROM\n3's\nNEXT_ITEM (0 when it is PROG).\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "7195": {"comment":"DE = the place to count to"},
        "7199": {"comment":"The first line?"},
        "7204": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "7207": {"comment":"BC = 0 lines"},
        "7210": {"synopsis":"The next line: is it the one?","comment":"The count kept"},
        "7211": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: DE = the next line"},
        "7214": {"comment":"The place reached?"},
        "7222": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "7223": {"comment":"One more line"},
        "7227": {"synopsis":"Found: DE = the count.","comment":"DE = the count"},
        "7228": {"comment":"Plus the line just stepped over"},
        "7230": {"synopsis":"It is the first: DE = 0.","comment":"None before it"},
        "7234": {"synopsis":"HL moved on, then SKIP_SPACES.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "7235": {"synopsis":"A = the byte at HL, HL moved past spaces.","comment":"A = the byte"},
        "7236": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "7241": {"synopsis":"Writes HL (0-9999) as four digits at DE (NUMBER_DIGIT for the thousands, hundreds and tens),\nthen turns up to three leading '0's into spaces.\nExit: HL = the first digit kept, B = the digits after it; DE past the text.","comment":"The text's start kept"},
        "7242": {"comment":"-1000"},
        "7245": {"comment":"The thousands (NUMBER_DIGIT)"},
        "7248": {"comment":"-100"},
        "7251": {"comment":"The hundreds"},
        "7254": {"comment":"-10"},
        "7256": {"comment":"The tens"},
        "7259": {"comment":"The units"},
        "7260": {"comment":"As a character"},
        "7262": {"comment":"Written"},
        "7264": {"comment":"B = up to three leading '0's"},
        "7266": {"comment":"HL = the first digit"},
        "7267": {"synopsis":"A leading '0'?","comment":"A = the digit"},
        "7268": {"comment":"A '0'?"},
        "7270": {"comment":"Not a '0': HL = the first digit kept"},
        "7271": {"comment":"Made a space"},
        "7274": {"comment":"Up to three"},
        "7277": {"synopsis":"One digit: how many times BC (a negative power of ten) goes into HL, as a character at DE;\nHL\nkeeps the rest.","comment":"A counts"},
        "7278": {"synopsis":"One more.","comment":"The power of ten taken off"},
        "7279": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "7280": {"comment":"Not below zero yet?"},
        "7282": {"comment":"The last one undone"},
        "7284": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "7285": {"comment":"As a character"},
        "7287": {"comment":"Written at DE"},
        "7290": {"synopsis":"The editor's window for the main screen, copied to $FD98 (IX) by WINDOW_SET: a count (8),\nthen the bytes 0, 0 (IX + 1, its top line), 20 (IX + 2, its last line counted from the top),\n0, 0, 0, $0F (IX + 6, the cursor's colour), 0."},
        "7299": {"synopsis":"The window for the lower screen: a count (8), then 0, 22 (its top line), 1 (its last line\ncounted from the top: lines 22-23), 0, 0, 0, $0F, 0."},
        "7308": {"synopsis":"IX = $FD98, the window there from WINDOW_MAIN_DATA (main screen, lines 0-20).","comment":"IX = the window's bytes at $FD98"},
        "7312": {"comment":"HL = WINDOW_MAIN_DATA"},
        "7317": {"synopsis":"The window at $FD98 from WINDOW_LOW_DATA (lines 22-23).","comment":"HL = WINDOW_LOW_DATA (IX as it was)"},
        "7320": {"synopsis":"The 8 bytes at HL to $FD98 (COPY_COUNTED, $2152).","comment":"DE = the window at $FD98"},
        "7323": {"comment":"The 8 bytes copied (COPY_COUNTED)"},
        "7326": {"synopsis":"Prints A, then D (RST $10 each); carry. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"A printed"},
        "7327": {"comment":"Then D"},
        "7329": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7331": {"synopsis":"The cursor's colour, IX + 6 = A's PAPER and INK bits ($3F); carry.","comment":"PAPER and INK only"},
        "7333": {"comment":"The cursor's colour"},
        "7336": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7338": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor at line B of the window (IX + 1 added), column C: the attribute there kept\nin IX + 7, then replaced by IX + 6's colour with the old FLASH and BRIGHT bits inverted.\nCarry.\nChanges: A, B, DE, HL.","comment":"B = the screen line: B + the window's top"},
        "7343": {"comment":"ATTR_ADDRESS: HL = the cell's attribute address"},
        "7346": {"comment":"The old attribute kept in IX + 7"},
        "7350": {"comment":"FLASH, BRIGHT inverted"},
        "7353": {"comment":"Plus the cursor's colour"},
        "7356": {"comment":"Shown"},
        "7357": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7359": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off line B of the window, column C: the attribute kept in IX + 7 put back.","comment":"B = the screen line: B + the window's top"},
        "7364": {"comment":"ATTR_ADDRESS: HL = the cell's attribute address"},
        "7367": {"comment":"The attribute kept in IX + 7 put back"},
        "7372": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's lines B to E up by one (pixels and attributes, each line from the one\nbelow), then prints the 32 characters at HL on line E (PRINT_ROW).","comment":"The text kept"},
        "7373": {"comment":"H = 0: up"},
        "7375": {"comment":"A = the lines to move, E less B"},
        "7379": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's lines B to E down by one (B the upper; each line from the one above,\nstarting at E), then prints the 32 characters at HL on line B (PRINT_ROW).","comment":"The text kept"},
        "7380": {"comment":"B = the lower line E, E = the upper B"},
        "7383": {"comment":"A = the lines to move"},
        "7384": {"comment":"H = $FF: down"},
        "7386": {"synopsis":"C = the lines to move; none when B = E.","comment":"C = the count"},
        "7387": {"comment":"Only one line?"},
        "7391": {"comment":"The line to print kept in E"},
        "7392": {"comment":"LINE_TO_ROM3: B in ROM 3's form"},
        "7395": {"synopsis":"One line: its display address (ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR), and the source's, one below (up)\nor one above (down).","comment":"Line and count kept"},
        "7396": {"comment":"C = the direction"},
        "7397": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: the line's display address"},
        "7400": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "7401": {"comment":"Up?"},
        "7405": {"comment":"Down: the line above (ROM 3 counts lines upwards)"},
        "7408": {"synopsis":"Up: the line below.","comment":"Up: the line below"},
        "7409": {"synopsis":"Its 8 pixel rows copied, 32 bytes each, then its 32 attributes.","comment":"The target kept"},
        "7410": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: HL = the source's"},
        "7413": {"comment":"DE = the target"},
        "7414": {"comment":"A = the direction"},
        "7415": {"comment":"32 bytes a row, 8 rows"},
        "7419": {"synopsis":"One pixel row.","comment":"Count and addresses kept"},
        "7422": {"comment":"BC = 32"},
        "7424": {"comment":"One row copied"},
        "7426": {"comment":"Addresses and count back"},
        "7429": {"comment":"Both one pixel row down"},
        "7431": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "7433": {"comment":"The direction and the target kept"},
        "7435": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR: the source's attributes"},
        "7438": {"comment":"DE = them"},
        "7439": {"comment":"The target's row taken, the source's attributes kept"},
        "7440": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR: the target's attributes"},
        "7443": {"comment":"DE = them"},
        "7444": {"comment":"HL = the source's attributes, the target's kept"},
        "7445": {"comment":"DE = the target's attributes"},
        "7446": {"comment":"32 attributes copied"},
        "7451": {"comment":"A = the direction"},
        "7452": {"comment":"B = the line, C = the count"},
        "7453": {"comment":"Up?"},
        "7456": {"comment":"Down: the line above"},
        "7459": {"synopsis":"Up: the next line is the one below.","comment":"Up: the line below"},
        "7460": {"synopsis":"The next, while C counts.","comment":"One fewer: more to move?"},
        "7461": {"comment":"H = the direction again"},
        "7464": {"comment":"DE = the lines given"},
        "7465": {"comment":"B = E: the freed line"},
        "7466": {"synopsis":"The freed line printed.","comment":"HL = the text"},
        "7467": {"synopsis":"Prints the 32 characters at HL on line B, from column 0 (PRINT_AT_BC), with the editor's\ncolours (SWAP_COLOURS around it); in the lower screen (TV_FLAG bit 0 set) when $EC0D bit 6\nis\nset. A 0 prints a space; codes from $90 (UDGs) are printed with bank 0 paged in.\nExit: carry; TV_FLAG as it was.","comment":"SWAP_COLOURS: the editor's colours in"},
        "7470": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "7471": {"comment":"TV_FLAG kept"},
        "7475": {"comment":"The lower screen ($EC0D bit 6)?"},
        "7480": {"comment":"Bit 0 off: the main screen"},
        "7484": {"comment":"Bit 0 on: the lower screen"},
        "7486": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG set; AT B,0.","comment":"TV_FLAG set"},
        "7489": {"comment":"AT B,0 (PRINT_AT_BC)"},
        "7494": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "7495": {"comment":"32 characters"},
        "7497": {"synopsis":"One character: 0 is a space.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "7498": {"comment":"A 0?"},
        "7501": {"comment":"A space instead"},
        "7503": {"synopsis":"From $90 up?","comment":"A UDG or a token?"},
        "7507": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A: printed"},
        "7510": {"synopsis":"The next.","comment":"The next character"},
        "7511": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "7513": {"comment":"TV_FLAG back"},
        "7517": {"comment":"SWAP_COLOURS: the program's colours back"},
        "7520": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7522": {"synopsis":"From $90: printed with bank 0 and the machine stack, then back to bank 7.","comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "7525": {"comment":"Printed (RST $10), with bank 0's UDGs in place"},
        "7526": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 and its stack"},
        "7529": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "7531": {"synopsis":"Clears the window's lines B to D (IX + 1 added): their pixels to 0 and their attributes to\nthe editor's ATTR_P (SWAP_COLOURS around it), through ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR and\nLINE_ATTR_ADDR. Carry.","comment":"SWAP_COLOURS: the editor's colours in"},
        "7534": {"comment":"C = the number of lines"},
        "7538": {"comment":"LINE_TO_ROM3: B in ROM 3's form"},
        "7541": {"synopsis":"One line.","comment":"Line and count kept"},
        "7542": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: HL = the display address"},
        "7545": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "7547": {"synopsis":"One of its 8 pixel rows.","comment":"The row's start kept"},
        "7548": {"comment":"32 bytes of 0"},
        "7551": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Cleared"},
        "7553": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "7555": {"comment":"HL = the row's start"},
        "7556": {"comment":"The next pixel row"},
        "7557": {"comment":"All 8?"},
        "7560": {"comment":"B = 32, kept"},
        "7563": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR: the line's attributes"},
        "7566": {"comment":"HL = them"},
        "7567": {"comment":"B = 32"},
        "7568": {"comment":"A = ATTR_P"},
        "7571": {"synopsis":"One attribute.","comment":"One attribute"},
        "7573": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "7575": {"comment":"B = the line, C = the count"},
        "7576": {"comment":"One line lower (ROM 3 counts lines upwards)"},
        "7577": {"comment":"One fewer: more?"},
        "7580": {"comment":"SWAP_COLOURS: the program's colours back"},
        "7583": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7585": {"synopsis":"Line B, column C of the window in ROM 3's print-position form: C = 33 - C, then\nLINE_TO_ROM3.","comment":"C = 33 - C, the column as ROM 3 counts it"},
        "7589": {"synopsis":"B = 24 - B - (IX + 1): line B of the window as ROM 3 counts lines.\nChanges: A, B.","comment":"A = 24 - B"},
        "7592": {"comment":"Less the window's top line"},
        "7595": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "7597": {"synopsis":"HL = $5800 + 32 x B + C, the attribute address of line B, column C. Keeps BC.\nChanges: A, DE, HL.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "7598": {"comment":"DE = B x 256"},
        "7601": {"comment":"Three shifts right: DE = B x 32"},
        "7613": {"comment":"The attribute area"},
        "7616": {"comment":"BC = the column"},
        "7617": {"comment":"Plus the column and 32 x the line"},
        "7619": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "7621": {"synopsis":"Swaps ATTR_P, MASK_P, ATTR_T and MASK_T ($5C8D-$5C90) with the copies at $EC0F-$EC12, and\nP_FLAG with $EC13: the editor's colours in, or the program's back. Keeps AF, DE and HL.\nChanges: DE', HL'.","comment":"AF, HL and DE kept"},
        "7624": {"comment":"HL = ATTR_P and MASK_P"},
        "7627": {"comment":"DE = ATTR_T and MASK_T"},
        "7631": {"comment":"The alternate set for the copies"},
        "7632": {"comment":"HL, DE = the copies at $EC0F"},
        "7639": {"comment":"To the system variables"},
        "7646": {"comment":"The old values"},
        "7647": {"comment":"Kept at $EC0F"},
        "7654": {"comment":"HL = $EC13, P_FLAG's copy"},
        "7657": {"comment":"A = P_FLAG"},
        "7660": {"comment":"D = the copy"},
        "7661": {"comment":"P_FLAG kept"},
        "7662": {"comment":"The copy to P_FLAG"},
        "7666": {"comment":"DE, HL and AF back"},
        "7670": {"synopsis":"The tokenizer at $1DFC in mode 1 ($FDB6 = 1), from $0DCF: the line is walked, not written.","comment":"Mode 1: the line walked, not written"},
        "7672": {"comment":"To TOKENIZE at $1DFC"},
        "7674": {"synopsis":"The tokenizer at $1DFC in mode 0 ($FDB6 = 0), from $0D8C: the line is written.","comment":"Mode 0: the line written"},
        "7676": {"synopsis":"Turns the line the editor holds, read character by character ($0E22 through TOK_GET_CHAR),\ninto a BASIC line at E_LINE, keywords typed letter by letter becoming their tokens:\n1. $FDB6 = the mode; $FDB1 (characters read) and $FDB3 (written) = 0; $FDB7 = SP, for the\nreturns from deeper down; $FC9F and $FCA1 = 0 ($15E4); $FDB0 = 0; the word buffer $FDA0\nempty ($FDA9 its end).\n2. The edit line emptied (ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS, bank 0); $FDAD = 0, the state; $FDAE =\nE_LINE, the place written; $FDAB = 0.\n3. Each character's class (TOK_GET_CHAR): letters gather in the buffer; at the first\ncharacter that cannot be in a word the buffer is looked up (KEYWORD_LOOKUP) and written\nas a token or as its letters. A space in a word is kept once ($FDAB marks it), so that GO\nTO and DEF FN are found; when the two words are not one keyword the first is written as\ntext and the rest looked up again.\n4. The state: 0 between words, 1 in a word, 2 in quotes ('\"' toggles it), 4 after REM: in 2\nand 4 the characters are written as they are.\n5. Writing goes through TOK_OUT (< >, <= >= and <> joined), TOK_PUT (states) and TOK_SPACING\n(spaces around keywords dropped).\nEntry: A = the mode, from $1DF6 (1: the line walked, not written, up to X_PTR) or $1DFA\n(0: the line written).\nExit: mode 0: no carry at the line's ENTER; mode 1: carry, BC = the characters read up to\nX_PTR (the smaller of read and written) or to ENTER.","comment":"$FDB6 = the mode"},
        "7679": {"comment":"$FDB1 and $FDB3 = 0: none read, none written"},
        "7688": {"comment":"$FDB7 = SP"},
        "7692": {"comment":"$FCA1 and $FC9F = 0 ($15E4)"},
        "7695": {"comment":"$FDB0 = 0: no keyword last, no space held"},
        "7700": {"comment":"The word buffer empty"},
        "7706": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack ($05A7)"},
        "7709": {"comment":"The edit line emptied (ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS)"},
        "7712": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack ($05CC)"},
        "7715": {"comment":"$FDAD = 0: between words"},
        "7720": {"comment":"$FDAE: the place to write, at E_LINE"},
        "7726": {"comment":"$FDAB = 0: no space in the word"},
        "7732": {"synopsis":"The next character: $FDB1 counted, B = it, C = its class (TOK_GET_CHAR).","comment":"One more read ($FDB1)"},
        "7739": {"comment":"B = the character, A = its class (TOK_GET_CHAR)"},
        "7742": {"comment":"C = the class"},
        "7743": {"comment":"Between words?"},
        "7748": {"comment":"No: TOK_IN_STATE"},
        "7750": {"synopsis":"State 0: a letter starts a word; anything else is written (TOK_CHAR_OUT).","comment":"Can it start a word?"},
        "7753": {"comment":"No: written as it is"},
        "7755": {"synopsis":"Into the word buffer (TOK_BUF_ADD): state 1.","comment":"Into the word buffer (TOK_BUF_ADD)"},
        "7758": {"comment":"Full?"},
        "7760": {"comment":"State 1: in a word"},
        "7765": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "7767": {"synopsis":"The buffer is full: with a space in it, TOK_SPLIT.","comment":"A space in the word?"},
        "7772": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPLIT"},
        "7775": {"synopsis":"The buffer written as text (TOK_FLUSH); state 0.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "7776": {"comment":"The word written as text (TOK_FLUSH)"},
        "7780": {"comment":"State 0"},
        "7785": {"synopsis":"The rest of the word passed as text, up to a character that ends a word (class bit 0), which\nis taken again in state 0.","comment":"Can it end a word?"},
        "7788": {"comment":"Yes: back to state 0"},
        "7790": {"comment":"No: it is written (TOK_OUT)"},
        "7794": {"comment":"The line's end: done"},
        "7795": {"comment":"One more read"},
        "7802": {"comment":"B = the next, A = its class"},
        "7805": {"comment":"C = the class"},
        "7806": {"comment":"Until one ends the word"},
        "7808": {"synopsis":"B written (TOK_OUT); at ENTER in mode 0, TOKENIZE ends with no carry.","comment":"Written (TOK_OUT)"},
        "7812": {"comment":"The line's end: done"},
        "7813": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "7815": {"synopsis":"State 1 (a word): a letter, '#' or '$' goes into the buffer; other states: written as it is.","comment":"In a word?"},
        "7817": {"comment":"No: written as it is"},
        "7819": {"comment":"The word ended?"},
        "7822": {"comment":"No: into the buffer"},
        "7824": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "7825": {"synopsis":"The word ended: looked up (KEYWORD_LOOKUP); a keyword: TOK_KEYWORD.","comment":"A keyword? (KEYWORD_LOOKUP)"},
        "7828": {"comment":"B, C = the character again"},
        "7829": {"comment":"A keyword: TOK_KEYWORD"},
        "7831": {"comment":"A space in the buffer?"},
        "7836": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPLIT"},
        "7838": {"comment":"A space ended it?"},
        "7841": {"comment":"No: the word written as text"},
        "7843": {"comment":"The space into the buffer (TOK_BUF_ADD)"},
        "7846": {"comment":"Full?"},
        "7848": {"comment":"$FDAB = the space's place"},
        "7855": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "7857": {"synopsis":"The buffer is two words and not a keyword: the first written as text, and what follows from\nthe space moved to the buffer's start, then looked up again (at the second time the space\nitself is written and dropped).","comment":"The character kept"},
        "7858": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's start"},
        "7861": {"comment":"DE = the space's place"},
        "7865": {"comment":"The space first?"},
        "7873": {"comment":"Yes: DE one on, so the space itself is written"},
        "7874": {"synopsis":"DE = the last character to write.","comment":"DE = the last character before the space"},
        "7875": {"comment":"From the first"},
        "7877": {"synopsis":"The next.","comment":"The next character"},
        "7878": {"synopsis":"One character written (TOK_OUT).","comment":"A = the character, bit 7 off"},
        "7881": {"comment":"Both places kept"},
        "7883": {"comment":"Written (TOK_OUT)"},
        "7886": {"comment":"Both places back"},
        "7888": {"comment":"Up to DE?"},
        "7896": {"comment":"The rest moved down"},
        "7900": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's start"},
        "7903": {"comment":"$FDAB = it: the space now first"},
        "7906": {"comment":"BC = the last character's place"},
        "7911": {"comment":"The space was first?"},
        "7913": {"comment":"No: the rest moved down"},
        "7919": {"comment":"DE = the character after the space"},
        "7920": {"comment":"$FDAB = 0: no space in the word"},
        "7928": {"comment":"Only the space in the buffer?"},
        "7936": {"comment":"Yes: the character back, the buffer emptied"},
        "7937": {"comment":"State 0, the buffer empty"},
        "7939": {"synopsis":"One byte down, up to the one with bit 7 set; $FDA9 = the new end; looked up again.","comment":"One byte down"},
        "7943": {"comment":"The last one (bit 7)?"},
        "7947": {"comment":"$FDA9 = the new end"},
        "7950": {"comment":"Looked up again"},
        "7952": {"synopsis":"A keyword: its token written (TOK_OUT); $FDAB = 0; the state 0 unless it is 4 (after REM);\nthe buffer emptied; the character that ended the word taken again at TOK_BETWEEN.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "7953": {"comment":"The token written (TOK_OUT)"},
        "7956": {"comment":"B, C = the character again"},
        "7957": {"comment":"$FDAB = 0: no space in the word"},
        "7963": {"comment":"After REM (state 4)?"},
        "7968": {"comment":"Yes: the state kept"},
        "7970": {"synopsis":"State 0."},
        "7975": {"synopsis":"The buffer empty.","comment":"$FDA9 = the start: the buffer empty"},
        "7981": {"comment":"The ending character taken again"},
        "7984": {"synopsis":"The next character of the line ($0E22) in B, and its class in A: 6 a letter (bits 1 and 2),\n2 '#' or '$' (bit 1), 3 a space (bits 0 and 1), 1 anything else (bit 0). Bit 2: starts a\nword; bit 1: can be in one; bit 0: ends one.","comment":"A = the next character ($0E22)"},
        "7987": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "7988": {"comment":"Below '?'"},
        "7990": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_CLASS_LOW"},
        "7992": {"comment":"Made lower case"},
        "7994": {"comment":"A letter? (LOWER_TEST)"},
        "7997": {"comment":"A letter: 6"},
        "7999": {"synopsis":"1: anything else."},
        "8001": {"comment":"1: anything else"},
        "8002": {"synopsis":"Below '?': a space, '#' or '$'?","comment":"A space?"},
        "8004": {"comment":"A space: 3"},
        "8006": {"comment":"A '#'?"},
        "8008": {"comment":"A '#': 2"},
        "8010": {"comment":"Below '#': anything else"},
        "8012": {"comment":"A '$'?"},
        "8014": {"comment":"Not a $: 1"},
        "8016": {"synopsis":"2: '#' or '$'."},
        "8019": {"synopsis":"3: a space."},
        "8022": {"synopsis":"6: a letter."},
        "8025": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a lower-case letter ('a'-'z').","comment":"Past 'z'?"},
        "8027": {"comment":"Past 'z': no carry"},
        "8028": {"comment":"From 'a' on: carry"},
        "8032": {"synopsis":"Writes the word buffer as text (TOK_SPACING for each character, up to the one with bit 7\nset) and empties it: $FDA9 = $FDA0, $FDAB = 0.","comment":"The buffer's start"},
        "8035": {"comment":"$FDA9 = it: empty"},
        "8038": {"comment":"$FDAB = 0: no space in it"},
        "8045": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"A = the character, bit 7 off"},
        "8048": {"comment":"Its place kept"},
        "8049": {"comment":"Written (TOK_SPACING)"},
        "8053": {"comment":"The last one (bit 7)?"},
        "8056": {"comment":"The last: done"},
        "8057": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8058": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8060": {"synopsis":"Adds character B to the word buffer ($FDA0-$FDA8), the last character marked with bit 7.\nExit: carry; no carry when it is full (its end at $FDA9).","comment":"HL = the buffer's end"},
        "8063": {"comment":"Full (the end at $FDA9)?"},
        "8066": {"comment":"Full?"},
        "8068": {"comment":"No: room for it"},
        "8072": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8075": {"synopsis":"Not the first: the last one's bit 7 cleared.","comment":"The first character?"},
        "8080": {"comment":"Not the first: link it"},
        "8084": {"comment":"The first: stored at once"},
        "8086": {"synopsis":"Bit 7 off the one before.","comment":"The one before"},
        "8088": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "8092": {"synopsis":"B stored with bit 7 set; $FDA9 moved on.","comment":"B with bit 7: now the last"},
        "8096": {"comment":"$FDA9 = the new end"},
        "8100": {"comment":"Carry: added"},
        "8101": {"comment":"Carry: added"},
        "8102": {"synopsis":"Full: no carry.","comment":"No carry: full"},
        "8105": {"synopsis":"Writes A, joining a '<' or '>' with the character after it: either is held in $FDB5; then <\n> gives <> ($C9), < = gives <= ($C7), > = gives >= ($C8); otherwise the held one is written\nfirst. The rest goes to TOK_PUT.\nExit: carry; no carry at the line's end in mode 0.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8106": {"comment":"One held in $FDB5?"},
        "8110": {"comment":"One held: TOK_OUT_PAIR"},
        "8112": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "8113": {"comment":"A '>'?"},
        "8115": {"comment":"Held"},
        "8117": {"comment":"A '<'?"},
        "8119": {"comment":"Held"},
        "8121": {"synopsis":"On to TOK_PUT.","comment":"Written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8125": {"synopsis":"'<' or '>' held; carry.","comment":"Held"},
        "8128": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "8130": {"synopsis":"One is held: $FDB5 = 0; was it '<'?","comment":"The held one a '<'?"},
        "8132": {"comment":"Nothing held now"},
        "8137": {"comment":"A '>' was held: TOK_OUT_GT"},
        "8139": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "8140": {"comment":"A '>' after it?"},
        "8142": {"comment":"No: TOK_OUT_LT_EQ"},
        "8144": {"comment":"The <> token, $C9"},
        "8146": {"comment":"Written"},
        "8148": {"synopsis":"'<' then '='?","comment":"A '=' after it?"},
        "8150": {"comment":"No: '<' first"},
        "8152": {"comment":"The <= token, $C7"},
        "8154": {"comment":"Written"},
        "8156": {"synopsis":"'<' then something else: '<' written first.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8157": {"comment":"The '<' written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8159": {"comment":"The '<' written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8162": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8163": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8165": {"synopsis":"'>' held: then '='?","comment":"A = the character"},
        "8166": {"comment":"A '=' after it?"},
        "8168": {"comment":"No: '>' first"},
        "8170": {"comment":"The >= token, $C8"},
        "8172": {"comment":"Written"},
        "8174": {"synopsis":"'>' then something else: '>' written first.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8175": {"comment":"The '>' written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8177": {"comment":"The '>' written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8180": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8181": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8183": {"synopsis":"Writes A (TOK_SPACING), keeping the state: REM ($EA) makes it 4; '\"' toggles state 2 (bit 1,\nbit 0 cleared). ENTER ends the line: TOK_PUT_ENTER.","comment":"ENTER? Not written: the edit line has one"},
        "8185": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_PUT_ENTER"},
        "8187": {"comment":"REM?"},
        "8189": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "8190": {"comment":"No: a quote?"},
        "8192": {"comment":"State 4: after REM"},
        "8197": {"comment":"Written"},
        "8199": {"synopsis":"A quote?","comment":"A '\"'?"},
        "8201": {"comment":"No: written as it is"},
        "8203": {"comment":"The state's bit 0 off, bit 1 toggled"},
        "8213": {"synopsis":"Written; carry.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "8214": {"comment":"Written (TOK_SPACING)"},
        "8217": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "8218": {"comment":"Carry: on"},
        "8219": {"synopsis":"ENTER: in mode 0 no carry (the line done); in mode 1 BC = $FDB1, SP = $FDB7 and a return\nfrom TOKENIZE with carry.","comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "8224": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8226": {"comment":"BC = the characters read"},
        "8230": {"comment":"SP as TOKENIZE found it"},
        "8234": {"comment":"Carry, back to TOKENIZE's caller"},
        "8235": {"comment":"Back to TOKENIZE's caller"},
        "8236": {"synopsis":"No carry.","comment":"No carry"},
        "8238": {"comment":"Back to the caller"},
        "8239": {"synopsis":"Writes A (TOK_WRITE), dropping the spaces around keywords, with the flags in $FDB0 (bit 0: a\nkeyword was the last written; bit 1: a space held back): a space after a keyword is dropped;\nof a run of spaces the last is held; a keyword ($A3 and up) drops a held space; any other\ncharacter writes the held one first.","comment":"E = the character"},
        "8240": {"comment":"D = the flags"},
        "8245": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "8247": {"comment":"No: TOK_SPACING_CHR"},
        "8249": {"comment":"After a keyword?"},
        "8252": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPACE_AFTER"},
        "8254": {"comment":"One held already?"},
        "8257": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPACE_HELD"},
        "8259": {"comment":"Held: bit 1 set, nothing written"},
        "8266": {"synopsis":"A space held already: this one written.","comment":"This one written (TOK_WRITE)"},
        "8270": {"comment":"A = the flags"},
        "8273": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8274": {"synopsis":"After a keyword: dropped.","comment":"Bit 0 off: the space dropped"},
        "8281": {"synopsis":"Not a space: a keyword ($A3 up)?","comment":"A keyword?"},
        "8283": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPACING_KEY"},
        "8285": {"comment":"A space held?"},
        "8288": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPACE_FIRST"},
        "8290": {"comment":"No: bit 0 off"},
        "8296": {"comment":"The character written (TOK_WRITE)"},
        "8301": {"synopsis":"The held space written first, then the character; both flags cleared.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8302": {"comment":"The held space written (TOK_WRITE)"},
        "8307": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "8308": {"comment":"Both bits off"},
        "8316": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8321": {"synopsis":"A keyword: a held space dropped, bit 0 set; written.","comment":"Bit 1 off (the held space dropped), bit 0 on"},
        "8329": {"comment":"The token written (TOK_WRITE)"},
        "8334": {"synopsis":"Writes A at the place in $FDAE and moves it on ($FDB3 counted). Mode 0: one byte of room\nopened there (ROOM_TEST_BC, ROM 3's MOVE_POINTERS, the bytes above moved up) and A stored.\nMode 1: nothing written, the place moved past the byte there (and past a hidden number after\n$0E); when the place is X_PTR, BC = the smaller of $FDB1 and $FDB3, SP = $FDB7 and a return\nfrom TOKENIZE with carry.","comment":"One more written ($FDB3)"},
        "8341": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "8344": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "8345": {"comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "8350": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "8351": {"comment":"Mode 0: TOK_WRITE_ZERO"},
        "8353": {"comment":"At X_PTR?"},
        "8359": {"comment":"No: TOK_FIND_ON"},
        "8363": {"comment":"No: TOK_FIND_ON"},
        "8365": {"comment":"BC = the characters read"},
        "8369": {"comment":"Fewer written than read?"},
        "8375": {"comment":"No: BC = the characters read"},
        "8377": {"comment":"Then BC = the characters written"},
        "8381": {"synopsis":"SP back: out of TOKENIZE, carry.","comment":"SP as TOKENIZE found it"},
        "8385": {"comment":"Carry, back to TOKENIZE's caller"},
        "8386": {"comment":"Back to TOKENIZE's caller"},
        "8387": {"synopsis":"Mode 1: carry.","comment":"Carry: mode 1"},
        "8390": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: no carry.","comment":"No carry: mode 0"},
        "8392": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 and the machine stack.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack ($05A7; carry kept)"},
        "8395": {"comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "8397": {"comment":"A = the byte at the place"},
        "8398": {"comment":"DE = the place"},
        "8399": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "8401": {"comment":"No: past the byte"},
        "8403": {"comment":"DE past its five bytes"},
        "8408": {"comment":"Then past the byte"},
        "8410": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: room for one byte at HL, then A stored there.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8411": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "8414": {"comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "8416": {"comment":"Room for it? (ROOM_TEST_BC; report 4 if not)"},
        "8419": {"comment":"DE and HL back"},
        "8421": {"comment":"Pointers moved (ROM 3's MOVE_POINTERS)"},
        "8424": {"comment":"The bytes up to STKEND moved up"},
        "8427": {"comment":"DE = the new STKEND, HL = the old"},
        "8430": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "8431": {"comment":"Stored at the place"},
        "8432": {"synopsis":"$FDAE = the next place; bank 7.","comment":"DE = the next place"},
        "8433": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack ($05CC)"},
        "8436": {"comment":"$FDAE = it"},
        "8440": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8441": {"synopsis":"Whether BC bytes fit between STKEND and the stack, with $82 bytes to spare; returns with\ncarry when they do. Otherwise ERR_NR = 3 and REPORT_4_ROOM (report 4, \"Out of memory\").","comment":"HL = STKEND + BC"},
        "8445": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "8447": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "8448": {"comment":"Plus $82 to spare"},
        "8452": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "8454": {"comment":"Below SP?"},
        "8456": {"comment":"Yes: carry, they fit"},
        "8457": {"synopsis":"No room: ERR_NR = 3 (report 4), then ROM 1's $25CB through $3E80, which calls the ROM 1\nroutine whose address is the word after the CALL.","comment":"ERR_NR = 3: report 4"},
        "8462": {"comment":"To ROM 1's $25CB (the word after the CALL)"},
        "8467": {"synopsis":"Looks the word in the buffer at $FDA0 up as a keyword, letters in either case:\n1. $142D copies the RAM routines to $FCAE again ($E8 bytes from $1442), clearing $FC9F and\n$FCA1.\n2. ROM 3's keywords: the RAM routine at $FD43 (the copy of $14DC) pages ROM 3 in and looks\nthrough its list at $0096, codes from $A5.\n3. Then this ROM's list at $168E (the RAM routine at $FD5C, the copy of $14F0, B = $F9):\nSPECTRUM, PLAY, GOTO, GOSUB, DEFFN, OPEN#, CLOSE# (the spellings as stored there), which\ngive $A3, $A4, $EC (GO TO), $ED (GO SUB), $CE (DEF FN), $D3 (OPEN #), $D4 (CLOSE #).\nExit: carry and A = the token when found; no carry otherwise.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The RAM routines copied to $FCAE again ($142D)"},
        "8470": {"comment":"ROM 3's keywords (the RAM routine at $FD43)"},
        "8473": {"comment":"Found: carry, A = the token"},
        "8474": {"comment":"The 128K's own list, codes from $F9"},
        "8476": {"comment":"DE = the word"},
        "8479": {"comment":"HL = the 128K's list"},
        "8482": {"comment":"Looked up (the RAM routine at $FD5C)"},
        "8485": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "8486": {"comment":"$FF: CLOSE # ($D4)?"},
        "8488": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FF"},
        "8490": {"comment":"The CLOSE # token"},
        "8492": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8494": {"synopsis":"$FE: OPEN # ($D3)?"},
        "8496": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FE"},
        "8498": {"comment":"The OPEN # token"},
        "8500": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8502": {"synopsis":"$FD: DEF FN ($CE)?"},
        "8504": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FD"},
        "8506": {"comment":"The DEF FN token"},
        "8508": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8510": {"synopsis":"$FC: GO SUB ($ED)?"},
        "8512": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FC"},
        "8514": {"comment":"The GO SUB token"},
        "8516": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8518": {"synopsis":"$FB: GO TO ($EC)?"},
        "8520": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FB"},
        "8522": {"comment":"The GO TO token"},
        "8524": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8526": {"synopsis":"$F9 or $FA: less $56 (SPECTRUM $A3, PLAY $A4).","comment":"$A3 SPECTRUM or $A4 PLAY"},
        "8528": {"synopsis":"Carry: found."},
        "8529": {"comment":"Back with the token"},
        "8530": {"synopsis":"Copies the bytes at HL, a count first, to DE.\nExit: HL and DE past them; B = 0.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "8532": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Copied"},
        "8534": {"comment":"Both on"},
        "8536": {"comment":"All?"},
        "8538": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8539": {"synopsis":"Carry and A = its value when A is a digit '0'-'9'; no carry otherwise. Nothing in this ROM\ncalls it.","comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "8542": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8543": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "8545": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8546": {"comment":"A = its value"},
        "8548": {"comment":"Carry: a digit"},
        "8550": {"synopsis":"Looks key A up in the table at HL (a count, then code and address per key) and runs the\nroutine found.\nExit: no carry and NZ when not found; Z when found, carry as the routine\nreturned it.","comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "8552": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "8554": {"synopsis":"The next entry: its code compared with A.","comment":"This key?"},
        "8555": {"comment":"DE = the entry's address"},
        "8559": {"comment":"Yes: TABLE_FOUND"},
        "8561": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8562": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8564": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "8566": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "8569": {"synopsis":"Found: the routine run (TABLE_CALL), Z, its carry kept.","comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "8570": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "8572": {"comment":"Run (TABLE_CALL)"},
        "8575": {"comment":"It returned carry?"},
        "8577": {"comment":"Z and no carry"},
        "8579": {"synopsis":"The routine returned carry: Z and carry.","comment":"Z"},
        "8580": {"comment":"And carry"},
        "8582": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL."},
        "8583": {"synopsis":"The routine ROM 2 reaches through this ROM's $3FF0 (its ASK_RETRY's hook): prints a message\nin the lower screen and waits for a key:\n1. With Z, DE is the list of keys to take ($FF at its end); with NZ any key (DE = 0).\n2. Stream -3 ($FD, the lower screen) selected (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT).\n3. The message wrapped to 32 columns: in a stretch of 32 characters without its end, the\nlast space becomes ENTER (the message is changed where it is).\n4. AT 0,0 and the message printed.\n5. Keys read ($1871) until one in the list comes.\n6. ROM 3's CLS_LOWER, and stream -2 ($FE, the upper screen) selected.\nEntry: HL = the message ($FF at its end); DE = the keys, when Z is set.\nExit: A = the key; 0 when there was no list. HL = the list.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Z: DE is the list of keys"},
        "8585": {"comment":"NZ: no list, any key"},
        "8588": {"synopsis":"The list kept, then the message.","comment":"The list kept"},
        "8589": {"comment":"The message kept"},
        "8590": {"comment":"Stream -3: the lower screen"},
        "8592": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8595": {"comment":"HL = the message"},
        "8597": {"synopsis":"A stretch of up to 32 characters from HL.","comment":"B = 32: one screen line"},
        "8599": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"A space?"},
        "8602": {"comment":"No: DE kept"},
        "8604": {"comment":"DE = the last space so far"},
        "8606": {"synopsis":"The message's end?","comment":"The message's end?"},
        "8608": {"comment":"Yes: the message fits"},
        "8610": {"comment":"The next, up to 32"},
        "8611": {"comment":"Up to 32"},
        "8613": {"comment":"No end in 32: the last space becomes ENTER"},
        "8617": {"comment":"The next stretch from there"},
        "8619": {"synopsis":"AT 0,0, then the message.","comment":"AT 0,0"},
        "8621": {"comment":"AT"},
        "8624": {"comment":"Row 0"},
        "8627": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "8628": {"comment":"HL = the message"},
        "8629": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"Its end?"},
        "8632": {"comment":"Yes: a key"},
        "8634": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8636": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8638": {"synopsis":"A key ($1871); with a list, one in it.","comment":"A key ($1871)"},
        "8641": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "8642": {"comment":"HL = the list"},
        "8643": {"comment":"No list? Any key, A = 0"},
        "8646": {"comment":"No list: done"},
        "8648": {"synopsis":"The next key in the list.","comment":"The list's key the one pressed?"},
        "8650": {"comment":"Found: done"},
        "8652": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8653": {"comment":"The list's end? Then another key"},
        "8655": {"comment":"Not the end: the next"},
        "8657": {"comment":"Another key"},
        "8659": {"synopsis":"The key taken: the lower screen cleared, the upper screen's stream again.","comment":"The key kept"},
        "8660": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "8663": {"comment":"Stream -2: the upper screen"},
        "8665": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8668": {"comment":"A = the key, HL = the list"},
        "8671": {"synopsis":"The start of a program that tests the machine's hardware; no call or jump in this ROM's\ncode reaches it. Each check shifts one bit into IX at bit 0 (TEST_RESULT_BIT), 1 for a pass:\n1. Interrupts off, IX = $FFFF, border white, SP = $7FFF; $28F7 first.\n2. The screen cleared, INK 7 and PAPER 0, the text at $3261, 40 frames waited.\n3. Border green and the RAM test: banks 0-7 filled with D = $00; each byte checked and\nmade its complement, banks 0 up; each checked and given D again, from $FFFF of bank 7\ndown; the same again with D = $FF. A byte that differs: RAM_FAIL.\n4. Then BANK_ID_TEST.","comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "8672": {"comment":"IX: the results, one bit per check"},
        "8676": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "8678": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "8680": {"comment":"The stack below $8000"},
        "8683": {"comment":"First $28F7"},
        "8686": {"comment":"Interrupts off, border white"},
        "8691": {"comment":"Screen cleared, plain colours (TEST_CLS)"},
        "8694": {"comment":"INK 7, PAPER 0"},
        "8700": {"comment":"The text at $3261"},
        "8706": {"comment":"40 frames (WAIT_40_FRAMES)"},
        "8709": {"comment":"Border green: the RAM test"},
        "8711": {"comment":"Border green"},
        "8713": {"comment":"Two passes; D = $00, the pattern"},
        "8716": {"synopsis":"One pass with pattern D: every bank filled with it.","comment":"Bank 0 first"},
        "8718": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "8721": {"synopsis":"Bank A filled with D, $C000-$FFFF.","comment":"Bank A paged in at $C000"},
        "8723": {"comment":"The bank number aside"},
        "8724": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "8727": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"The pattern"},
        "8728": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "8731": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "8733": {"comment":"The next bank, up to 7"},
        "8737": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "8739": {"comment":"Bank 0 again"},
        "8741": {"synopsis":"Bank A checked upwards: each byte must be D, then is made its complement.","comment":"Paged in"},
        "8743": {"comment":"The number aside"},
        "8744": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "8747": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Still the pattern? If not, RAM_FAIL"},
        "8749": {"comment":"No: RAM_FAIL"},
        "8751": {"comment":"Its complement written"},
        "8753": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "8756": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "8758": {"comment":"The next bank, up to 7"},
        "8762": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "8764": {"comment":"From bank 7 down"},
        "8765": {"synopsis":"Bank A checked from the top down: each byte must be D's complement, then is D again.","comment":"The number aside; HL from $FFFF down"},
        "8769": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Down one; below $C000?"},
        "8773": {"comment":"Yes: the next bank"},
        "8775": {"comment":"Still the complement? If not, RAM_FAIL"},
        "8778": {"comment":"No: RAM_FAIL"},
        "8780": {"comment":"The pattern again"},
        "8781": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "8783": {"synopsis":"The next bank down.","comment":"Bank 0 done?"},
        "8786": {"comment":"Yes: the pass ends"},
        "8788": {"comment":"The bank below"},
        "8789": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "8791": {"comment":"And checked"},
        "8793": {"synopsis":"The pass's end: a second one with D = $FF, then BANK_ID_TEST.","comment":"Both passes done? On to BANK_ID_TEST"},
        "8794": {"comment":"Both: BANK_ID_TEST"},
        "8797": {"comment":"The second pass with $FF"},
        "8799": {"comment":"Again"},
        "8802": {"synopsis":"A RAM byte did not hold its value: the start-up run again (TEST_REINIT), bank 0, INK 7 and\nPAPER 0, the screen cleared and \"RAM fail: address hhhh, page n\" printed, HL being the\naddress and A' the bank, in hex; then the machine stops (interrupts off and HALT).\nBANK_ID_FAIL comes here too, with HL = 0.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "8803": {"comment":"Bank and address kept"},
        "8805": {"comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "8808": {"comment":"Bank 0, paging byte 0"},
        "8815": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "8817": {"comment":"INK 7, PAPER 0"},
        "8823": {"comment":"Screen cleared (TEST_CLS)"},
        "8826": {"comment":"'RAM fail: address '"},
        "8832": {"comment":"The address"},
        "8833": {"comment":"Its high byte in hex (TEST_HEX_A)"},
        "8834": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "8837": {"comment":"Its low byte"},
        "8841": {"comment":"The main registers aside"},
        "8842": {"comment":"', page '"},
        "8848": {"comment":"The bank, 0-7"},
        "8851": {"comment":"In hex"},
        "8855": {"comment":"Stopped for good"},
        "8856": {"comment":"For good"},
        "8857": {"synopsis":"Prints A as two hex digits (HEX_DIGITS, TEST_PRINT_A), the alternate DE and HL used for\nthe lookup.\nChanges: AF, B, the alternate DE and HL.","comment":"HL and A kept"},
        "8860": {"comment":"The high digit"},
        "8868": {"comment":"Two digits"},
        "8870": {"synopsis":"One digit.","comment":"DE = the digit (alternate set)"},
        "8874": {"comment":"Its character from HEX_DIGITS"},
        "8879": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8882": {"comment":"Then the low digit"},
        "8886": {"comment":"Both?"},
        "8888": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "8889": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8890": {"synopsis":"RAM_FAIL's text: AT 10,0, \"RAM fail: address \", $FF at its end."},
        "8912": {"synopsis":"No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it. Border black, the picture cleared, then for\never each attribute from $5800 to $5AFF made of three samples of the EAR input (port $FE\nbit 6) shifted into C.","comment":"Border black"},
        "8914": {"comment":"Border black"},
        "8916": {"comment":"The picture cleared, $4000-$57FF"},
        "8929": {"synopsis":"Again from $5800.","comment":"From the first attribute"},
        "8932": {"synopsis":"One attribute.","comment":"Three samples, C = 0"},
        "8935": {"synopsis":"One sample.","comment":"The EAR bit"},
        "8939": {"comment":"Into C, shifted on"},
        "8943": {"comment":"Timing"},
        "8947": {"comment":"Three?"},
        "8949": {"comment":"The attribute"},
        "8951": {"comment":"Past $5AFF?"},
        "8954": {"comment":"No: the next attribute"},
        "8956": {"comment":"For ever"},
        "8958": {"synopsis":"RAM_FAIL's \", page \", $FF at its end."},
        "8966": {"synopsis":"The 16 hex digits, \"0123456789ABCDEF\", for TEST_HEX_A."},
        "8982": {"synopsis":"PAGING_RESULT's text: AT 10,0, \"RAM test passed\", $FF at its end."},
        "9001": {"synopsis":"Checks that the eight banks are eight: each gets its number at $CAFE, banks 0 up; then from\n7 down each must still hold its own (BANK_ID_FAIL if not). Then each bank's number goes to\n$E000, PAGE_ROM_TEST is copied to $D000 in banks 7 and 3 (COPY_PAGE_TEST) and run there\nwith bank 3 paged in.","comment":"Bank 0 first; HL = $CAFE"},
        "9006": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "9009": {"synopsis":"Its number written.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9011": {"comment":"Its number at $CAFE"},
        "9012": {"comment":"The next, up to 7"},
        "9015": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "9017": {"synopsis":"Bank A - 1 checked, from 7 down.","comment":"The bank below paged in"},
        "9018": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9020": {"comment":"Its number still there?"},
        "9021": {"comment":"No: BANK_ID_FAIL"},
        "9024": {"comment":"Bank 0 done?"},
        "9025": {"comment":"No: the next one down"},
        "9027": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9031": {"comment":"Bank 0 first"},
        "9033": {"synopsis":"Its number at $E000.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9035": {"comment":"Its number at $E000"},
        "9038": {"comment":"The next, up to 7"},
        "9041": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "9043": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9044": {"comment":"The ROM test copied into it"},
        "9047": {"comment":"And into bank 3"},
        "9052": {"comment":"Run there, bank 3 paged in"},
        "9055": {"synopsis":"Pages bank A in at $C000 and copies PAGE_ROM_TEST ($B9 bytes from $2370) to $D000 in it.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9058": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9060": {"comment":"PAGE_ROM_TEST to $D000, $B9 bytes"},
        "9071": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9072": {"synopsis":"Runs at $D000, copied there in banks 3 and 7 by COPY_PAGE_TEST (its calls of $D08E and\n$D09B are RESULT_BIT_RAM and ROM_SUM; SPECIAL_BANKS is read at $D0A9):\n1. The four all-RAM configurations of port $1FFD (1, 3, 5, 7): the bytes at $1FFB, $6000,\n$A000 and $E000, where BANK_ID_TEST put each bank's number, must give SPECIAL_BANKS;\nD = 1 when all do, 0 when one does not, kept in the alternate set.\n2. The ROMs summed (ROM_SUM): ROM 0 and ROM 1 together give one result bit; then with\n$1FFD = 4, two more sums give another.\n3. Normal paging back, ROM 0, the copies at $5B5C and $5B67 = 0, and on at PAGING_RESULT.","comment":"Configuration 0, all-RAM paging on"},
        "9074": {"comment":"DE = SPECIAL_BANKS (its copy at $D0A9)"},
        "9077": {"comment":"HL = $1FFB, in the first quarter"},
        "9080": {"synopsis":"One configuration of port $1FFD.","comment":"The configuration set (port $1FFD)"},
        "9083": {"comment":"All-RAM configuration A"},
        "9085": {"comment":"Kept aside"},
        "9086": {"comment":"BC = $4000: a quarter"},
        "9089": {"synopsis":"One quarter: its byte must be the bank number expected.","comment":"The bank expected here"},
        "9091": {"comment":"The number BANK_ID_TEST wrote?"},
        "9092": {"comment":"No: SPECIAL_FAIL"},
        "9094": {"comment":"The next quarter, up to $E000"},
        "9095": {"comment":"Until past $FFFF"},
        "9097": {"comment":"The next configuration: 3, 5, 7"},
        "9100": {"comment":"All four?"},
        "9102": {"comment":"No: the next configuration"},
        "9104": {"comment":"D = 1: all right"},
        "9106": {"comment":"On to the ROMs"},
        "9108": {"synopsis":"A wrong bank: D = 0.","comment":"D = 0: a wrong bank"},
        "9111": {"synopsis":"The ROM checksums.","comment":"D into the alternate set"},
        "9112": {"comment":"Bank 3 and ROM 0 ($7FFD = 3, $1FFD = 0)"},
        "9117": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9122": {"comment":"Normal paging, ROM 0"},
        "9124": {"comment":"ROM 0 sums to 0? (ROM_SUM)"},
        "9127": {"comment":"No: ROM_LOW_BAD"},
        "9129": {"comment":"ROM 1: $7FFD = $13"},
        "9134": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9136": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9139": {"comment":"No: ROM_LOW_BAD"},
        "9141": {"comment":"Both: a 1 result bit"},
        "9142": {"comment":"Carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9145": {"synopsis":"The second pair of sums, $1FFD bit 2 set.","comment":"$1FFD = 4"},
        "9150": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9152": {"comment":"$7FFD = 3: ROM 2"},
        "9157": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9159": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9162": {"comment":"No: ROM_HIGH_BAD"},
        "9164": {"comment":"$7FFD = $0B: still ROM 2 (bit 4 clear)"},
        "9169": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9171": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9174": {"comment":"No: ROM_HIGH_BAD"},
        "9176": {"comment":"Both: a 1 result bit"},
        "9177": {"comment":"Carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9180": {"synopsis":"Normal paging again, ROM 0; the copies of both ports 0; on in ROM 0.","comment":"$7FFD = 3"},
        "9187": {"comment":"$1FFD = 0: ROM 0"},
        "9193": {"comment":"The copies at $5B5C and $5B67 = 0"},
        "9199": {"comment":"On in ROM 0"},
        "9202": {"synopsis":"ROM 0 or 1 did not sum to 0: a 0 bit; on to the second pair.","comment":"A 0 result bit"},
        "9203": {"comment":"No carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9206": {"comment":"The second pair"},
        "9208": {"synopsis":"The second pair failed: a 0 bit.","comment":"A 0 result bit"},
        "9209": {"comment":"No carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9212": {"comment":"Normal paging again"},
        "9214": {"synopsis":"PAGE_ROM_TEST's copy of TEST_RESULT_BIT (at $D08E): the carry shifted into IX at bit 0.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "9215": {"comment":"DE = IX"},
        "9218": {"comment":"Carry in at bit 0, the rest up one"},
        "9222": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "9226": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9227": {"synopsis":"Runs at $D09B: adds up the 16K at $0000-$3FFF, the ROM paged in, in A (modulo 256).\nExit: Z when the sum is 0.\nChanges: A, D, HL.","comment":"A = 0, HL = 0"},
        "9230": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Added"},
        "9232": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9233": {"comment":"Up to $3FFF?"},
        "9237": {"comment":"No: the next byte"},
        "9239": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "9241": {"synopsis":"The banks PAGE_ROM_TEST expects at $0000, $4000, $8000 and $C000 in the four all-RAM\nconfigurations: 0 1 2 3, 4 5 6 7, 4 5 6 3, 4 7 6 3 (read at $D0A9)."},
        "9257": {"synopsis":"Shifts the carry into IX at bit 0, the rest up one: each check's result, carry for a pass.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "9258": {"comment":"DE = IX"},
        "9261": {"comment":"Carry in at bit 0, the rest up one"},
        "9265": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "9270": {"synopsis":"Back in ROM 0 after PAGE_ROM_TEST: bank 0, SP = $7FFF, the configurations' result (D = 1) as\na\nbit; the start-up run again, \"RAM test passed\" shown for 40 frames; then TEST_SEQUENCE.","comment":"Bank 0, ROM 0"},
        "9275": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9277": {"comment":"The stack again"},
        "9280": {"comment":"D = the configurations' result"},
        "9281": {"comment":"Carry when D is 1"},
        "9283": {"comment":"The result bit"},
        "9286": {"comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "9289": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9292": {"comment":"'RAM test passed'"},
        "9298": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "9301": {"comment":"The other tests"},
        "9303": {"synopsis":"A bank did not hold its number: the start-up run again (TEST_REINIT), then RAM_FAIL with\nHL = 0.","comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "9306": {"comment":"AF swapped, as RAM_FAIL swaps it back"},
        "9307": {"comment":"Address 0"},
        "9310": {"comment":"Reported (RAM_FAIL)"},
        "9313": {"synopsis":"The other tests in turn: $2C99, $28B6, $295D, KEYBOARD_TEST, $2C1F, $2C6E, $29D0, $2B24,\n$2A4B, PRINTER_TEST, $3558 and $35A3, then on at $2B91.","comment":"Each test in turn"},
        "9316": {"comment":"$28B6"},
        "9319": {"comment":"$295D"},
        "9322": {"comment":"The keys (KEYBOARD_TEST)"},
        "9325": {"comment":"$2C1F"},
        "9328": {"comment":"$2C6E"},
        "9331": {"comment":"$29D0"},
        "9334": {"comment":"$2B24"},
        "9337": {"comment":"$2A4B"},
        "9340": {"comment":"The printer (PRINTER_TEST)"},
        "9343": {"comment":"$3558"},
        "9346": {"comment":"$35A3"},
        "9349": {"comment":"Then $2B91"},
        "9352": {"synopsis":"Tests the printer port:\n1. BUSY: with the printer turned off line (a key waited for), bit 0 of port $0FFD must be\n1; turned on line, 0. One result bit.\n2. Data: bit 4 set in $5B67 (the strobe's resting level); characters $20-$7F and $A0-$FF\nsent twice (PRN_COUNTED, an ENTER after each 72), Q stopping it; then ENTER (a pass) or\nSPACE asked for: another bit.","comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9355": {"comment":"'Printer BUSY signal test'"},
        "9361": {"comment":"'Turn the printer '"},
        "9367": {"comment":"'OFFLINE'"},
        "9373": {"comment":"'Press any key to continue'"},
        "9379": {"comment":"A key (WAIT_NEW_KEY)"},
        "9382": {"comment":"Port $0FFD: BUSY in bit 0"},
        "9387": {"comment":"Busy while off line? If not, a fail"},
        "9389": {"comment":"Not busy: BUSY_FAIL"},
        "9391": {"comment":"'ONLINE ' over it"},
        "9397": {"comment":"A key"},
        "9400": {"comment":"Port $0FFD again"},
        "9405": {"comment":"Not busy now?"},
        "9407": {"comment":"Busy: BUSY_FAIL"},
        "9409": {"comment":"Carry: a pass"},
        "9412": {"synopsis":"BUSY wrong: no carry.","comment":"No carry: a fail"},
        "9414": {"synopsis":"The BUSY result into IX; then the data test.","comment":"The result bit"},
        "9417": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9420": {"comment":"Strobe bit 4 set in the $1FFD copy"},
        "9425": {"comment":"'Printer data test'"},
        "9431": {"comment":"The instructions, two lines"},
        "9437": {"comment":"E = 0: the column"},
        "9439": {"synopsis":"One pass of the printer data test: characters from $20 (the space) up.","comment":"From the space"},
        "9441": {"synopsis":"One character: sent and counted (PRN_COUNTED), then the next; past $7F on from $A0, past $FF a new pass.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "9446": {"comment":"The next; past $7F?"},
        "9449": {"comment":"Yes: on from $A0"},
        "9451": {"comment":"Past $FF (0)? The next pass"},
        "9452": {"comment":"Yes: the next pass"},
        "9454": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9456": {"synopsis":"$80-$9F skipped.","comment":"From $A0"},
        "9458": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9460": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the printer (PRN_SEND) and counts it in E; after 72 an ENTER too, E = 0.\nKeeps A.","comment":"Sent (PRN_SEND)"},
        "9464": {"comment":"One more in the line"},
        "9465": {"comment":"72?"},
        "9468": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9470": {"comment":"E = 0; an ENTER sent"},
        "9477": {"synopsis":"A back.","comment":"A back"},
        "9479": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the printer: waits while bit 0 of port $0FFD (BUSY) is 1, Q giving up (PRN_QUIT);\nA out to port $0FFD; then a strobe pulse on port $1FFD bit 4, from the copy at $5B67\n(cleared, then set again), with interrupts off.\nChanges: A, BC.","comment":"A kept"},
        "9480": {"synopsis":"Waiting while the printer is busy.","comment":"Q down? Then the printing stops"},
        "9482": {"comment":"Half-row $FBFE"},
        "9485": {"comment":"Q down: PRN_QUIT"},
        "9487": {"comment":"BUSY?"},
        "9490": {"comment":"Port $0FFD"},
        "9494": {"comment":"Busy: wait"},
        "9496": {"comment":"The byte out to port $0FFD"},
        "9499": {"comment":"Interrupts off for the pulse"},
        "9500": {"comment":"A = the $1FFD copy, strobe bit set"},
        "9503": {"synopsis":"The strobe bit toggled out: low, then high again.","comment":"Strobe bit toggled out"},
        "9508": {"comment":"Out to port $1FFD"},
        "9510": {"comment":"Low now? Then back high"},
        "9514": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "9515": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9516": {"synopsis":"Q stops the printing: five words dropped (PRN_SEND's AF and return, PRN_COUNTED's return,\nthe loop's AF and BC), then PRN_ASK_OK.","comment":"Five words off the stack"},
        "9520": {"synopsis":"Asks whether the characters printed well: ENTER (carry) or SPACE (TEST_ENTER_SPACE); the\nanswer is the result bit.","comment":"'If characters printed OK, ...'"},
        "9526": {"comment":"ENTER: carry; SPACE: none"},
        "9529": {"comment":"The result bit"},
        "9532": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9533": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: FLAGS bit 5 cleared, waited for until the interrupt sets it, cleared again.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"FLAGS"},
        "9536": {"comment":"No new key"},
        "9538": {"synopsis":"Until bit 5 is set.","comment":"A key yet?"},
        "9540": {"comment":"No: wait"},
        "9542": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "9544": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9545": {"synopsis":"AT 4,4, \"Printer data test\", $FF at its end."},
        "9566": {"synopsis":"AT 8,1, \"Make sure printer is ready\", AT 10,1, \"Press Q to quit printing\", $FF."},
        "9623": {"synopsis":"AT 12,1, \"If characters printed OK,\", ENTER, \"Press [ENTER], otherwise [SPACE]\",\n$FF at its end."},
        "9685": {"synopsis":"OVER 0, AT 4,4, \"Printer BUSY signal test\", $FF at its end."},
        "9715": {"synopsis":"AT 8,8, \"Turn the printer \", $FF at its end."},
        "9736": {"synopsis":"AT 10,12, \"ONLINE \", $FF at its end."},
        "9747": {"synopsis":"AT 10,12, \"OFFLINE\", $FF at its end."},
        "9758": {"synopsis":"AT 12,4, \"Press any key to continue\", $FF at its end."},
        "9787": {"synopsis":"AT 16,5, \"Passed - press [ENTER]\", $FF at its end. No LD in this ROM's code points at it."},
        "9813": {"synopsis":"AT 16,5, \"Failed - press [SPACE]\", $FF at its end. No LD in this ROM's code points at it."},
        "9839": {"synopsis":"Runs the start-up again from $016C (the routines at $5B00, the system variables and so on)\nwith A' = 'R' ($52), which makes it end at TEST_RESTARTED instead; the stack is kept, as the\nstart-up from $016C does not set SP, so the RET there comes back to this routine's caller.\nChanges: all registers.","comment":"'R': back by TEST_RESTARTED"},
        "9842": {"comment":"The start-up from $016C"},
        "9845": {"synopsis":"Where the start-up goes on when A' is 'R' (from $025C): stream 2 selected (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT), then COLOUR_RESET, whose RET goes back to TEST_REINIT's caller.","comment":"Stream 2: the upper screen"},
        "9847": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "9850": {"synopsis":"Prints COLOUR_RESET_SEQ: INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT, INVERSE, OVER and FLASH 0.","comment":"INK 0, PAPER 7, the rest 0"},
        "9853": {"comment":"Printed (TEST_PRINT_TEXT)"},
        "9857": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_RESET's codes: INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT 0, INVERSE 0, OVER 0, FLASH 0, then $FF."},
        "9870": {"synopsis":"Waits 25 frames (HALT with interrupts on), then interrupts off. No call or jump in this\nROM's code reaches it.\nKeeps BC, HL.","comment":"BC and HL kept"},
        "9872": {"comment":"25 frames"},
        "9874": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "9875": {"synopsis":"One frame.","comment":"One frame"},
        "9876": {"comment":"25 of them"},
        "9880": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9882": {"synopsis":"Waits 40 frames (HALT with interrupts on), then interrupts off. Changes: B.","comment":"40 frames"},
        "9884": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "9885": {"synopsis":"One frame.","comment":"One frame"},
        "9886": {"comment":"40 of them"},
        "9888": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9890": {"synopsis":"A delay: HL counted down from $2FF3.\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"$3000 rounds"},
        "9893": {"synopsis":"One round.","comment":"One round"},
        "9894": {"comment":"Time spent"},
        "9898": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "9900": {"comment":"No: again"},
        "9903": {"synopsis":"Waits until no key is down, then for ENTER or SPACE (TEST_KEY_WAIT), then beeps\n(TEST_BEEP).\nExit: carry for ENTER, no carry for SPACE; interrupts off.\nKeeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL, DE and BC kept"},
        "9906": {"comment":"All half-rows (port $00FE)"},
        "9909": {"synopsis":"Until every key is up.","comment":"No key down?"},
        "9915": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "9917": {"synopsis":"Until ENTER or SPACE.","comment":"A key (TEST_KEY_WAIT)"},
        "9920": {"comment":"ENTER ($21)? Carry"},
        "9923": {"comment":"ENTER: done"},
        "9925": {"comment":"SPACE ($20)?"},
        "9927": {"comment":"Neither: another key"},
        "9929": {"synopsis":"The answer's flags kept over a beep.","comment":"Flags kept; a beep (TEST_BEEP)"},
        "9930": {"comment":"The beep (TEST_BEEP)"},
        "9938": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: TEST_KEY_SCAN.","comment":"Scanned until a key is down"},
        "9942": {"synopsis":"Scans the keyboard until a key is down. Each key gets a number from its half-row and bit:\nhalf-row $FEFE gives $27, $1F, $17, $0F, $07 for bits 0-4 and each later half-row one less\n($BFFE bit 0, ENTER, is $21; $7FFE gives SPACE $20, SYMBOL SHIFT $18). A third key starts\nthe scan again.\nExit: A = E = the last key found; D = the one before, $FF when only one.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"L = $2F: the first half-row's number"},
        "9944": {"comment":"No key yet: D and E = $FF"},
        "9947": {"comment":"Half-row $FEFE first"},
        "9950": {"synopsis":"One half-row.","comment":"Keys down in it?"},
        "9955": {"comment":"None: the next half-row"},
        "9957": {"comment":"H = them"},
        "9958": {"comment":"A = the half-row's number"},
        "9959": {"synopsis":"A key found: a third one starts again.","comment":"A third key? Then again from the start"},
        "9960": {"comment":"Yes: again from the start"},
        "9962": {"synopsis":"The key's bit found, its number worked out.","comment":"Less 8 for each bit"},
        "9964": {"comment":"This bit?"},
        "9966": {"comment":"Not this bit: the next"},
        "9968": {"comment":"D = the key before, E = this one"},
        "9970": {"comment":"More keys in the half-row?"},
        "9972": {"synopsis":"The next half-row, up to $7FFE.","comment":"The next half-row's number"},
        "9973": {"comment":"The next half-row; all eight?"},
        "9975": {"comment":"Not the last: again"},
        "9977": {"comment":"A key found? A = it"},
        "9980": {"comment":"Yes: back"},
        "9981": {"comment":"None? Scan again"},
        "9987": {"synopsis":"Prints the bytes at HL up to an $FF (RST $10).\nExit: HL at the $FF.\nChanges: A.","comment":"The end?"},
        "9990": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "9991": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9992": {"comment":"The next"},
        "9993": {"comment":"Again"},
        "9995": {"synopsis":"Prints INK B and PAPER C.\nChanges: A.","comment":"INK B"},
        "9997": {"comment":"INK"},
        "9999": {"comment":"Colour B"},
        "10000": {"comment":"PAPER C"},
        "10002": {"comment":"PAPER"},
        "10004": {"comment":"Colour C"},
        "10006": {"synopsis":"Prints A (ROM 3's PRINT_A at $0010).","comment":"Printed (ROM 3's PRINT_A)"},
        "10010": {"synopsis":"Clears the screen (ROM 3's CLEAR_SCREEN) and prints COLOUR_RESET_SEQ.","comment":"Screen cleared (ROM 3's CLEAR_SCREEN)"},
        "10013": {"comment":"Plain colours (COLOUR_RESET)"},
        "10016": {"synopsis":"A short beep: the tone routine at $34E9 with HL = $0100 and DE = $00A0; interrupts\noff after it.","comment":"The tone's HL and DE"},
        "10022": {"synopsis":"The tone at $34E9 with HL and DE as given (from $280D and $2C86); interrupts off after it.","comment":"The tone ($34E9)"},
        "10025": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "10027": {"synopsis":"Carry when SPACE is up (port $7FFE bit 0). No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10031": {"comment":"Carry: SPACE up"},
        "10033": {"synopsis":"As SPACE_UP, through RR A (from $29F8).\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10037": {"comment":"Carry: SPACE up"},
        "10040": {"synopsis":"Z when, in half-row $7FFE, SPACE and SYMBOL SHIFT are down and M, N and B up. No call or\njump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10044": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 1 down, 2-4 up?"},
        "10049": {"synopsis":"Prints D spaces; A' = $38. No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nExit: D = 0.","comment":"A' = $38"},
        "10052": {"synopsis":"One space.","comment":"A space"},
        "10054": {"comment":"Printed (TEST_PRINT_A)"},
        "10057": {"comment":"D of them"},
        "10058": {"comment":"Until D is 0"},
        "10061": {"synopsis":"Tests the keys: screen cleared, BORDCR = $38, border white, the text at $2F17 printed, a\ndelay (TEST_DELAY), then KEY_TEST_KEYS.","comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "10064": {"comment":"BORDCR: paper white, ink black"},
        "10069": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "10071": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "10073": {"comment":"The text at $2F17"},
        "10079": {"comment":"A delay (TEST_DELAY)"},
        "10082": {"comment":"The keys (KEY_TEST_KEYS)"},
        "10086": {"synopsis":"Asks for the keys listed at $2841 in turn ($FF at its end): each a key number as\nTEST_KEY_SCAN gives it, or a code for a pair of keys (KEY_CAPS_PAIR, KEY_SYM_PAIR). Any\nother\nkey or pair is passed over; the code in E goes on to the comparison at $27F9.","comment":"The list of keys expected"},
        "10090": {"synopsis":"The next key expected.","comment":"The list's place"},
        "10091": {"comment":"A = the key expected"},
        "10092": {"comment":"The end ($FF)?"},
        "10093": {"comment":"The list done"},
        "10094": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "10095": {"comment":"A key (TEST_KEY_WAIT)"},
        "10098": {"comment":"A pause of $1000 rounds"},
        "10101": {"synopsis":"The pause.","comment":"Down to 0"},
        "10104": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "10106": {"comment":"One key only?"},
        "10109": {"comment":"Single: KEY_CODE_READY"},
        "10111": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT ($27) and another?"},
        "10113": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_CAPS_PAIR"},
        "10115": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT ($18) first?"},
        "10117": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_SYM_PAIR"},
        "10119": {"comment":"D and E swapped: SYMBOL SHIFT last?"},
        "10124": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_SYM_PAIR"},
        "10126": {"comment":"Another pair: passed over"},
        "10128": {"synopsis":"CAPS SHIFT and E's key: 0 gives $28, 1 $29, 2 $2A, 3 $2B, 4 $2C, 5 $2D, 6 $2E, 7 $2F, 8 $30,\n9 $31, SPACE $32, SYMBOL SHIFT $37; any other is passed over.","comment":"E = the other key: 0?"},
        "10135": {"comment":"1?"},
        "10141": {"comment":"2?"},
        "10147": {"comment":"3?"},
        "10153": {"comment":"4?"},
        "10159": {"comment":"5?"},
        "10165": {"comment":"6?"},
        "10171": {"comment":"7?"},
        "10177": {"comment":"8?"},
        "10183": {"comment":"9?"},
        "10189": {"comment":"SPACE?"},
        "10195": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "10201": {"comment":"Any other: passed over"},
        "10203": {"synopsis":"SYMBOL SHIFT and E's key: M gives $33, N $34, O $35, P $36; any other is passed over.","comment":"E = the other key: M?"},
        "10208": {"synopsis":"The code in E (a single key comes here with Z set): on to the comparison at $27F9.","comment":"Matched: to the comparison"},
        "10210": {"comment":"N?"},
        "10216": {"comment":"O?"},
        "10222": {"comment":"P?"},
        "10228": {"comment":"Not one of them: wait again"},
        "10230": {"comment":"Always taken: NZ from the CP"},
        "10233": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's check of one key (from the combining at $2790-$27F2): code E against the\nexpected one at HL, which is kept on the stack.\n1. Different: back to the wait at $276A for\nthe same key.\n2. The same: the next entry stacked in its place; a short tone (TONE_OUT\nthrough $2726, HL = DE = $0080).\n3. The key's square in the picture painted red: its place\nfrom KEY_TEST_PLACES, $3B bytes on, gives the row (high nibble x 2 + 5) and the column (low\nnibble x 2 + 1), and a space is printed there with PAPER 2.\n4. On to the next key at $276A.","comment":"The code"},
        "10234": {"comment":"Expected one at HL, still stacked"},
        "10236": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "10237": {"comment":"No: wait again"},
        "10240": {"comment":"Next entry stacked instead"},
        "10243": {"comment":"A short tone: HL = DE = $0080"},
        "10249": {"comment":"Registers kept around it"},
        "10253": {"comment":"TONE_OUT, then DI"},
        "10256": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "10260": {"comment":"HL = the next entry, still stacked"},
        "10262": {"comment":"PAPER 2: red"},
        "10265": {"comment":"Colour 2"},
        "10268": {"comment":"Back to the matched entry"},
        "10269": {"comment":"Its place, $3B bytes on"},
        "10273": {"comment":"High nibble x 2"},
        "10276": {"comment":"Down three bits: the nibble x 2"},
        "10279": {"comment":"B = that + 6"},
        "10283": {"comment":"Low nibble x 2 + 1"},
        "10284": {"comment":"Low nibble only"},
        "10287": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "10290": {"comment":"C = the column"},
        "10291": {"comment":"AT B - 1, C"},
        "10294": {"comment":"Row B - 1"},
        "10297": {"comment":"Column C"},
        "10299": {"comment":"A red space over the key"},
        "10302": {"comment":"Next key"},
        "10305": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's keys in the order the picture (KEY_TEST_PIC) shows them, row by row:\n58 key codes as the scan at $26D6 numbers them ($27 CAPS SHIFT, $18 SYMBOL SHIFT, $26 A,\n$21 ENTER, $20 SPACE, ...), with $28-$32 and $37 for a key pressed with CAPS SHIFT and\n$33-$37 for one with SYMBOL SHIFT, as $2790-$27F9 combine them. CAPS SHIFT and SYMBOL SHIFT\nare each in it twice. $FF ends it. Read at $276B and $27FA."},
        "10364": {"synopsis":"Where each key of KEY_TEST_CODES is drawn, one byte per key at the same index ($3B bytes\non): the high nibble gives the row (x 2 + 5), the low one the column (x 2 + 1). Read at\n$2821."},
        "10422": {"synopsis":"The SYMBOL SHIFT and A test: the screen cleared ($271A), border cyan, INK 6 and PAPER 0\n($270B), the instructions (SYMA_TEST_MSG); then the wait until SYMBOL SHIFT and A are both\ndown (SYMA_HELD), and $0200 more scans that must all find them still down.\nExit: through $2429, the result into IX: carry when they were held throughout.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10425": {"comment":"Border 5: cyan"},
        "10429": {"comment":"INK 6, PAPER 0"},
        "10435": {"comment":"Title and instructions"},
        "10441": {"synopsis":"Waits until both keys are down.","comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT and A down?"},
        "10444": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "10446": {"comment":"$0200 scans with both held"},
        "10449": {"synopsis":"One more scan with both held.","comment":"Count kept round the scan"},
        "10450": {"comment":"Still both down?"},
        "10454": {"comment":"Let go: failed"},
        "10456": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "10459": {"comment":"More to go"},
        "10461": {"comment":"Held throughout: passed"},
        "10462": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10465": {"synopsis":"Let go too soon: no carry.","comment":"Failed: no carry"},
        "10469": {"synopsis":"Whether the keys down are SYMBOL SHIFT ($18) and A ($26), in either order, by the scan at\n$26D2.\nExit: Z when they are.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"D, E = the keys down"},
        "10472": {"comment":"The first SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "10477": {"comment":"No: the two swapped"},
        "10480": {"comment":"The other SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "10482": {"comment":"Neither: NZ"},
        "10483": {"synopsis":"SYMBOL SHIFT found: is the other key A?","comment":"Then the other A?"},
        "10486": {"comment":"Z when it is"},
        "10487": {"synopsis":"The test program's first test (from $21EB): $266F (on through the start-up code at $016C),\nthe colour bars and a tone (COLOUR_BARS), the title, the instructions and the warning\n(TITLE_MSG), the answer read ($26AF: ENTER passes, SPACE fails) and recorded in IX ($2429);\nthen the sound chip's mixer (register 7) set to $FF, all off.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Start-up's set-up at $016C, A' = $52"},
        "10490": {"comment":"Colour bars and a tone"},
        "10493": {"comment":"BC = 0 (not read by the printer)"},
        "10496": {"comment":"Title, instructions, warning"},
        "10502": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "10505": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10508": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "10514": {"comment":"Register 7 (mixer) = $FF: all off"},
        "10516": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "10521": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "10525": {"synopsis":"The colour test's picture and tone: the top attribute row gets 16 pairs of cells with\nattribute 0, 8, 16 ... 120 (PAPER 0-7, then the same with BRIGHT 1) and is copied down the\nwhole screen; the sound chip's registers are set from AY_SETTINGS; the mixer (register 7) =\n$FB, the tone on channel C only.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Attribute 0 first"},
        "10526": {"comment":"Top attribute row"},
        "10529": {"comment":"16 pairs"},
        "10531": {"synopsis":"One pair of cells.","comment":"Two cells alike"},
        "10534": {"comment":"Next paper colour; BRIGHT from the 9th"},
        "10537": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "10539": {"comment":"The row copied down the screen"},
        "10542": {"comment":"The other 23 rows"},
        "10547": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "10553": {"comment":"Register/value pairs"},
        "10556": {"synopsis":"One register/value pair, until a byte with bit 7 set.","comment":"Register number"},
        "10558": {"comment":"The end marker?"},
        "10560": {"comment":"Yes: the mixer next"},
        "10562": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "10565": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "10567": {"comment":"Written"},
        "10570": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "10572": {"synopsis":"The mixer: tone C only.","comment":"AY ports again"},
        "10578": {"comment":"$FB: only channel C's tone on"},
        "10580": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "10585": {"comment":"Written"},
        "10589": {"synopsis":"The ULA test: the screen cleared, the title (ULA_TEST_MSG); OUT_LOOP copied to $6000 and\nrun there, in contended RAM; then, when a byte at $8000 keeps $AA, copied to $8000 and run\nthere too; border yellow. It always passes.\nExit: through $2429, carry into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10592": {"comment":"ULA TEST title"},
        "10598": {"comment":"OUT_LOOP to $6000"},
        "10604": {"comment":"Run in contended RAM"},
        "10607": {"comment":"Does $8000 keep a byte?"},
        "10612": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "10615": {"comment":"Kept?"},
        "10617": {"comment":"No: skip"},
        "10619": {"comment":"OUT_LOOP to $8000 too"},
        "10625": {"comment":"Run in uncontended RAM"},
        "10628": {"synopsis":"Border yellow; passed.","comment":"Border 6: yellow"},
        "10632": {"comment":"Always passed"},
        "10633": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10636": {"synopsis":"Copies OUT_LOOP's $3B bytes to DE.\nEntry: DE = the place.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"From OUT_LOOP"},
        "10639": {"comment":"$3B bytes"},
        "10645": {"synopsis":"Copied to $6000 and $8000 by ULA_TEST and run there: $2000 rounds of 16 writes to port\n$FE, A flipping between $00 and $FF (border black and white, the MIC and speaker bits\ntoggling). Its only jump is relative, so it runs anywhere.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"$2000 rounds"},
        "10648": {"synopsis":"One round of 16 writes.","comment":"Border 0 first"},
        "10652": {"comment":"Flipped between the writes"},
        "10698": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "10701": {"comment":"More rounds"},
        "10703": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10704": {"synopsis":"The joystick test: the screen cleared and the instructions and picture (JOY_TEST_MSG); then\nscan after scan of the keyboard rows the joysticks read as, $EFFE (joystick 1, kept in D)\nand $F7FE (joystick 2, in E): each direction seen clears its bit, and when the bits change\nevery label seen so far is painted out (JOY_WIPE). All ten seen: passed; SPACE gives up:\nfailed.\nExit: through $2429, the result into IX: carry when all ten were seen.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10707": {"comment":"Instructions and picture"},
        "10713": {"comment":"Five directions each, all unseen"},
        "10716": {"synopsis":"One scan of both joysticks.","comment":"The state kept for the next scan"},
        "10717": {"comment":"Row $EFFE: joystick 1"},
        "10720": {"comment":"Bits 0-4: 0 when pressed"},
        "10722": {"comment":"Pressed bits as 1s"},
        "10723": {"comment":"Cleared from D"},
        "10725": {"comment":"D = what is still unseen"},
        "10726": {"comment":"Row $F7FE: joystick 2"},
        "10729": {"comment":"Bits 0-4: 0 when pressed"},
        "10731": {"comment":"Pressed bits as 1s"},
        "10732": {"comment":"Cleared from E"},
        "10734": {"comment":"E = what is still unseen"},
        "10735": {"comment":"BC = the last state"},
        "10736": {"comment":"Joystick 1 changed?"},
        "10740": {"comment":"Joystick 2 changed?"},
        "10744": {"comment":"SPACE pressed? (carry: no)"},
        "10747": {"comment":"Not pressed: again"},
        "10749": {"comment":"A zero byte read: again"},
        "10751": {"comment":"Given up: failed"},
        "10752": {"comment":"To the record"},
        "10754": {"synopsis":"Every direction seen: carry.","comment":"All seen: passed"},
        "10755": {"synopsis":"The result into IX.","comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10758": {"synopsis":"The bits changed: the label of every direction seen so far painted out, joystick 1's\nfrom D's bits 0-4, then joystick 2's from E's, with their places from JOY_PLACES.","comment":"New state kept"},
        "10759": {"comment":"Joystick 1's label places"},
        "10762": {"comment":"Five directions"},
        "10764": {"synopsis":"One direction of joystick 1.","comment":"Next bit: seen?"},
        "10766": {"comment":"Seen: its label painted out"},
        "10769": {"comment":"Next place"},
        "10771": {"comment":"Next of five"},
        "10773": {"comment":"Joystick 2's five"},
        "10775": {"synopsis":"One direction of joystick 2.","comment":"Next bit: seen?"},
        "10777": {"comment":"Seen: its label painted out"},
        "10780": {"comment":"Next place"},
        "10782": {"comment":"Next of five"},
        "10784": {"comment":"State back"},
        "10785": {"comment":"Everything seen?"},
        "10787": {"comment":"Yes: passed"},
        "10789": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "10792": {"synopsis":"Paints one label out: two spaces with PAPER 2 at the place HL points to (a row, 3 below\nthe screen row, then a column), then PAPER 7.\nEntry: HL = the place's row byte.\nExit: HL as it came.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Counter kept"},
        "10793": {"comment":"B = row, C = column"},
        "10796": {"comment":"AT B - 3, C"},
        "10799": {"comment":"Row - 3"},
        "10804": {"comment":"Column"},
        "10806": {"comment":"PAPER 2: red"},
        "10812": {"comment":"Two red spaces"},
        "10815": {"comment":"Second space"},
        "10818": {"comment":"PAPER 7"},
        "10824": {"comment":"HL back to the row byte"},
        "10825": {"comment":"Counter back"},
        "10827": {"synopsis":"The second screen test: with interrupts off, the attributes all 0 (black on black); the\ntitle and 'Passed - press [ENTER]' printed; RAM bank 7 paged in at $C000 and the screen\ncopied to its screen ($C000-$D7FF); the title and 'Failed - press [SPACE]' printed over the\nnormal screen; bit 3 of port $7FFD set, which shows bank 7's screen, and both screens'\nattributes set to $38 so the text shows. The answer ($26AF: ENTER passes) is recorded in IX;\nthen the screen cleared, the paging byte put back, cleared again, interrupts on.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10830": {"comment":"No interrupts while paging"},
        "10831": {"comment":"Attributes all 0: black on black"},
        "10837": {"comment":"All $0300 attribute bytes"},
        "10844": {"comment":"Title, not yet visible"},
        "10850": {"comment":"'Passed - press [ENTER]'"},
        "10856": {"comment":"Paging byte kept"},
        "10860": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000"},
        "10862": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "10865": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "10870": {"comment":"The screen copied to bank 7's"},
        "10876": {"comment":"$1800 bytes: the pixels"},
        "10881": {"comment":"Title again, on the normal screen"},
        "10887": {"comment":"'Failed - press [SPACE]' over it"},
        "10893": {"comment":"Bit 3: bank 7's screen shown"},
        "10898": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "10901": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "10906": {"comment":"Normal screen's attributes $38"},
        "10915": {"comment":"$38: black INK on white PAPER"},
        "10919": {"comment":"Bank 7's too"},
        "10928": {"comment":"$38 there too"},
        "10932": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "10935": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10938": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "10941": {"comment":"Paging byte back"},
        "10942": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "10945": {"comment":"Port $7FFD: bank and screen as before"},
        "10950": {"comment":"Cleared again, the normal screen"},
        "10953": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "10955": {"synopsis":"SCREEN_TEST's title: AT 8,3, PAPER 0, INK 0, 'Screen switching test'."},
        "10984": {"synopsis":"AT 12,3, PAPER 0, INK 0, 'Passed - press [ENTER]': seen on the second screen."},
        "11014": {"synopsis":"The same place: 'Failed - press [SPACE]', seen on the normal screen."},
        "11044": {"synopsis":"The cassette output test: the screen cleared, border red, BORDCR = $08, the title\n(CASS_OUT_MSG); a tone of $0A00 cycles with HL = $0100 sent to the MIC output (port $FE bit\n3) by an inline copy of TONE_OUT's loop that flips bit 3 and holds the speaker bit set;\nthen HEARD_TONE_MSG and the answer ($26AF: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $2429, the result into IX.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11047": {"comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11051": {"comment":"BORDCR = $08: border 1 in the tone"},
        "11056": {"comment":"CASSETTE OUTPUT TEST title"},
        "11062": {"comment":"HL = $0100, DE = $0A00 cycles"},
        "11068": {"comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "11069": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "11071": {"comment":"L's low bits: 0-3 extra NOPs"},
        "11072": {"comment":"L / 4: the inner count"},
        "11076": {"comment":"IX = MIC_TONE_NOPS + 3 - low bits"},
        "11082": {"comment":"From MIC_TONE_NOPS"},
        "11086": {"comment":"+ 3 - low bits"},
        "11088": {"comment":"Border from BORDCR"},
        "11091": {"comment":"Bits 3-5: the border colour"},
        "11093": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-2"},
        "11096": {"comment":"Speaker bit 4 held set"},
        "11098": {"synopsis":"The entry JP (IX) uses: 0 to 3 NOPs, then the delay.","comment":"0-3 of these run, by IX"},
        "11101": {"comment":"B, C one more for the first DEC"},
        "11103": {"synopsis":"A half-cycle's delay: C inner rounds, B outer ones.","comment":"Inner delay"},
        "11104": {"comment":"Inner rounds"},
        "11106": {"comment":"C = $3F for the later rounds"},
        "11108": {"comment":"Outer count"},
        "11109": {"comment":"Outer rounds"},
        "11112": {"comment":"MIC bit 3 flipped"},
        "11114": {"comment":"Out: MIC flipped"},
        "11116": {"comment":"Outer count again; port byte in C"},
        "11118": {"comment":"MIC bit now set?"},
        "11120": {"comment":"Rising edge: the longer half"},
        "11122": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "11124": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "11126": {"comment":"Port byte back, inner count from L"},
        "11128": {"comment":"One cycle fewer"},
        "11129": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "11131": {"synopsis":"After a rising edge: the second half-cycle, one inner count longer.","comment":"One inner count longer"},
        "11135": {"synopsis":"The cycles done: IX back; the question and the answer.","comment":"IX back"},
        "11137": {"comment":"BC = $11FB (not read by the printer)"},
        "11140": {"comment":"Heard the tone?"},
        "11146": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11149": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11153": {"synopsis":"The test program's verdict (jumped to after the last test): the 16 results in IX, a bit\neach. All set: border green, ALL_PASSED_MSG. Otherwise border red, TEST_FAILED_MSG and, for\nevery bit that is 0, its message from FAIL_MSGS (E's bits 0-7, then D's). Then REPEAT_MSG\nand a wait: ENTER is ignored, SPACE (BREAK) restarts the machine at $0000.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11156": {"comment":"DE = the 16 results"},
        "11159": {"comment":"All bits set?"},
        "11161": {"comment":"$FF only when both are"},
        "11163": {"comment":"No: something failed"},
        "11165": {"comment":"Border 4: green"},
        "11169": {"comment":"'ALL TESTS PASSED'"},
        "11175": {"comment":"On to the repeat prompt"},
        "11177": {"synopsis":"Something failed: the failed tests listed.","comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11179": {"comment":"Border written"},
        "11181": {"comment":"'TEST FAILED, because:-'"},
        "11187": {"comment":"BC = $0802 (B counted, not read)"},
        "11190": {"comment":"The results again"},
        "11192": {"comment":"Results again"},
        "11193": {"comment":"Kept for D's turn"},
        "11194": {"comment":"FAIL_MSGS: E's bits first"},
        "11197": {"comment":"Eight bits"},
        "11199": {"synopsis":"One bit of E: its message when it is 0.","comment":"Next bit: passed?"},
        "11201": {"comment":"Yes: no message"},
        "11203": {"comment":"Entry and count kept"},
        "11205": {"comment":"The message's address"},
        "11207": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "11209": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "11212": {"comment":"Count and entry back"},
        "11214": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "11216": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11217": {"comment":"More bits"},
        "11219": {"comment":"D's bits now"},
        "11220": {"comment":"E = D's results"},
        "11221": {"comment":"Eight bits"},
        "11223": {"synopsis":"One bit of D: its message when it is 0.","comment":"Next bit: passed?"},
        "11225": {"comment":"Yes: no message"},
        "11227": {"comment":"Entry, count, BC kept"},
        "11230": {"comment":"The message's address"},
        "11231": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "11234": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "11237": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "11240": {"comment":"D's failures counted in B"},
        "11241": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "11243": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11244": {"comment":"More bits"},
        "11246": {"synopsis":"The repeat prompt and the wait.","comment":"'Hold [BREAK] to repeat tests'"},
        "11249": {"comment":"BC = $0FFB (not read by the printer)"},
        "11255": {"synopsis":"Waits for SPACE; ENTER is ignored.","comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11258": {"comment":"ENTER: wait again"},
        "11260": {"comment":"SPACE: restart the machine"},
        "11261": {"comment":"$0000: the machine starts again"},
        "11264": {"synopsis":"Two new lines and 'Hold [BREAK] to repeat tests'."},
        "11295": {"synopsis":"The RS232 test, through the sound chip's register 14 (its I/O port) and a loopback\nconnector: $FF, $FE, $FD, $FB and $F7 are written and must read back as $FF, $7E, $BD, $DB\nand $E7, so bit 0 must come back on bit 7, 1 on 6, 2 on 5 and 3 on 4. Nothing is printed.\nExit: through $2429, the result into IX: carry when every value read back right.","comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "11301": {"comment":"Register 14 selected"},
        "11302": {"comment":"Register 14"},
        "11306": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "11308": {"comment":"B = $BF: write"},
        "11311": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11314": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "11316": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11318": {"comment":"Bit 0 low"},
        "11321": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11323": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11326": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 7 low: $7E?"},
        "11328": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11330": {"comment":"Bit 1 low"},
        "11333": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11335": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11338": {"comment":"Bits 1 and 6 low: $BD?"},
        "11340": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11342": {"comment":"Bit 2 low"},
        "11345": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11347": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11350": {"comment":"Bits 2 and 5 low: $DB?"},
        "11352": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11354": {"comment":"Bit 3 low"},
        "11357": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11359": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11362": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4 low: $E7?"},
        "11364": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11366": {"comment":"All right: passed"},
        "11370": {"synopsis":"A value read back wrong: no carry.","comment":"Failed: no carry"},
        "11374": {"synopsis":"The ULA sound test: the screen cleared, border red, BORDCR = $08, the title\n(ULA_SOUND_MSG); a tone on the speaker (TONE_OUT through $2726: HL = $0100, DE = $09FB);\nHEARD_TONE_MSG and the answer ($26AF: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $2429, the result into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11377": {"comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11381": {"comment":"BORDCR = $08: border 1 in the tone"},
        "11386": {"comment":"ULA SOUND TEST title"},
        "11392": {"comment":"HL = $0100, DE = $0A00 cycles"},
        "11395": {"comment":"$0A00 cycles"},
        "11398": {"comment":"TONE_OUT, then DI"},
        "11401": {"comment":"BC = $11FB (not read by the printer)"},
        "11404": {"comment":"Heard the tone?"},
        "11410": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11413": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11417": {"synopsis":"The sound chip test: the screen cleared, border cyan, the title (GI_SOUND_MSG); the\nregisters set from AY_SETTINGS; the tones of channels A, B and C each alone for 40 frames\n(mixer $FE, $FD, $FB), then all three together (mixer $F8) for 40 more, then the mixer $FF\n(all off); FOUR_SOUNDS_MSG and the answer ($26AF: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $2429, the result into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11420": {"comment":"Border 5: cyan"},
        "11424": {"comment":"GI SOUND TEST title"},
        "11430": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "11436": {"comment":"Register/value pairs"},
        "11439": {"synopsis":"One register/value pair, until a byte with bit 7 set.","comment":"Register number"},
        "11441": {"comment":"The end marker?"},
        "11443": {"comment":"Yes: the mixer next"},
        "11445": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "11446": {"comment":"Out"},
        "11448": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "11450": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11451": {"comment":"Out"},
        "11453": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "11455": {"synopsis":"The four sounds.","comment":"AY ports again"},
        "11461": {"comment":"Three channels, one at a time"},
        "11463": {"comment":"Mixer $FE: tone A only"},
        "11465": {"synopsis":"One channel's tone alone for 40 frames.","comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "11466": {"comment":"Register 7"},
        "11470": {"comment":"Mixer written"},
        "11471": {"comment":"Out: mixer value H"},
        "11473": {"comment":"Kept round the wait"},
        "11476": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "11482": {"comment":"Next channel: $FD, then $FB"},
        "11483": {"comment":"Carry into bit 0, next bit out"},
        "11485": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11486": {"comment":"More channels"},
        "11488": {"comment":"Mixer $F8: all three tones"},
        "11490": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "11495": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11498": {"comment":"Kept round the wait"},
        "11501": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "11504": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "11507": {"comment":"Mixer $FF: all off"},
        "11509": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "11514": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "11515": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11517": {"comment":"BC = $09FB (not read by the printer)"},
        "11520": {"comment":"Heard four sounds?"},
        "11526": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11529": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11532": {"synopsis":"The sound chip's registers for COLOUR_BARS and GI_SOUND_TEST, as register/value pairs\nended by $80: tone periods A $0040, B $0080, C $0100; noise period $1F; volumes A, B and C\n15. Read at $293C and $2CAF."},
        "11553": {"synopsis":"The question after the ULA sound and cassette output tones: 'Press [ENTER] if you heard\nthe tone, else press [SPACE]'."},
        "11610": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 15 (D bit 7 of the results): the colour test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11630": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 7 (E bit 7 of the results): the ULA sound test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11653": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 10 (D bit 2 of the results): the SYMBOL SHIFT/A test's failure line, ended\nby a new line."},
        "11680": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 9 (D bit 1 of the results): the ULA test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11697": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 8 (D bit 0 of the results): the RS232 test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11716": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 11 (D bit 3 of the results): the sound chip test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11738": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 12 (D bit 4 of the results): the RAM paging test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11764": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 6 (E bit 6 of the results): the joystick test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11786": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 14 (D bit 6 of the results): the IC 7 checksum's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11808": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 13 (D bit 5 of the results): the IC 8 checksum's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11830": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 1 (E bit 1 of the results): the disk test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11849": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 4 (E bit 4 of the results): the second screen test's failure line, ended by\na new line."},
        "11876": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 5 (E bit 5 of the results): the cassette output test's failure line, ended\nby a new line."},
        "11900": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 0 (E bit 0 of the results): the cassette input test's failure line, ended by\na new line."},
        "11923": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 3 (E bit 3 of the results): the printer BUSY test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11949": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 2 (E bit 2 of the results): the printer DATA test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11975": {"synopsis":"TEST_REPORT's failure lines, one word per result bit: entries 0-7 for E's bits 0-7 (IX's\nlow byte), 8-15 for D's. In order: cassette input, disk, printer DATA, printer BUSY, second\nscreen, cassette output, joystick, ULA sound; RS232, ULA, SYMBOL SHIFT/A, sound chip, RAM\npaging, IC 8, IC 7, colour. The first test shifted into IX ends up in D's bit 7, the last\nin E's bit 0. Read at $2BC5 and $2BDE."},
        "12007": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, FLASH 1, 'ROM TEST FAILED', FLASH 0 and a new line. No code in this ROM loads its\naddress."},
        "12031": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, FLASH 1, 'RAM TEST FAILED', FLASH 0 and a new line. No code in this ROM loads its\naddress."},
        "12055": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's screen (printed at $275C): AT 2,0, the title, then INVERSE 1 and the\nkeyboard drawn row by row as letters two columns apart, a lower-case letter for each key\nwithout a single character of its own (the CAPS SHIFT and SYMBOL SHIFT combinations of\nKEY_TEST_CODES, the two shifts, ENTER, BREAK); INVERSE 0, then AT 20,5, FLASH 1, 'TEST ALL\nTHE KEYS'."},
        "12505": {"synopsis":"SYMA_TEST's screen: AT 5,5, INVERSE 1 ' SYM SHFT/A  TEST ', and at rows 10-14 'Press',\n'SYM SHFT/A' (flashing) and 'for 1 sec'."},
        "12574": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_TEST's screen: AT 9,0, INVERSE 1, the test program's title and version line, 'Check\nTV tuning', a reminder to fit the loopback connector, the ENTER/SPACE question about the\ncolours, and a flashing warning that the tests corrupt disks and need factory equipment."},
        "12878": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' ULA TEST ', INVERSE 0, a new line."},
        "12897": {"synopsis":"AT 5,7, INVERSE 1, 'RAM DATA TESTS', AT 10,5, '.. STARTING NOW ..', INVERSE 0, a new line."},
        "12941": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' GI SOUND TEST ', two new lines, INVERSE 0."},
        "12966": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' ULA SOUND TEST ', two new lines, INVERSE 0."},
        "12992": {"synopsis":"A 0 before CASS_OUT_MSG; the print starts after it."},
        "12993": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, 'CASSETTE OUTPUT TEST', INVERSE 0, two new lines."},
        "13023": {"synopsis":"A 0 before JOY_TEST_MSG; the print starts after it."},
        "13024": {"synopsis":"JOYSTICK_TEST's screen: AT 0,10, INVERSE 1 'JOYSTICK TEST', the instructions (move both\njoysticks and press fire until the letters are wiped out; SPACE gives up) and a box drawn\nwith + - ! holding the J1 and J2 labels UP, LF, FI, RI and DN."},
        "13423": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, ' ALL TESTS PASSED ', a new line."},
        "13446": {"synopsis":"AT 0,0, FLASH 1, ' TEST FAILED, because:- ', FLASH 0, two new lines."},
        "13480": {"synopsis":"GI_SOUND_TEST's question: 'press [ENTER] if you heard four sounds, else press [SPACE].'"},
        "13545": {"synopsis":"Makes a tone on the speaker (port $FE bit 4) for the test program, with the border in\nBORDCR's colour (its bits 3-5) and the MIC bit 3 set in every write: about DE cycles, each\nhalf-cycle a delay set by HL (H counts the outer loop, L / 4 the inner one, and L's low two\nbits pick an entry into TONE_NOPS for the finest step). Interrupts are off while it runs and\nturned on at the end. $2726 calls it.\nEntry: HL = the pitch, DE = the cycles.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "13546": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "13548": {"comment":"L's low bits: 0-3 extra NOPs"},
        "13549": {"comment":"L / 4: the inner count"},
        "13551": {"comment":"Inner count in L"},
        "13553": {"comment":"IX = TONE_NOPS + 3 - low bits"},
        "13554": {"comment":"3 - low bits"},
        "13559": {"comment":"From TONE_NOPS"},
        "13563": {"comment":"+ 3 - low bits"},
        "13565": {"comment":"Border from BORDCR"},
        "13568": {"comment":"Bits 3-5: the border colour"},
        "13570": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-2"},
        "13573": {"comment":"MIC bit 3 held set"},
        "13575": {"synopsis":"The entry JP (IX) uses: 0 to 3 NOPs, then the delay.","comment":"0-3 of these run, by IX"},
        "13578": {"comment":"B, C one more for the first DEC"},
        "13580": {"synopsis":"A half-cycle's delay: C inner rounds, B outer ones.","comment":"Inner delay"},
        "13581": {"comment":"Inner rounds"},
        "13583": {"comment":"C = $3F for the later rounds"},
        "13585": {"comment":"Outer count"},
        "13586": {"comment":"Outer rounds"},
        "13589": {"comment":"Speaker bit 4 flipped"},
        "13591": {"comment":"Out: speaker flipped"},
        "13593": {"comment":"Outer count again; port byte in C"},
        "13595": {"comment":"Speaker bit now set?"},
        "13597": {"comment":"Rising edge: the longer half"},
        "13599": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "13601": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "13603": {"comment":"Port byte back, inner count from L"},
        "13605": {"comment":"One cycle fewer"},
        "13606": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "13608": {"synopsis":"After a rising edge: the second half-cycle, one inner count longer.","comment":"One inner count longer"},
        "13610": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "13612": {"synopsis":"The cycles done: interrupts on, IX back.","comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "13613": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13616": {"synopsis":"Where JOYSTICK_TEST's ten labels are, as row/column pairs with the row 3 more than the\nscreen row: joystick 1's FI, UP, DN, RI, LF (D's bits 0-4), then joystick 2's LF, RI, DN,\nUP, FI (E's bits 0-4). Read at $2A07 and $2A29."},
        "13636": {"synopsis":"The ten labels' names in JOY_PLACES's order, two letters each, no end marker. Nothing in\nthis ROM reads them."},
        "13656": {"synopsis":"The disk test: DISK_TEST_RAM copied to $5F00 and run there, since it pages this ROM out.\nExit: through $2429, the drive test's carry into IX.","comment":"From DISK_TEST_RAM"},
        "13659": {"comment":"To $5F00"},
        "13662": {"comment":"$3D bytes"},
        "13667": {"comment":"Run there"},
        "13670": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5F00 (DISK_TEST copies it):\n1. Port $1FFD = 4: ROM 2 paged in.\n2. $0C00 bytes of\nROM 2 from $2492 (its drive test program, DT_START) copied to $6000.\n3. Port $1FFD = 0 and\nport $7FFD = $10, with their copies $5B67 and $5B5C: ROM 1 and RAM bank 0.\n4. Interrupts\non, the copy called at $6000, IX kept round it.\n5. Port $7FFD = 0 ($5B5C too): this ROM\nback; the copy's carry into IX through $2429.","comment":"$1FFD bit 2: ROM 2 in"},
        "13672": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "13677": {"comment":"ROM 2's drive test program"},
        "13680": {"comment":"To $6000"},
        "13683": {"comment":"$0C00 bytes"},
        "13686": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13688": {"comment":"Port $1FFD = 0"},
        "13690": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "13695": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "13698": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = $10: ROM 1, bank 0"},
        "13700": {"comment":"B = $7F: port $7FFD"},
        "13704": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "13707": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "13708": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "13710": {"comment":"The drive test"},
        "13713": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13715": {"comment":"Its result kept"},
        "13716": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = 0: this ROM back"},
        "13718": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "13723": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "13726": {"comment":"The result"},
        "13727": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "13731": {"synopsis":"The cassette input test: the instructions (TAPE_TEST_MSG) and a 25-frame pause (CI_WAIT);\nwith interrupts off, six black marks across attribute row 7 (columns 1, 7, ... 31); then,\nround after round, the EAR input (port $FE bit 6) polled $1000 times and its changes\ncounted, the count / 32 (at most 32) shown as a bright cyan cell over a bright blue row 8;\nuntil ENTER (passed) or SPACE (failed) is pressed.\nExit: through CI_WAIT after the result went into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "13734": {"comment":"Instructions"},
        "13737": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "13740": {"comment":"25 frames' pause"},
        "13743": {"comment":"No interrupts while counting"},
        "13744": {"comment":"Row 7, column 1"},
        "13747": {"comment":"Every sixth cell"},
        "13750": {"comment":"Six marks, attribute 0"},
        "13752": {"synopsis":"One mark.","comment":"A black cell"},
        "13753": {"comment":"Six cells on"},
        "13754": {"comment":"Next mark"},
        "13756": {"synopsis":"One round: $1000 polls of the EAR input and the keys, then the reading shown.","comment":"Changes counted in HL"},
        "13759": {"comment":"$1000 polls"},
        "13762": {"comment":"C = $FE: no level yet"},
        "13764": {"comment":"SPACE pressed?"},
        "13766": {"comment":"Row $7FFE"},
        "13768": {"comment":"Bit 0: SPACE"},
        "13770": {"comment":"Yes: failed"},
        "13773": {"comment":"ENTER pressed?"},
        "13776": {"comment":"Row $BFFE"},
        "13778": {"comment":"Bit 0: ENTER"},
        "13780": {"comment":"Yes: passed"},
        "13783": {"synopsis":"One poll of the EAR input.","comment":"Count the polls down"},
        "13786": {"comment":"Done: show the reading"},
        "13788": {"comment":"EAR level (bit 6)"},
        "13790": {"comment":"Only bit 6"},
        "13792": {"comment":"Same as last time?"},
        "13793": {"comment":"Same: next poll"},
        "13795": {"comment":"Changed: counted"},
        "13796": {"comment":"New level kept"},
        "13797": {"comment":"Next poll"},
        "13799": {"synopsis":"The reading: the changes / 32, at most 32.","comment":"HL x 8: H = changes / 32"},
        "13811": {"comment":"L = the reading"},
        "13812": {"comment":"Over 32?"},
        "13814": {"comment":"Compared with H"},
        "13817": {"comment":"Kept at 32"},
        "13819": {"synopsis":"Row 8 redrawn after a frame and the marker set at the reading's column.","comment":"HL = the reading"},
        "13820": {"comment":"H = 0"},
        "13821": {"comment":"Row 8's last cell"},
        "13824": {"comment":"32 cells"},
        "13826": {"comment":"$48: bright blue paper"},
        "13828": {"comment":"Wait for a frame"},
        "13829": {"comment":"One frame"},
        "13830": {"comment":"Interrupts off again"},
        "13831": {"synopsis":"One cell.","comment":"Row 8 filled, right to left"},
        "13833": {"comment":"32 cells"},
        "13835": {"comment":"DE = row 8's first cell"},
        "13836": {"comment":"The reading's cell"},
        "13837": {"comment":"$68: bright cyan marker"},
        "13839": {"comment":"Marker written"},
        "13840": {"comment":"Next round"},
        "13842": {"synopsis":"A 25-frame pause with interrupts on, then FLAGS bit 5 (a new key) cleared.\nExit: carry; interrupts on.\nChanges: B, HL, F.","comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "13843": {"comment":"25 frames"},
        "13845": {"synopsis":"One frame."},
        "13846": {"comment":"25 times"},
        "13848": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared: no key waiting"},
        "13853": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "13854": {"comment":"Done"},
        "13855": {"synopsis":"SPACE: no carry into IX (failed); the pause; out of CASS_IN_TEST.","comment":"No carry: failed"},
        "13856": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "13859": {"comment":"Pause, then out"},
        "13861": {"synopsis":"ENTER: carry into IX (passed); the pause; out of CASS_IN_TEST.","comment":"Carry: passed"},
        "13862": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "13865": {"comment":"Pause, then out"},
        "13867": {"synopsis":"CASS_IN_TEST's instructions: AT 0,0, insert the test tape and press PLAY, adjust the\nazimuth screw for the largest reading, then ENTER for success or SPACE for failure."},
        "14010": {"synopsis":"Bytes nothing in this ROM reads, up to $37BA. Each byte XORed with $30 and with bit 7\ndropped gives, for most of them, a credits text with lines ended by $0D: who did the test\nprogram, thanks, and the machines and tools it was written with. Some bytes, mostly near\nthe end, do not decode that way."},
        "15872": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's CALL_ROM0, of which these are the same bytes: it parks AF and HL at $5B56 and\n$5B52, reads the word after the CALL into HL (stepping the return address past it) and\nclears bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) with interrupts off. That OUT, at $3E1C, pages this\nROM in, so the code goes on here at $3E1E: CALL_ROM0_BACK is pushed as the return, AF and\nHL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "15875": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "15877": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "15880": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "15881": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "15885": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "15886": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "15888": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "15894": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "15897": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "15900": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3E1E here"},
        "15902": {"comment":"From here in this ROM"},
        "15903": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "15907": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "15908": {"comment":"AF and HL back"},
        "15912": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "15913": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "15916": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "15917": {"synopsis":"Where a routine called through CALL_ROM0 returns: bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) set\nagain with interrupts off, keeping AF and BC; after the OUT at $3E3B the code goes on in ROM\n2's copy.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "15919": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD set: ROM 2"},
        "15925": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "15928": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "15931": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3E3D there"},
        "15933": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "15934": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "16000": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 1, keeping AF, BC and HL (parked at\n$5B56, $5B54 and $5B52): the word is read into HL and the return address stepped past it;\nbit 4 of the paging byte $5B5C (port $7FFD) is set with interrupts off, which pages ROM 1\nin, and the code goes on at $3EA2 in ROM 1's copy; CALL_ROM1_BACK is pushed as the return,\nAF, BC and HL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. The return runs ROM 1's\n$3EB5, which clears the bit again. ROM 1 has the same routine here with the bit cleared,\nfor its calls into this ROM. Called at $0285, $08E2, $0911, $092B, $0D94 and $210E.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16003": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16007": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16009": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16012": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16013": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16017": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16018": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16020": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16023": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16026": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16032": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3EA2 there"},
        "16034": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16035": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16039": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16040": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16044": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16045": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16049": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16052": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16053": {"synopsis":"Where a routine of this ROM called through ROM 1's copy of CALL_ROM1 returns: bit 4 of\n$5B5C (port $7FFD) set again with interrupts off, which pages ROM 1 back in, keeping AF and\nBC; the code after the OUT at $3EC3 runs in ROM 1.","comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "16055": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16058": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16061": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16067": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3EC5 there"},
        "16069": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16070": {"comment":"BC and AF back"},
        "16128": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's CALL_ROM2, of which these are the same bytes, and of which this ROM runs the middle:\nROM 1 parks HL, BC and AF at $5B52, $5B54 and $5B56, reads the word after the CALL and\nclears bit 4 of port $7FFD (and $5B5C); that OUT, at $3F20, pages this ROM in, so\n$3F22-$3F2D\nrun here and set bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67), which pages ROM 2 in, where the code goes\non at $3F2F. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16131": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16135": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16137": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16140": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16141": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16145": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16146": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16148": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16151": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "16154": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16160": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F22 here"},
        "16162": {"comment":"From here in this ROM: bit 2 of $1FFD set"},
        "16165": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "16170": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "16173": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3F2F there"},
        "16175": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "16176": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16180": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16181": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16185": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16186": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16190": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16193": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16194": {"synopsis":"The way back from ROM 2 to ROM 1, keeping AF and BC: ROM 2 clears bit 2 of port $1FFD (and\n$5B67), which pages this ROM in, so $3F52-$3F5D run here and set bit 4 of port $7FFD (and\n$5B5C), which pages ROM 1 back in for the RET.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "16196": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16199": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "16202": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16208": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F52 here"},
        "16210": {"comment":"From here in this ROM: bit 4 set"},
        "16213": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16218": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "16221": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3F5F there"},
        "16223": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16224": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "16368": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's way into this ROM: its ROM0_HOOK_A0 and ROM0_HOOK_A call $3FF0 through CALL_ROM0.\nIt jumps to $2187, which takes the zero flag, A and HL as ROM 2 passes them.","comment":"On to $2187"},
        "16383": {"synopsis":"The last byte, $8B. Probably balances a checksum (the test program's ROM checks)."}
      }
    }
  },
